\mt1 THE BOOK OF PSALMS
\c 1
\p
\v 1 Blessed \add is\add* the man that walketh not in the counsel of the ungodly, nor standeth in the way of sinners, nor sitteth in the seat of the scornful.\f + \fr 1:1 \fr*\fq ungodly \fq*\ft - or, wicked\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 But his delight \add is\add* in the law of the \nd LORD\nd*; and in his law doth he meditate day and night.
\p
\v 3 And he shall be like a tree planted by the rivers of water, that bringeth forth his fruit in his season; his leaf also shall not wither; and whatsoever he doeth shall prosper.\f + \fr 1:3 \fr*\fq wither \fq*\ft - Heb. fade\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 The ungodly \add are\add* not so: but \add are\add* like the chaff which the wind driveth away.
\p
\v 5 Therefore the ungodly shall not stand in the judgment, nor sinners in the congregation of the righteous.
\p
\v 6 For the \nd LORD\nd* knoweth the way of the righteous: but the way of the ungodly shall perish.
\c 2
\p
\v 1 Why do the heathen rage, and the people imagine a vain thing?\f + \fr 2:1 \fr*\fq rage \fq*\ft - or, tumultuously assemble\ft*\f*\f + \fr 2:1 \fr*\fq imagine \fq*\ft - Heb. meditate\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 The kings of the earth set themselves, and the rulers take counsel together, against the \nd LORD\nd*, and against his anointed, \add saying\add*,
\p
\v 3 Let us break their bands asunder, and cast away their cords from us.
\p
\v 4 He that sitteth in the heavens shall laugh: the Lord shall have them in derision.
\p
\v 5 Then shall he speak unto them in his wrath, and vex them in his sore displeasure.\f + \fr 2:5 \fr*\fq vex \fq*\ft - or, trouble\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Yet have I set my king upon my holy hill of Zion.\f + \fr 2:6 \fr*\fq set \fq*\ft - Heb. anointed\ft*\f*\f + \fr 2:6 \fr*\fq upon… \fq*\ft - Heb. upon Zion, the hill of my holiness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 I will declare the decree: the \nd LORD\nd* hath said unto me, Thou \add art\add* my Son; this day have I begotten thee.\f + \fr 2:7 \fr*\fq the decree \fq*\ft - or, for a decree\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 Ask of me, and I shall give \add thee\add* the heathen \add for\add* thine inheritance, and the uttermost parts of the earth \add for\add* thy possession.
\p
\v 9 Thou shalt break them with a rod of iron; thou shalt dash them in pieces like a potter’s vessel.
\p
\v 10 Be wise now therefore, O ye kings: be instructed, ye judges of the earth.
\p
\v 11 Serve the \nd LORD\nd* with fear, and rejoice with trembling.
\p
\v 12 Kiss the Son, lest he be angry, and ye perish \add from\add* the way, when his wrath is kindled but a little. Blessed \add are\add* all they that put their trust in him.
\c 3
\d A Psalm of David, when he fled from Absalom his son.
\p
\v 1 \nd LORD\nd*, how are they increased that trouble me! many \add are\add* they that rise up against me.
\p
\v 2 Many \add there be\add* which say of my soul, \add There is\add* no help for him in God. Selah.
\p
\v 3 But thou, O \nd LORD\nd*, \add art\add* a shield for me; my glory, and the lifter up of mine head.\f + \fr 3:3 \fr*\fq for \fq*\ft - or, about\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 I cried unto the \nd LORD\nd* with my voice, and he heard me out of his holy hill. Selah.
\p
\v 5 I laid me down and slept; I awaked; for the \nd LORD\nd* sustained me.
\p
\v 6 I will not be afraid of ten thousands of people, that have set \add themselves\add* against me round about.
\p
\v 7 Arise, O \nd LORD\nd*; save me, O my God: for thou hast smitten all mine enemies \add upon\add* the cheek bone; thou hast broken the teeth of the ungodly.
\p
\v 8 Salvation \add belongeth\add* unto the \nd LORD\nd*: thy blessing \add is\add* upon thy people. Selah.
\c 4
\d To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 Hear me when I call, O God of my righteousness: thou hast enlarged me \add when I was\add* in distress; have mercy upon me, and hear my prayer.\f + \fr 4:1 \fr*\fq chief… \fq*\ft - or, overseer\ft*\f*\f + \fr 4:1 \fr*\fq have… \fq*\ft - or, be gracious unto me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 O ye sons of men, how long \add will ye turn\add* my glory into shame? \add how long\add* will ye love vanity, \add and\add* seek after leasing? Selah.
\p
\v 3 But know that the \nd LORD\nd* hath set apart him that is godly for himself: the \nd LORD\nd* will hear when I call unto him.
\p
\v 4 Stand in awe, and sin not: commune with your own heart upon your bed, and be still. Selah.
\p
\v 5 Offer the sacrifices of righteousness, and put your trust in the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 6 \add There be\add* many that say, Who will shew us \add any\add* good? \nd LORD\nd*, lift thou up the light of thy countenance upon us.
\p
\v 7 Thou hast put gladness in my heart, more than in the time \add that\add* their corn and their wine increased.
\p
\v 8 I will both lay me down in peace, and sleep: for thou, \nd LORD\nd*, only makest me dwell in safety.
\c 5
\d To the chief Musician upon Nehiloth, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 Give ear to my words, O \nd LORD\nd*, consider my meditation.
\p
\v 2 Hearken unto the voice of my cry, my King, and my God: for unto thee will I pray.
\p
\v 3 My voice shalt thou hear in the morning, O \nd LORD\nd*; in the morning will I direct \add my prayer\add* unto thee, and will look up.
\p
\v 4 For thou \add art\add* not a God that hath pleasure in wickedness: neither shall evil dwell with thee.
\p
\v 5 The foolish shall not stand in thy sight: thou hatest all workers of iniquity.\f + \fr 5:5 \fr*\fq in… \fq*\ft - Heb. before thine eyes\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Thou shalt destroy them that speak leasing: the \nd LORD\nd* will abhor the bloody and deceitful man.\f + \fr 5:6 \fr*\fq bloody… \fq*\ft - Heb. man of bloods and deceit\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 But as for me, I will come \add into\add* thy house in the multitude of thy mercy: \add and\add* in thy fear will I worship toward thy holy temple.\f + \fr 5:7 \fr*\fq thy holy… \fq*\ft - Heb. the temple of thy holiness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 Lead me, O \nd LORD\nd*, in thy righteousness because of mine enemies; make thy way straight before my face.\f + \fr 5:8 \fr*\fq mine… \fq*\ft - Heb. those which observe me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 For \add there is\add* no faithfulness in their mouth; their inward part \add is\add* very wickedness; their throat \add is\add* an open sepulchre; they flatter with their tongue.\f + \fr 5:9 \fr*\fq faithfulness \fq*\ft - or, stedfastness\ft*\f*\f + \fr 5:9 \fr*\fq their mouth \fq*\ft - Heb. his mouth, that is, the mouth of any of them\ft*\f*\f + \fr 5:9 \fr*\fq very… \fq*\ft - Heb. wickednesses\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 Destroy thou them, O God; let them fall by their own counsels; cast them out in the multitude of their transgressions; for they have rebelled against thee.\f + \fr 5:10 \fr*\fq Destroy… \fq*\ft - or, Make them guilty\ft*\f*\f + \fr 5:10 \fr*\fq by… \fq*\ft - or, from their counsels\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 But let all those that put their trust in thee rejoice: let them ever shout for joy, because thou defendest them: let them also that love thy name be joyful in thee.\f + \fr 5:11 \fr*\fq defendest… \fq*\ft - Heb. coverest over, or, protectest them\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 For thou, \nd LORD\nd*, wilt bless the righteous; with favour wilt thou compass him as \add with\add* a shield.\f + \fr 5:12 \fr*\fq compass \fq*\ft - Heb. crown\ft*\f*
\c 6
\d To the chief Musician on Neginoth upon Sheminith, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 O \nd LORD\nd*, rebuke me not in thine anger, neither chasten me in thy hot displeasure.\f + \fr 6:1 \fr*\fq chief… \fq*\ft - or, overseer\ft*\f*\f + \fr 6:1 \fr*\fq Sheminith \fq*\ft - or, the eighth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Have mercy upon me, O \nd LORD\nd*; for I \add am\add* weak: O \nd LORD\nd*, heal me; for my bones are vexed.
\p
\v 3 My soul is also sore vexed: but thou, O \nd LORD\nd*, how long?
\p
\v 4 Return, O \nd LORD\nd*, deliver my soul: oh save me for thy mercies’ sake.
\p
\v 5 For in death \add there is\add* no remembrance of thee: in the grave who shall give thee thanks?
\p
\v 6 I am weary with my groaning; all the night make I my bed to swim; I water my couch with my tears.\f + \fr 6:6 \fr*\fq all… \fq*\ft - or, every night\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 Mine eye is consumed because of grief; it waxeth old because of all mine enemies.
\p
\v 8 Depart from me, all ye workers of iniquity; for the \nd LORD\nd* hath heard the voice of my weeping.
\p
\v 9 The \nd LORD\nd* hath heard my supplication; the \nd LORD\nd* will receive my prayer.
\p
\v 10 Let all mine enemies be ashamed and sore vexed: let them return \add and\add* be ashamed suddenly.
\c 7
\d Shiggaion of David, which he sang unto the \nd LORD\nd*, concerning the words of Cush the Benjamite.
\p
\v 1 O \nd LORD\nd* my God, in thee do I put my trust: save me from all them that persecute me, and deliver me:\f + \fr 7:1 \fr*\fq words \fq*\ft - or, business\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Lest he tear my soul like a lion, rending \add it\add* in pieces, while \add there is\add* none to deliver.\f + \fr 7:2 \fr*\fq none… \fq*\ft - Heb. not a deliverer\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 O \nd LORD\nd* my God, if I have done this; if there be iniquity in my hands;
\p
\v 4 If I have rewarded evil unto him that was at peace with me; (yea, I have delivered him that without cause is mine enemy:)
\p
\v 5 Let the enemy persecute my soul, and take \add it;\add* yea, let him tread down my life upon the earth, and lay mine honour in the dust. Selah.
\p
\v 6 Arise, O \nd LORD\nd*, in thine anger, lift up thyself because of the rage of mine enemies: and awake for me \add to\add* the judgment \add that\add* thou hast commanded.
\p
\v 7 So shall the congregation of the people compass thee about: for their sakes therefore return thou on high.
\p
\v 8 The \nd LORD\nd* shall judge the people: judge me, O \nd LORD\nd*, according to my righteousness, and according to mine integrity \add that is\add* in me.
\p
\v 9 Oh let the wickedness of the wicked come to an end; but establish the just: for the righteous God trieth the hearts and reins.
\p
\v 10 My defence \add is\add* of God, which saveth the upright in heart.\f + \fr 7:10 \fr*\fq My… \fq*\ft - Heb. My buckler is upon God\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 God judgeth the righteous, and God is angry \add with the wicked\add* every day.\f + \fr 7:11 \fr*\fq judgeth… \fq*\ft - or, is a righteous judge\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 If he turn not, he will whet his sword; he hath bent his bow, and made it ready.
\p
\v 13 He hath also prepared for him the instruments of death; he ordaineth his arrows against the persecutors.
\p
\v 14 Behold, he travaileth with iniquity, and hath conceived mischief, and brought forth falsehood.
\p
\v 15 He made a pit, and digged it, and is fallen into the ditch \add which\add* he made.\f + \fr 7:15 \fr*\fq He made a pit \fq*\ft - Heb. He hath digged a pit\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 His mischief shall return upon his own head, and his violent dealing shall come down upon his own pate.
\p
\v 17 I will praise the \nd LORD\nd* according to his righteousness: and will sing praise to the name of the \nd LORD\nd* most high.
\c 8
\d To the chief Musician upon Gittith, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 O \nd LORD\nd* our Lord, how excellent \add is\add* thy name in all the earth! who hast set thy glory above the heavens.
\p
\v 2 Out of the mouth of babes and sucklings hast thou ordained strength because of thine enemies, that thou mightest still the enemy and the avenger.\f + \fr 8:2 \fr*\fq ordained \fq*\ft - Heb. founded\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 When I consider thy heavens, the work of thy fingers, the moon and the stars, which thou hast ordained;
\p
\v 4 What is man, that thou art mindful of him? and the son of man, that thou visitest him?
\p
\v 5 For thou hast made him a little lower than the angels, and hast crowned him with glory and honour.
\p
\v 6 Thou madest him to have dominion over the works of thy hands; thou hast put all \add things\add* under his feet:
\p
\v 7 All sheep and oxen, yea, and the beasts of the field;\f + \fr 8:7 \fr*\fq All… \fq*\ft - Heb. Flocks and oxen all of them\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 The fowl of the air, and the fish of the sea, \add and whatsoever\add* passeth through the paths of the seas.
\p
\v 9 O \nd LORD\nd* our Lord, how excellent \add is\add* thy name in all the earth!
\c 9
\d To the chief Musician upon Muthlabben, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 I will praise \add thee\add*, O \nd LORD\nd*, with my whole heart; I will shew forth all thy marvellous works.
\p
\v 2 I will be glad and rejoice in thee: I will sing praise to thy name, O thou most High.
\p
\v 3 When mine enemies are turned back, they shall fall and perish at thy presence.
\p
\v 4 For thou hast maintained my right and my cause; thou satest in the throne judging right.\f + \fr 9:4 \fr*\fq maintained… \fq*\ft - Heb. made my judgment\ft*\f*\f + \fr 9:4 \fr*\fq judging right \fq*\ft - Heb. judging in righteousness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 Thou hast rebuked the heathen, thou hast destroyed the wicked, thou hast put out their name for ever and ever.
\p
\v 6 O thou enemy, destructions are come to a perpetual end: and thou hast destroyed cities; their memorial is perished with them.\f + \fr 9:6 \fr*\fq O thou… \fq*\ft - or, The destructions of the enemy are come to a perpetual end: and their cities hast thou destroyed, etc\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 But the \nd LORD\nd* shall endure for ever: he hath prepared his throne for judgment.
\p
\v 8 And he shall judge the world in righteousness, he shall minister judgment to the people in uprightness.
\p
\v 9 The \nd LORD\nd* also will be a refuge for the oppressed, a refuge in times of trouble.\f + \fr 9:9 \fr*\fq a refuge \fq*\ft - Heb. an high place\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 And they that know thy name will put their trust in thee: for thou, \nd LORD\nd*, hast not forsaken them that seek thee.
\p
\v 11 Sing praises to the \nd LORD\nd*, which dwelleth in Zion: declare among the people his doings.
\p
\v 12 When he maketh inquisition for blood, he remembereth them: he forgetteth not the cry of the humble.\f + \fr 9:12 \fr*\fq humble \fq*\ft - or, afflicted\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 Have mercy upon me, O \nd LORD\nd*; consider my trouble \add which I suffer\add* of them that hate me, thou that liftest me up from the gates of death:
\p
\v 14 That I may shew forth all thy praise in the gates of the daughter of Zion: I will rejoice in thy salvation.
\p
\v 15 The heathen are sunk down in the pit \add that\add* they made: in the net which they hid is their own foot taken.
\p
\v 16 The \nd LORD\nd* is known \add by\add* the judgment \add which\add* he executeth: the wicked is snared in the work of his own hands. Higgaion. Selah.\f + \fr 9:16 \fr*\fq Higgaion \fq*\ft - that is, Meditation\ft*\f*
\p
\v 17 The wicked shall be turned into hell, \add and\add* all the nations that forget God.
\p
\v 18 For the needy shall not alway be forgotten: the expectation of the poor shall \add not\add* perish for ever.
\p
\v 19 Arise, O \nd LORD\nd*; let not man prevail: let the heathen be judged in thy sight.
\p
\v 20 Put them in fear, O \nd LORD\nd*: \add that\add* the nations may know themselves \add to be but\add* men. Selah.
\c 10
\p
\v 1 Why standest thou afar off, O \nd LORD\nd*? \add why\add* hidest thou \add thyself\add* in times of trouble?
\p
\v 2 The wicked in \add his\add* pride doth persecute the poor: let them be taken in the devices that they have imagined.\f + \fr 10:2 \fr*\fq The wicked… \fq*\ft - Heb. In the pride of the wicked he doth persecute\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 For the wicked boasteth of his heart’s desire, and blesseth the covetous, \add whom\add* the \nd LORD\nd* abhorreth.\f + \fr 10:3 \fr*\fq heart’s \fq*\ft - Heb. soul’s\ft*\f*\f + \fr 10:3 \fr*\fq blesseth… \fq*\ft - or, the covetous blesseth himself, he abhorreth the\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 The wicked, through the pride of his countenance, will not seek \add after God:\add* God \add is\add* not in all his thoughts.\f + \fr 10:4 \fr*\fq God is… \fq*\ft - or, all his thoughts are, There is no God\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 His ways are always grievous; thy judgments \add are\add* far above out of his sight: \add as for\add* all his enemies, he puffeth at them.
\p
\v 6 He hath said in his heart, I shall not be moved: for \add I shall\add* never \add be\add* in adversity.\f + \fr 10:6 \fr*\fq never \fq*\ft - Heb. unto generation and generation\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 His mouth is full of cursing and deceit and fraud: under his tongue \add is\add* mischief and vanity.\f + \fr 10:7 \fr*\fq deceit \fq*\ft - Heb. deceits\ft*\f*\f + \fr 10:7 \fr*\fq vanity \fq*\ft - or, iniquity\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 He sitteth in the lurking places of the villages: in the secret places doth he murder the innocent: his eyes are privily set against the poor.\f + \fr 10:8 \fr*\fq are… \fq*\ft - Heb. hide themselves\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 He lieth in wait secretly as a lion in his den: he lieth in wait to catch the poor: he doth catch the poor, when he draweth him into his net.\f + \fr 10:9 \fr*\fq secretly \fq*\ft - Heb. in the secret places\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 He croucheth, \add and\add* humbleth himself, that the poor may fall by his strong ones.\f + \fr 10:10 \fr*\fq He… \fq*\ft - Heb. He breaketh himself\ft*\f*\f + \fr 10:10 \fr*\fq by… \fq*\ft - or, into his strong parts\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 He hath said in his heart, God hath forgotten: he hideth his face; he will never see \add it\add*.
\p
\v 12 Arise, O \nd LORD\nd*; O God, lift up thine hand: forget not the humble.\f + \fr 10:12 \fr*\fq humble \fq*\ft - or, afflicted\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 Wherefore doth the wicked contemn God? he hath said in his heart, Thou wilt not require \add it\add*.
\p
\v 14 Thou hast seen \add it;\add* for thou beholdest mischief and spite, to requite \add it\add* with thy hand: the poor committeth himself unto thee; thou art the helper of the fatherless.\f + \fr 10:14 \fr*\fq committeth \fq*\ft - Heb. leaveth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 Break thou the arm of the wicked and the evil \add man:\add* seek out his wickedness \add till\add* thou find none.
\p
\v 16 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* King for ever and ever: the heathen are perished out of his land.
\p
\v 17 \nd LORD\nd*, thou hast heard the desire of the humble: thou wilt prepare their heart, thou wilt cause thine ear to hear:\f + \fr 10:17 \fr*\fq prepare \fq*\ft - or, establish\ft*\f*
\p
\v 18 To judge the fatherless and the oppressed, that the man of the earth may no more oppress.\f + \fr 10:18 \fr*\fq oppress \fq*\ft - or, terrify\ft*\f*
\c 11
\d To the chief Musician, \add A Psalm\add* of David.
\p
\v 1 In the \nd LORD\nd* put I my trust: how say ye to my soul, Flee \add as\add* a bird to your mountain?
\p
\v 2 For, lo, the wicked bend \add their\add* bow, they make ready their arrow upon the string, that they may privily shoot at the upright in heart.\f + \fr 11:2 \fr*\fq privily \fq*\ft - Heb. in darkness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 If the foundations be destroyed, what can the righteous do?
\p
\v 4 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* in his holy temple, the \nd LORD’s\nd* throne \add is\add* in heaven: his eyes behold, his eyelids try, the children of men.
\p
\v 5 The \nd LORD\nd* trieth the righteous: but the wicked and him that loveth violence his soul hateth.
\p
\v 6 Upon the wicked he shall rain snares, fire and brimstone, and an horrible tempest: \add this shall be\add* the portion of their cup.\f + \fr 11:6 \fr*\fq an horrible… \fq*\ft - or, a burning tempest\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 For the righteous \nd LORD\nd* loveth righteousness; his countenance doth behold the upright.
\c 12
\d To the chief Musician upon Sheminith, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 Help, \nd LORD\nd*; for the godly man ceaseth; for the faithful fail from among the children of men.\f + \fr 12:1 \fr*\fq upon… \fq*\ft - or, upon the eighth\ft*\f*\f + \fr 12:1 \fr*\fq Help \fq*\ft - or, Save\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 They speak vanity every one with his neighbour: \add with\add* flattering lips \add and\add* with a double heart do they speak.\f + \fr 12:2 \fr*\fq a double… \fq*\ft - Heb. an heart and an heart\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 The \nd LORD\nd* shall cut off all flattering lips, \add and\add* the tongue that speaketh proud things:\f + \fr 12:3 \fr*\fq proud \fq*\ft - Heb. great\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Who have said, With our tongue will we prevail; our lips \add are\add* our own: who \add is\add* lord over us?\f + \fr 12:4 \fr*\fq are… \fq*\ft - Heb. are with us\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 For the oppression of the poor, for the sighing of the needy, now will I arise, saith the \nd LORD\nd*; I will set \add him\add* in safety \add from him that\add* puffeth at him.\f + \fr 12:5 \fr*\fq puffeth… \fq*\ft - or, would ensnare him\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 The words of the \nd LORD\nd* \add are\add* pure words: \add as\add* silver tried in a furnace of earth, purified seven times.
\p
\v 7 Thou shalt keep them, O \nd LORD\nd*, thou shalt preserve them from this generation for ever.\f + \fr 12:7 \fr*\fq them from \fq*\ft - Heb. him, etc: that is, every one of them, etc\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 The wicked walk on every side, when the vilest men are exalted.\f + \fr 12:8 \fr*\fq men \fq*\ft - Heb. of the sons of the men\ft*\f*
\c 13
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 How long wilt thou forget me, O \nd LORD\nd*? for ever? how long wilt thou hide thy face from me?\f + \fr 13:1 \fr*\fq chief… \fq*\ft - or, overseer\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 How long shall I take counsel in my soul, \add having\add* sorrow in my heart daily? how long shall mine enemy be exalted over me?
\p
\v 3 Consider \add and\add* hear me, O \nd LORD\nd* my God: lighten mine eyes, lest I sleep the \add sleep of\add* death;
\p
\v 4 Lest mine enemy say, I have prevailed against him; \add and\add* those that trouble me rejoice when I am moved.
\p
\v 5 But I have trusted in thy mercy; my heart shall rejoice in thy salvation.
\p
\v 6 I will sing unto the \nd LORD\nd*, because he hath dealt bountifully with me.
\c 14
\d To the chief Musician, \add A Psalm\add* of David.
\p
\v 1 The fool hath said in his heart, \add There is\add* no God. They are corrupt, they have done abominable works, \add there is\add* none that doeth good.
\p
\v 2 The \nd LORD\nd* looked down from heaven upon the children of men, to see if there were any that did understand, \add and\add* seek God.
\p
\v 3 They are all gone aside, they are \add all\add* together become filthy: \add there is\add* none that doeth good, no, not one.\f + \fr 14:3 \fr*\fq filthy \fq*\ft - Heb. stinking\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Have all the workers of iniquity no knowledge? who eat up my people \add as\add* they eat bread, and call not upon the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 5 There were they in great fear: for God \add is\add* in the generation of the righteous.\f + \fr 14:5 \fr*\fq were… \fq*\ft - Heb. they feared a fear\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Ye have shamed the counsel of the poor, because the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* his refuge.
\p
\v 7 Oh that the salvation of Israel \add were come\add* out of Zion! when the \nd LORD\nd* bringeth back the captivity of his people, Jacob shall rejoice, \add and\add* Israel shall be glad.\f + \fr 14:7 \fr*\fq Oh… \fq*\ft - Heb. Who will give\ft*\f*
\c 15
\d A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 \nd LORD\nd*, who shall abide in thy tabernacle? who shall dwell in thy holy hill?\f + \fr 15:1 \fr*\fq abide \fq*\ft - Heb. sojourn\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 He that walketh uprightly, and worketh righteousness, and speaketh the truth in his heart.
\p
\v 3 \add He that\add* backbiteth not with his tongue, nor doeth evil to his neighbour, nor taketh up a reproach against his neighbour.\f + \fr 15:3 \fr*\fq taketh… \fq*\ft - or, receiveth, or, endureth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 In whose eyes a vile person is contemned; but he honoureth them that fear the \nd LORD\nd*. \add He that\add* sweareth to \add his own\add* hurt, and changeth not.
\p
\v 5 \add He that\add* putteth not out his money to usury, nor taketh reward against the innocent. He that doeth these \add things\add* shall never be moved.
\c 16
\d Michtam of David.
\p
\v 1 Preserve me, O God: for in thee do I put my trust.\f + \fr 16:1 \fr*\fq Michtam \fq*\ft - or, A golden Psalm\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 \add O my soul\add*, thou hast said unto the \nd LORD\nd*, Thou \add art\add* my Lord: my goodness \add extendeth\add* not to thee;
\p
\v 3 \add But\add* to the saints that \add are\add* in the earth, and \add to\add* the excellent, in whom \add is\add* all my delight.
\p
\v 4 Their sorrows shall be multiplied \add that\add* hasten \add after\add* another \add god:\add* their drink offerings of blood will I not offer, nor take up their names into my lips.\f + \fr 16:4 \fr*\fq hasten… \fq*\ft - or, give gifts to another\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* the portion of mine inheritance and of my cup: thou maintainest my lot.\f + \fr 16:5 \fr*\fq of mine… \fq*\ft - Heb. of my part\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 The lines are fallen unto me in pleasant \add places;\add* yea, I have a goodly heritage.
\p
\v 7 I will bless the \nd LORD\nd*, who hath given me counsel: my reins also instruct me in the night seasons.
\p
\v 8 I have set the \nd LORD\nd* always before me: because \add he is\add* at my right hand, I shall not be moved.
\p
\v 9 Therefore my heart is glad, and my glory rejoiceth: my flesh also shall rest in hope.\f + \fr 16:9 \fr*\fq rest… \fq*\ft - Heb. dwell confidently\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 For thou wilt not leave my soul in hell; neither wilt thou suffer thine Holy One to see corruption.
\p
\v 11 Thou wilt shew me the path of life: in thy presence \add is\add* fulness of joy; at thy right hand \add there are\add* pleasures for evermore.
\c 17
\d A Prayer of David.
\p
\v 1 Hear the right, O \nd LORD\nd*, attend unto my cry, give ear unto my prayer, \add that goeth\add* not out of feigned lips.\f + \fr 17:1 \fr*\fq the right \fq*\ft - Heb. justice\ft*\f*\f + \fr 17:1 \fr*\fq not… \fq*\ft - Heb. without lips of deceit\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Let my sentence come forth from thy presence; let thine eyes behold the things that are equal.
\p
\v 3 Thou hast proved mine heart; thou hast visited \add me\add* in the night; thou hast tried me, \add and\add* shalt find nothing; I am purposed \add that\add* my mouth shall not transgress.
\p
\v 4 Concerning the works of men, by the word of thy lips I have kept \add me from\add* the paths of the destroyer.
\p
\v 5 Hold up my goings in thy paths, \add that\add* my footsteps slip not.\f + \fr 17:5 \fr*\fq slip… \fq*\ft - Heb. be not moved\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 I have called upon thee, for thou wilt hear me, O God: incline thine ear unto me, \add and hear\add* my speech.
\p
\v 7 Shew thy marvellous lovingkindness, O thou that savest by thy right hand them which put their trust \add in thee\add* from those that rise up \add against them\add*.\f + \fr 17:7 \fr*\fq by thy… \fq*\ft - or, them which trust in thee from those that rise up against thy right hand\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 Keep me as the apple of the eye, hide me under the shadow of thy wings,
\p
\v 9 From the wicked that oppress me, \add from\add* my deadly enemies, \add who\add* compass me about.\f + \fr 17:9 \fr*\fq oppress \fq*\ft - Heb. waste\ft*\f*\f + \fr 17:9 \fr*\fq my… \fq*\ft - Heb. my enemies against the soul\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 They are inclosed in their own fat: with their mouth they speak proudly.
\p
\v 11 They have now compassed us in our steps: they have set their eyes bowing down to the earth;
\p
\v 12 Like as a lion \add that\add* is greedy of his prey, and as it were a young lion lurking in secret places.\f + \fr 17:12 \fr*\fq Like… \fq*\ft - Heb. The likeness of him (that is, of every one of them) is as a lion that desireth to ravin\ft*\f*\f + \fr 17:12 \fr*\fq lurking \fq*\ft - Heb. sitting\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 Arise, O \nd LORD\nd*, disappoint him, cast him down: deliver my soul from the wicked, \add which is\add* thy sword:\f + \fr 17:13 \fr*\fq disappoint… \fq*\ft - Heb. prevent his face\ft*\f*\f + \fr 17:13 \fr*\fq which is \fq*\ft - or, by\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 From men \add which are\add* thy hand, O \nd LORD\nd*, from men of the world, \add which have\add* their portion in \add this\add* life, and whose belly thou fillest with thy hid \add treasure:\add* they are full of children, and leave the rest of their \add substance\add* to their babes.\f + \fr 17:14 \fr*\fq which are \fq*\ft - or, by\ft*\f*\f + \fr 17:14 \fr*\fq they… \fq*\ft - or, their children are full\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 As for me, I will behold thy face in righteousness: I shall be satisfied, when I awake, with thy likeness.
\c 18
\d To the chief Musician, \add A Psalm\add* of David, the servant of the \nd LORD\nd*, who spake unto the \nd LORD\nd* the words of this song in the day \add that\add* the \nd LORD\nd* delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,
\p
\v 1 I will love thee, O \nd LORD\nd*, my strength.
\p
\v 2 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer; my God, my strength, in whom I will trust; my buckler, and the horn of my salvation, \add and\add* my high tower.\f + \fr 18:2 \fr*\fq my strength \fq*\ft - Heb. my rock\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 I will call upon the \nd LORD\nd*, \add who is worthy\add* to be praised: so shall I be saved from mine enemies.
\p
\v 4 The sorrows of death compassed me, and the floods of ungodly men made me afraid.\f + \fr 18:4 \fr*\fq ungodly men \fq*\ft - Heb. Belial\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 The sorrows of hell compassed me about: the snares of death prevented me.\f + \fr 18:5 \fr*\fq sorrows \fq*\ft - or, cords\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 In my distress I called upon the \nd LORD\nd*, and cried unto my God: he heard my voice out of his temple, and my cry came before him, \add even\add* into his ears.
\p
\v 7 Then the earth shook and trembled; the foundations also of the hills moved and were shaken, because he was wroth.
\p
\v 8 There went up a smoke out of his nostrils, and fire out of his mouth devoured: coals were kindled by it.\f + \fr 18:8 \fr*\fq out of his nostrils \fq*\ft - Heb. by his, etc\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 He bowed the heavens also, and came down: and darkness \add was\add* under his feet.
\p
\v 10 And he rode upon a cherub, and did fly: yea, he did fly upon the wings of the wind.
\p
\v 11 He made darkness his secret place; his pavilion round about him \add were\add* dark waters \add and\add* thick clouds of the skies.
\p
\v 12 At the brightness \add that was\add* before him his thick clouds passed, hail \add stones\add* and coals of fire.
\p
\v 13 The \nd LORD\nd* also thundered in the heavens, and the Highest gave his voice; hail \add stones\add* and coals of fire.
\p
\v 14 Yea, he sent out his arrows, and scattered them; and he shot out lightnings, and discomfited them.
\p
\v 15 Then the channels of waters were seen, and the foundations of the world were discovered at thy rebuke, O \nd LORD\nd*, at the blast of the breath of thy nostrils.
\p
\v 16 He sent from above, he took me, he drew me out of many waters.\f + \fr 18:16 \fr*\fq many \fq*\ft - or, great\ft*\f*
\p
\v 17 He delivered me from my strong enemy, and from them which hated me: for they were too strong for me.
\p
\v 18 They prevented me in the day of my calamity: but the \nd LORD\nd* was my stay.
\p
\v 19 He brought me forth also into a large place; he delivered me, because he delighted in me.
\p
\v 20 The \nd LORD\nd* rewarded me according to my righteousness; according to the cleanness of my hands hath he recompensed me.
\p
\v 21 For I have kept the ways of the \nd LORD\nd*, and have not wickedly departed from my God.
\p
\v 22 For all his judgments \add were\add* before me, and I did not put away his statutes from me.
\p
\v 23 I was also upright before him, and I kept myself from mine iniquity.\f + \fr 18:23 \fr*\fq before \fq*\ft - Heb. with\ft*\f*
\p
\v 24 Therefore hath the \nd LORD\nd* recompensed me according to my righteousness, according to the cleanness of my hands in his eyesight.\f + \fr 18:24 \fr*\fq in… \fq*\ft - Heb. before his eyes\ft*\f*
\p
\v 25 With the merciful thou wilt shew thyself merciful; with an upright man thou wilt shew thyself upright;
\p
\v 26 With the pure thou wilt shew thyself pure; and with the froward thou wilt shew thyself froward.\f + \fr 18:26 \fr*\fq shew thyself froward \fq*\ft - or, wrestle\ft*\f*
\p
\v 27 For thou wilt save the afflicted people; but wilt bring down high looks.
\p
\v 28 For thou wilt light my candle: the \nd LORD\nd* my God will enlighten my darkness.\f + \fr 18:28 \fr*\fq candle \fq*\ft - or, lamp\ft*\f*
\p
\v 29 For by thee I have run through a troop; and by my God have I leaped over a wall.\f + \fr 18:29 \fr*\fq run… \fq*\ft - or, broken\ft*\f*
\p
\v 30 \add As for\add* God, his way \add is\add* perfect: the word of the \nd LORD\nd* is tried: he \add is\add* a buckler to all those that trust in him.\f + \fr 18:30 \fr*\fq tried \fq*\ft - or, refined\ft*\f*
\p
\v 31 For who \add is\add* God save the \nd LORD\nd*? or who \add is\add* a rock save our God?
\p
\v 32 \add It is\add* God that girdeth me with strength, and maketh my way perfect.
\p
\v 33 He maketh my feet like hinds’ \add feet\add*, and setteth me upon my high places.
\p
\v 34 He teacheth my hands to war, so that a bow of steel is broken by mine arms.
\p
\v 35 Thou hast also given me the shield of thy salvation: and thy right hand hath holden me up, and thy gentleness hath made me great.\f + \fr 18:35 \fr*\fq thy gentleness… \fq*\ft - or, with thy meekness thou hast multiplied me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 36 Thou hast enlarged my steps under me, that my feet did not slip.\f + \fr 18:36 \fr*\fq my feet \fq*\ft - Heb. mine ankles\ft*\f*
\p
\v 37 I have pursued mine enemies, and overtaken them: neither did I turn again till they were consumed.
\p
\v 38 I have wounded them that they were not able to rise: they are fallen under my feet.
\p
\v 39 For thou hast girded me with strength unto the battle: thou hast subdued under me those that rose up against me.\f + \fr 18:39 \fr*\fq subdued \fq*\ft - Heb. caused to bow\ft*\f*
\p
\v 40 Thou hast also given me the necks of mine enemies; that I might destroy them that hate me.
\p
\v 41 They cried, but \add there was\add* none to save \add them: even\add* unto the \nd LORD\nd*, but he answered them not.
\p
\v 42 Then did I beat them small as the dust before the wind: I did cast them out as the dirt in the streets.
\p
\v 43 Thou hast delivered me from the strivings of the people; \add and\add* thou hast made me the head of the heathen: a people \add whom\add* I have not known shall serve me.
\p
\v 44 As soon as they hear of me, they shall obey me: the strangers shall submit themselves unto me.\f + \fr 18:44 \fr*\fq As soon… \fq*\ft - Heb. At the hearing of the ear\ft*\f*\f + \fr 18:44 \fr*\fq submit… \fq*\ft - or, yield feigned obedience\ft*\f*\f + \fr 18:44 \fr*\fq strangers \fq*\ft - Heb. sons of the stranger\ft*\f*
\p
\v 45 The strangers shall fade away, and be afraid out of their close places.\f + \fr 18:45 \fr*\fq strangers \fq*\ft - Heb. sons of the stranger\ft*\f*
\p
\v 46 The \nd LORD\nd* liveth; and blessed \add be\add* my rock; and let the God of my salvation be exalted.
\p
\v 47 \add It is\add* God that avengeth me, and subdueth the people under me.\f + \fr 18:47 \fr*\fq avengeth \fq*\ft - Heb. giveth avengements for\ft*\f*\f + \fr 18:47 \fr*\fq subdueth \fq*\ft - or, destroyeth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 48 He delivereth me from mine enemies: yea, thou liftest me up above those that rise up against me: thou hast delivered me from the violent man.\f + \fr 18:48 \fr*\fq violent… \fq*\ft - Heb. man of violence\ft*\f*
\p
\v 49 Therefore will I give thanks unto thee, O \nd LORD\nd*, among the heathen, and sing praises unto thy name.\f + \fr 18:49 \fr*\fq give… \fq*\ft - or, confess\ft*\f*
\p
\v 50 Great deliverance giveth he to his king; and sheweth mercy to his anointed, to David, and to his seed for evermore.
\c 19
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 The heavens declare the glory of God; and the firmament sheweth his handywork.
\p
\v 2 Day unto day uttereth speech, and night unto night sheweth knowledge.
\p
\v 3 \add There is\add* no speech nor language, \add where\add* their voice is not heard.\f + \fr 19:3 \fr*\fq where… \fq*\ft - or, without these their voice is heard: Heb. without their voice heard\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Their line is gone out through all the earth, and their words to the end of the world. In them hath he set a tabernacle for the sun,\f + \fr 19:4 \fr*\fq line \fq*\ft - or, rule, or, direction\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 Which \add is\add* as a bridegroom coming out of his chamber, \add and\add* rejoiceth as a strong man to run a race.
\p
\v 6 His going forth \add is\add* from the end of the heaven, and his circuit unto the ends of it: and there is nothing hid from the heat thereof.
\p
\v 7 The law of the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* sure, making wise the simple.\f + \fr 19:7 \fr*\fq law \fq*\ft - or, doctrine\ft*\f*\f + \fr 19:7 \fr*\fq converting \fq*\ft - or, restoring\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 The statutes of the \nd LORD\nd* \add are\add* right, rejoicing the heart: the commandment of the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* pure, enlightening the eyes.
\p
\v 9 The fear of the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* clean, enduring for ever: the judgments of the \nd LORD\nd* \add are\add* true \add and\add* righteous altogether.\f + \fr 19:9 \fr*\fq true \fq*\ft - Heb. truth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 More to be desired \add are they\add* than gold, yea, than much fine gold: sweeter also than honey and the honeycomb.\f + \fr 19:10 \fr*\fq the honeycomb \fq*\ft - Heb. the dropping of honeycombs\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 Moreover by them is thy servant warned: \add and\add* in keeping of them \add there is\add* great reward.
\p
\v 12 Who can understand \add his\add* errors? cleanse thou me from secret \add faults\add*.
\p
\v 13 Keep back thy servant also from presumptuous \add sins;\add* let them not have dominion over me: then shall I be upright, and I shall be innocent from the great transgression.\f + \fr 19:13 \fr*\fq the great \fq*\ft - or, much\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 Let the words of my mouth, and the meditation of my heart, be acceptable in thy sight, O \nd LORD\nd*, my strength, and my redeemer.\f + \fr 19:14 \fr*\fq strength \fq*\ft - Heb. rock\ft*\f*
\c 20
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 The \nd LORD\nd* hear thee in the day of trouble; the name of the God of Jacob defend thee;\f + \fr 20:1 \fr*\fq defend… \fq*\ft - Heb. set thee on an high place\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Send thee help from the sanctuary, and strengthen thee out of Zion;\f + \fr 20:2 \fr*\fq thee help \fq*\ft - Heb. thy help\ft*\f*\f + \fr 20:2 \fr*\fq strengthen \fq*\ft - Heb. support\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 Remember all thy offerings, and accept thy burnt sacrifice; Selah.\f + \fr 20:3 \fr*\fq accept \fq*\ft - Heb. turn to ashes: or, make fat\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Grant thee according to thine own heart, and fulfil all thy counsel.
\p
\v 5 We will rejoice in thy salvation, and in the name of our God we will set up \add our\add* banners: the \nd LORD\nd* fulfil all thy petitions.
\p
\v 6 Now know I that the \nd LORD\nd* saveth his anointed; he will hear him from his holy heaven with the saving strength of his right hand.\f + \fr 20:6 \fr*\fq his holy… \fq*\ft - Heb. the heaven of his holiness\ft*\f*\f + \fr 20:6 \fr*\fq with… \fq*\ft - Heb. by the strength of the salvation of\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 Some \add trust\add* in chariots, and some in horses: but we will remember the name of the \nd LORD\nd* our God.
\p
\v 8 They are brought down and fallen: but we are risen, and stand upright.
\p
\v 9 Save, \nd LORD\nd*: let the king hear us when we call.
\c 21
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 The king shall joy in thy strength, O \nd LORD\nd*; and in thy salvation how greatly shall he rejoice!
\p
\v 2 Thou hast given him his heart’s desire, and hast not withholden the request of his lips. Selah.
\p
\v 3 For thou preventest him with the blessings of goodness: thou settest a crown of pure gold on his head.
\p
\v 4 He asked life of thee, \add and\add* thou gavest \add it\add* him, \add even\add* length of days for ever and ever.
\p
\v 5 His glory \add is\add* great in thy salvation: honour and majesty hast thou laid upon him.
\p
\v 6 For thou hast made him most blessed for ever: thou hast made him exceeding glad with thy countenance.\f + \fr 21:6 \fr*\fq made him most… \fq*\ft - Heb. set him to be blessings\ft*\f*\f + \fr 21:6 \fr*\fq made him exceeding… \fq*\ft - Heb. make him glad with joy\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 For the king trusteth in the \nd LORD\nd*, and through the mercy of the most High he shall not be moved.
\p
\v 8 Thine hand shall find out all thine enemies: thy right hand shall find out those that hate thee.
\p
\v 9 Thou shalt make them as a fiery oven in the time of thine anger: the \nd LORD\nd* shall swallow them up in his wrath, and the fire shall devour them.
\p
\v 10 Their fruit shalt thou destroy from the earth, and their seed from among the children of men.
\p
\v 11 For they intended evil against thee: they imagined a mischievous device, \add which\add* they are not able \add to perform\add*.
\p
\v 12 Therefore shalt thou make them turn their back, \add when\add* thou shalt make ready \add thine arrows\add* upon thy strings against the face of them.\f + \fr 21:12 \fr*\fq shalt thou… \fq*\ft - or, thou shalt set them as a butt\ft*\f*\f + \fr 21:12 \fr*\fq back \fq*\ft - Heb. shoulder\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 Be thou exalted, \nd LORD\nd*, in thine own strength: \add so\add* will we sing and praise thy power.
\c 22
\d To the chief Musician upon Aijeleth Shahar, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me? \add why art thou so\add* far from helping me, \add and from\add* the words of my roaring?\f + \fr 22:1 \fr*\fq Aijeleth… \fq*\ft - or, the hind of the morning\ft*\f*\f + \fr 22:1 \fr*\fq helping… \fq*\ft - Heb. my salvation\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 O my God, I cry in the daytime, but thou hearest not; and in the night season, and am not silent.\f + \fr 22:2 \fr*\fq am… \fq*\ft - Heb. there is no silence to me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 But thou \add art\add* holy, \add O thou\add* that inhabitest the praises of Israel.
\p
\v 4 Our fathers trusted in thee: they trusted, and thou didst deliver them.
\p
\v 5 They cried unto thee, and were delivered: they trusted in thee, and were not confounded.
\p
\v 6 But I \add am\add* a worm, and no man; a reproach of men, and despised of the people.
\p
\v 7 All they that see me laugh me to scorn: they shoot out the lip, they shake the head, \add saying\add*,\f + \fr 22:7 \fr*\fq shoot… \fq*\ft - Heb. open\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 He trusted on the \nd LORD\nd* \add that\add* he would deliver him: let him deliver him, seeing he delighted in him.\f + \fr 22:8 \fr*\fq He trusted… \fq*\ft - Heb. He rolled himself on\ft*\f*\f + \fr 22:8 \fr*\fq seeing… \fq*\ft - or, if he delight in\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 But thou \add art\add* he that took me out of the womb: thou didst make me hope \add when I was\add* upon my mother’s breasts.\f + \fr 22:9 \fr*\fq didst… \fq*\ft - or, kept me in safety\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 I was cast upon thee from the womb: thou \add art\add* my God from my mother’s belly.
\p
\v 11 Be not far from me; for trouble \add is\add* near; for \add there is\add* none to help.\f + \fr 22:11 \fr*\fq none… \fq*\ft - Heb. not a helper\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 Many bulls have compassed me: strong \add bulls\add* of Bashan have beset me round.
\p
\v 13 They gaped upon me \add with\add* their mouths, \add as\add* a ravening and a roaring lion.\f + \fr 22:13 \fr*\fq gaped… \fq*\ft - Heb. opened their mouths against me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 I am poured out like water, and all my bones are out of joint: my heart is like wax; it is melted in the midst of my bowels.\f + \fr 22:14 \fr*\fq out of… \fq*\ft - or, sundered\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 My strength is dried up like a potsherd; and my tongue cleaveth to my jaws; and thou hast brought me into the dust of death.
\p
\v 16 For dogs have compassed me: the assembly of the wicked have inclosed me: they pierced my hands and my feet.
\p
\v 17 I may tell all my bones: they look \add and\add* stare upon me.
\p
\v 18 They part my garments among them, and cast lots upon my vesture.
\p
\v 19 But be not thou far from me, O \nd LORD\nd*: O my strength, haste thee to help me.
\p
\v 20 Deliver my soul from the sword; my darling from the power of the dog.\f + \fr 22:20 \fr*\fq my darling \fq*\ft - Heb. my only one\ft*\f*\f + \fr 22:20 \fr*\fq power \fq*\ft - Heb. hand\ft*\f*
\p
\v 21 Save me from the lion’s mouth: for thou hast heard me from the horns of the unicorns.
\p
\v 22 I will declare thy name unto my brethren: in the midst of the congregation will I praise thee.
\p
\v 23 Ye that fear the \nd LORD\nd*, praise him; all ye the seed of Jacob, glorify him; and fear him, all ye the seed of Israel.
\p
\v 24 For he hath not despised nor abhorred the affliction of the afflicted; neither hath he hid his face from him; but when he cried unto him, he heard.
\p
\v 25 My praise \add shall be\add* of thee in the great congregation: I will pay my vows before them that fear him.
\p
\v 26 The meek shall eat and be satisfied: they shall praise the \nd LORD\nd* that seek him: your heart shall live for ever.
\p
\v 27 All the ends of the world shall remember and turn unto the \nd LORD\nd*: and all the kindreds of the nations shall worship before thee.
\p
\v 28 For the kingdom \add is\add* the \nd LORD’s\nd*: and he \add is\add* the governor among the nations.
\p
\v 29 All \add they that be\add* fat upon earth shall eat and worship: all they that go down to the dust shall bow before him: and none can keep alive his own soul.
\p
\v 30 A seed shall serve him; it shall be accounted to the Lord for a generation.
\p
\v 31 They shall come, and shall declare his righteousness unto a people that shall be born, that he hath done \add this\add*.
\c 23
\d A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* my shepherd; I shall not want.
\p
\v 2 He maketh me to lie down in green pastures: he leadeth me beside the still waters.\f + \fr 23:2 \fr*\fq green… \fq*\ft - Heb. pastures of tender grass\ft*\f*\f + \fr 23:2 \fr*\fq still… \fq*\ft - Heb. waters of quietness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 He restoreth my soul: he leadeth me in the paths of righteousness for his name’s sake.
\p
\v 4 Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil: for thou \add art\add* with me; thy rod and thy staff they comfort me.
\p
\v 5 Thou preparest a table before me in the presence of mine enemies: thou anointest my head with oil; my cup runneth over.\f + \fr 23:5 \fr*\fq anointest \fq*\ft - Heb. makest fat\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Surely goodness and mercy shall follow me all the days of my life: and I will dwell in the house of the \nd LORD\nd* for ever.\f + \fr 23:6 \fr*\fq for ever \fq*\ft - Heb. to length of days\ft*\f*
\c 24
\d A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 The earth \add is\add* the \nd LORD’s\nd*, and the fulness thereof; the world, and they that dwell therein.
\p
\v 2 For he hath founded it upon the seas, and established it upon the floods.
\p
\v 3 Who shall ascend into the hill of the \nd LORD\nd*? or who shall stand in his holy place?
\p
\v 4 He that hath clean hands, and a pure heart; who hath not lifted up his soul unto vanity, nor sworn deceitfully.\f + \fr 24:4 \fr*\fq He… \fq*\ft - Heb. The clean of hands\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 He shall receive the blessing from the \nd LORD\nd*, and righteousness from the God of his salvation.
\p
\v 6 This \add is\add* the generation of them that seek him, that seek thy face, O Jacob. Selah.\f + \fr 24:6 \fr*\fq O Jacob \fq*\ft - or, O God of Jacob\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 Lift up your heads, O ye gates; and be ye lift up, ye everlasting doors; and the King of glory shall come in.
\p
\v 8 Who \add is\add* this King of glory? The \nd LORD\nd* strong and mighty, the \nd LORD\nd* mighty in battle.
\p
\v 9 Lift up your heads, O ye gates; even lift \add them\add* up, ye everlasting doors; and the King of glory shall come in.
\p
\v 10 Who is this King of glory? The \nd LORD\nd* of hosts, he \add is\add* the King of glory. Selah.
\c 25
\d \add A Psalm\add* of David.
\p
\v 1 Unto thee, O \nd LORD\nd*, do I lift up my soul.
\p
\v 2 O my God, I trust in thee: let me not be ashamed, let not mine enemies triumph over me.
\p
\v 3 Yea, let none that wait on thee be ashamed: let them be ashamed which transgress without cause.
\p
\v 4 Shew me thy ways, O \nd LORD\nd*; teach me thy paths.
\p
\v 5 Lead me in thy truth, and teach me: for thou \add art\add* the God of my salvation; on thee do I wait all the day.
\p
\v 6 Remember, O \nd LORD\nd*, thy tender mercies and thy lovingkindnesses; for they \add have been\add* ever of old.\f + \fr 25:6 \fr*\fq tender… \fq*\ft - Heb. bowels\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 Remember not the sins of my youth, nor my transgressions: according to thy mercy remember thou me for thy goodness’ sake, O \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 8 Good and upright \add is\add* the \nd LORD\nd*: therefore will he teach sinners in the way.
\p
\v 9 The meek will he guide in judgment: and the meek will he teach his way.
\p
\v 10 All the paths of the \nd LORD\nd* \add are\add* mercy and truth unto such as keep his covenant and his testimonies.
\p
\v 11 For thy name’s sake, O \nd LORD\nd*, pardon mine iniquity; for it \add is\add* great.
\p
\v 12 What man \add is\add* he that feareth the \nd LORD\nd*? him shall he teach in the way \add that\add* he shall choose.
\p
\v 13 His soul shall dwell at ease; and his seed shall inherit the earth.\f + \fr 25:13 \fr*\fq dwell… \fq*\ft - Heb. lodge in goodness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 The secret of the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* with them that fear him; and he will shew them his covenant.\f + \fr 25:14 \fr*\fq and… \fq*\ft - or, and his covenant to make them know it\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 Mine eyes \add are\add* ever toward the \nd LORD\nd*; for he shall pluck my feet out of the net.\f + \fr 25:15 \fr*\fq pluck \fq*\ft - Heb. bring forth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 Turn thee unto me, and have mercy upon me; for I \add am\add* desolate and afflicted.
\p
\v 17 The troubles of my heart are enlarged: \add O\add* bring thou me out of my distresses.
\p
\v 18 Look upon mine affliction and my pain; and forgive all my sins.
\p
\v 19 Consider mine enemies; for they are many; and they hate me with cruel hatred.\f + \fr 25:19 \fr*\fq cruel… \fq*\ft - Heb. hatred of violence\ft*\f*
\p
\v 20 O keep my soul, and deliver me: let me not be ashamed; for I put my trust in thee.
\p
\v 21 Let integrity and uprightness preserve me; for I wait on thee.
\p
\v 22 Redeem Israel, O God, out of all his troubles.
\c 26
\d \add A Psalm\add* of David.
\p
\v 1 Judge me, O \nd LORD\nd*; for I have walked in mine integrity: I have trusted also in the \nd LORD\nd*; \add therefore\add* I shall not slide.
\p
\v 2 Examine me, O \nd LORD\nd*, and prove me; try my reins and my heart.
\p
\v 3 For thy lovingkindness \add is\add* before mine eyes: and I have walked in thy truth.
\p
\v 4 I have not sat with vain persons, neither will I go in with dissemblers.
\p
\v 5 I have hated the congregation of evil doers; and will not sit with the wicked.
\p
\v 6 I will wash mine hands in innocency: so will I compass thine altar, O \nd LORD\nd*:
\p
\v 7 That I may publish with the voice of thanksgiving, and tell of all thy wondrous works.
\p
\v 8 \nd LORD\nd*, I have loved the habitation of thy house, and the place where thine honour dwelleth.\f + \fr 26:8 \fr*\fq where… \fq*\ft - Heb. of the tabernacle of thy honour\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 Gather not my soul with sinners, nor my life with bloody men:\f + \fr 26:9 \fr*\fq Gather… \fq*\ft - or, Take not away\ft*\f*\f + \fr 26:9 \fr*\fq bloody… \fq*\ft - Heb. men of blood\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 In whose hands \add is\add* mischief, and their right hand is full of bribes.\f + \fr 26:10 \fr*\fq full… \fq*\ft - Heb. filled with\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 But as for me, I will walk in mine integrity: redeem me, and be merciful unto me.
\p
\v 12 My foot standeth in an even place: in the congregations will I bless the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 27
\d \add A Psalm\add* of David.
\p
\v 1 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* my light and my salvation; whom shall I fear? the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* the strength of my life; of whom shall I be afraid?
\p
\v 2 When the wicked, \add even\add* mine enemies and my foes, came upon me to eat up my flesh, they stumbled and fell.\f + \fr 27:2 \fr*\fq came… \fq*\ft - Heb. approached against me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 Though an host should encamp against me, my heart shall not fear: though war should rise against me, in this \add will\add* I \add be\add* confident.
\p
\v 4 One \add thing\add* have I desired of the \nd LORD\nd*, that will I seek after; that I may dwell in the house of the \nd LORD\nd* all the days of my life, to behold the beauty of the \nd LORD\nd*, and to enquire in his temple.\f + \fr 27:4 \fr*\fq the beauty \fq*\ft - or, the delight\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 For in the time of trouble he shall hide me in his pavilion: in the secret of his tabernacle shall he hide me; he shall set me up upon a rock.
\p
\v 6 And now shall mine head be lifted up above mine enemies round about me: therefore will I offer in his tabernacle sacrifices of joy; I will sing, yea, I will sing praises unto the \nd LORD\nd*.\f + \fr 27:6 \fr*\fq joy \fq*\ft - Heb. shouting\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 Hear, O \nd LORD\nd*, \add when\add* I cry with my voice: have mercy also upon me, and answer me.
\p
\v 8 \add When thou saidst\add*, Seek ye my face; my heart said unto thee, Thy face, \nd LORD\nd*, will I seek.\f + \fr 27:8 \fr*\fq When… \fq*\ft - or, My heart said unto thee, Let my face seek thy face, etc\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 Hide not thy face \add far\add* from me; put not thy servant away in anger: thou hast been my help; leave me not, neither forsake me, O God of my salvation.
\p
\v 10 When my father and my mother forsake me, then the \nd LORD\nd* will take me up.\f + \fr 27:10 \fr*\fq take… \fq*\ft - Heb. gather me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 Teach me thy way, O \nd LORD\nd*, and lead me in a plain path, because of mine enemies.\f + \fr 27:11 \fr*\fq a plain… \fq*\ft - Heb. a way of plainness\ft*\f*\f + \fr 27:11 \fr*\fq mine… \fq*\ft - Heb. those which observe me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 Deliver me not over unto the will of mine enemies: for false witnesses are risen up against me, and such as breathe out cruelty.
\p
\v 13 \add I had fainted\add*, unless I had believed to see the goodness of the \nd LORD\nd* in the land of the living.
\p
\v 14 Wait on the \nd LORD\nd*: be of good courage, and he shall strengthen thine heart: wait, I say, on the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 28
\d \add A Psalm\add* of David.
\p
\v 1 Unto thee will I cry, O \nd LORD\nd* my rock; be not silent to me: lest, \add if\add* thou be silent to me, I become like them that go down into the pit.\f + \fr 28:1 \fr*\fq to me \fq*\ft - Heb. from me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Hear the voice of my supplications, when I cry unto thee, when I lift up my hands toward thy holy oracle.\f + \fr 28:2 \fr*\fq thy… \fq*\ft - or, the oracle of thy sanctuary\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 Draw me not away with the wicked, and with the workers of iniquity, which speak peace to their neighbours, but mischief \add is\add* in their hearts.
\p
\v 4 Give them according to their deeds, and according to the wickedness of their endeavours: give them after the work of their hands; render to them their desert.
\p
\v 5 Because they regard not the works of the \nd LORD\nd*, nor the operation of his hands, he shall destroy them, and not build them up.
\p
\v 6 Blessed \add be\add* the \nd LORD\nd*, because he hath heard the voice of my supplications.
\p
\v 7 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* my strength and my shield; my heart trusted in him, and I am helped: therefore my heart greatly rejoiceth; and with my song will I praise him.
\p
\v 8 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* their strength, and he \add is\add* the saving strength of his anointed.\f + \fr 28:8 \fr*\fq their \fq*\ft - or, his\ft*\f*\f + \fr 28:8 \fr*\fq saving… \fq*\ft - Heb. strength of salvations\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 Save thy people, and bless thine inheritance: feed them also, and lift them up for ever.\f + \fr 28:9 \fr*\fq feed \fq*\ft - or, rule\ft*\f*
\c 29
\d A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 Give unto the \nd LORD\nd*, O ye mighty, give unto the \nd LORD\nd* glory and strength.\f + \fr 29:1 \fr*\fq ye mighty \fq*\ft - Heb. ye sons of the mighty\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Give unto the \nd LORD\nd* the glory due unto his name; worship the \nd LORD\nd* in the beauty of holiness.\f + \fr 29:2 \fr*\fq the glory… \fq*\ft - Heb. the honour of his name\ft*\f*\f + \fr 29:2 \fr*\fq in… \fq*\ft - or, in his glorious sanctuary\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 The voice of the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* upon the waters: the God of glory thundereth: the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* upon many waters.\f + \fr 29:3 \fr*\fq many \fq*\ft - or, great\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 The voice of the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* powerful; the voice of the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* full of majesty.\f + \fr 29:4 \fr*\fq powerful \fq*\ft - Heb. in power\ft*\f*\f + \fr 29:4 \fr*\fq full… \fq*\ft - Heb. in majesty\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 The voice of the \nd LORD\nd* breaketh the cedars; yea, the \nd LORD\nd* breaketh the cedars of Lebanon.
\p
\v 6 He maketh them also to skip like a calf; Lebanon and Sirion like a young unicorn.
\p
\v 7 The voice of the \nd LORD\nd* divideth the flames of fire.\f + \fr 29:7 \fr*\fq divideth \fq*\ft - Heb. cutteth out\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 The voice of the \nd LORD\nd* shaketh the wilderness; the \nd LORD\nd* shaketh the wilderness of Kadesh.
\p
\v 9 The voice of the \nd LORD\nd* maketh the hinds to calve, and discovereth the forests: and in his temple doth every one speak of \add his\add* glory.\f + \fr 29:9 \fr*\fq to calve \fq*\ft - or, to be in pain\ft*\f*\f + \fr 29:9 \fr*\fq doth… \fq*\ft - or, every whit of it uttereth, etc\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 The \nd LORD\nd* sitteth upon the flood; yea, the \nd LORD\nd* sitteth King for ever.
\p
\v 11 The \nd LORD\nd* will give strength unto his people; the \nd LORD\nd* will bless his people with peace.
\c 30
\d A Psalm \add and\add* Song \add at\add* the dedication of the house of David.
\p
\v 1 I will extol thee, O \nd LORD\nd*; for thou hast lifted me up, and hast not made my foes to rejoice over me.
\p
\v 2 O \nd LORD\nd* my God, I cried unto thee, and thou hast healed me.
\p
\v 3 O \nd LORD\nd*, thou hast brought up my soul from the grave: thou hast kept me alive, that I should not go down to the pit.
\p
\v 4 Sing unto the \nd LORD\nd*, O ye saints of his, and give thanks at the remembrance of his holiness.\f + \fr 30:4 \fr*\fq at… \fq*\ft - or, to the memorial\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 For his anger \add endureth but\add* a moment; in his favour \add is\add* life: weeping may endure for a night, but joy \add cometh\add* in the morning.\f + \fr 30:5 \fr*\fq his anger… \fq*\ft - Heb. there is but a moment in his anger\ft*\f*\f + \fr 30:5 \fr*\fq for a night \fq*\ft - Heb. in the evening\ft*\f*\f + \fr 30:5 \fr*\fq joy \fq*\ft - Heb. singing\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 And in my prosperity I said, I shall never be moved.
\p
\v 7 \nd LORD\nd*, by thy favour thou hast made my mountain to stand strong: thou didst hide thy face, \add and\add* I was troubled.\f + \fr 30:7 \fr*\fq made… \fq*\ft - Heb. settled strength for my mountain\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 I cried to thee, O \nd LORD\nd*; and unto the \nd LORD\nd* I made supplication.
\p
\v 9 What profit \add is there\add* in my blood, when I go down to the pit? Shall the dust praise thee? shall it declare thy truth?
\p
\v 10 Hear, O \nd LORD\nd*, and have mercy upon me: \nd LORD\nd*, be thou my helper.
\p
\v 11 Thou hast turned for me my mourning into dancing: thou hast put off my sackcloth, and girded me with gladness;
\p
\v 12 To the end that \add my\add* glory may sing praise to thee, and not be silent. O \nd LORD\nd* my God, I will give thanks unto thee for ever.\f + \fr 30:12 \fr*\fq my glory \fq*\ft - that is, my tongue, or, my soul\ft*\f*
\c 31
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 In thee, O \nd LORD\nd*, do I put my trust; let me never be ashamed: deliver me in thy righteousness.
\p
\v 2 Bow down thine ear to me; deliver me speedily: be thou my strong rock, for an house of defence to save me.\f + \fr 31:2 \fr*\fq my… \fq*\ft - Heb. to me for a rock of strength\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 For thou \add art\add* my rock and my fortress; therefore for thy name’s sake lead me, and guide me.
\p
\v 4 Pull me out of the net that they have laid privily for me: for thou \add art\add* my strength.
\p
\v 5 Into thine hand I commit my spirit: thou hast redeemed me, O \nd LORD\nd* God of truth.
\p
\v 6 I have hated them that regard lying vanities: but I trust in the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 7 I will be glad and rejoice in thy mercy: for thou hast considered my trouble; thou hast known my soul in adversities;
\p
\v 8 And hast not shut me up into the hand of the enemy: thou hast set my feet in a large room.
\p
\v 9 Have mercy upon me, O \nd LORD\nd*, for I am in trouble: mine eye is consumed with grief, \add yea\add*, my soul and my belly.
\p
\v 10 For my life is spent with grief, and my years with sighing: my strength faileth because of mine iniquity, and my bones are consumed.
\p
\v 11 I was a reproach among all mine enemies, but especially among my neighbours, and a fear to mine acquaintance: they that did see me without fled from me.
\p
\v 12 I am forgotten as a dead man out of mind: I am like a broken vessel.\f + \fr 31:12 \fr*\fq a broken… \fq*\ft - Heb. a vessel that perisheth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 For I have heard the slander of many: fear \add was\add* on every side: while they took counsel together against me, they devised to take away my life.
\p
\v 14 But I trusted in thee, O \nd LORD\nd*: I said, Thou \add art\add* my God.
\p
\v 15 My times \add are\add* in thy hand: deliver me from the hand of mine enemies, and from them that persecute me.
\p
\v 16 Make thy face to shine upon thy servant: save me for thy mercies’ sake.
\p
\v 17 Let me not be ashamed, O \nd LORD\nd*; for I have called upon thee: let the wicked be ashamed, \add and\add* let them be silent in the grave.\f + \fr 31:17 \fr*\fq silent… \fq*\ft - or, cut off for\ft*\f*
\p
\v 18 Let the lying lips be put to silence; which speak grievous things proudly and contemptuously against the righteous.\f + \fr 31:18 \fr*\fq grievous… \fq*\ft - Heb. a hard thing\ft*\f*
\p
\v 19 \add Oh\add* how great \add is\add* thy goodness, which thou hast laid up for them that fear thee; \add which\add* thou hast wrought for them that trust in thee before the sons of men!
\p
\v 20 Thou shalt hide them in the secret of thy presence from the pride of man: thou shalt keep them secretly in a pavilion from the strife of tongues.
\p
\v 21 Blessed \add be\add* the \nd LORD\nd*: for he hath shewed me his marvellous kindness in a strong city.\f + \fr 31:21 \fr*\fq strong \fq*\ft - or, fenced\ft*\f*
\p
\v 22 For I said in my haste, I am cut off from before thine eyes: nevertheless thou heardest the voice of my supplications when I cried unto thee.
\p
\v 23 O love the \nd LORD\nd*, all ye his saints: \add for\add* the \nd LORD\nd* preserveth the faithful, and plentifully rewardeth the proud doer.
\p
\v 24 Be of good courage, and he shall strengthen your heart, all ye that hope in the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 32
\d \add A Psalm\add* of David, Maschil.
\p
\v 1 Blessed \add is he whose\add* transgression \add is\add* forgiven, \add whose\add* sin \add is\add* covered.\f + \fr 32:1 \fr*\fq A Psalm… \fq*\ft - or, A Psalm of David giving instruction\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Blessed \add is\add* the man unto whom the \nd LORD\nd* imputeth not iniquity, and in whose spirit \add there is\add* no guile.
\p
\v 3 When I kept silence, my bones waxed old through my roaring all the day long.
\p
\v 4 For day and night thy hand was heavy upon me: my moisture is turned into the drought of summer. Selah.
\p
\v 5 I acknowledged my sin unto thee, and mine iniquity have I not hid. I said, I will confess my transgressions unto the \nd LORD\nd*; and thou forgavest the iniquity of my sin. Selah.
\p
\v 6 For this shall every one that is godly pray unto thee in a time when thou mayest be found: surely in the floods of great waters they shall not come nigh unto him.\f + \fr 32:6 \fr*\fq when… \fq*\ft - Heb. of finding\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 Thou \add art\add* my hiding place; thou shalt preserve me from trouble; thou shalt compass me about with songs of deliverance. Selah.
\p
\v 8 I will instruct thee and teach thee in the way which thou shalt go: I will guide thee with mine eye.\f + \fr 32:8 \fr*\fq guide… \fq*\ft - Heb. counsel thee, mine eye shall be upon thee\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 Be ye not as the horse, \add or\add* as the mule, \add which\add* have no understanding: whose mouth must be held in with bit and bridle, lest they come near unto thee.
\p
\v 10 Many sorrows \add shall be\add* to the wicked: but he that trusteth in the \nd LORD\nd*, mercy shall compass him about.
\p
\v 11 Be glad in the \nd LORD\nd*, and rejoice, ye righteous: and shout for joy, all \add ye that are\add* upright in heart.
\c 33
\p
\v 1 Rejoice in the \nd LORD\nd*, O ye righteous: \add for\add* praise is comely for the upright.
\p
\v 2 Praise the \nd LORD\nd* with harp: sing unto him with the psaltery \add and\add* an instrument of ten strings.
\p
\v 3 Sing unto him a new song; play skilfully with a loud noise.
\p
\v 4 For the word of the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* right; and all his works \add are done\add* in truth.
\p
\v 5 He loveth righteousness and judgment: the earth is full of the goodness of the \nd LORD\nd*.\f + \fr 33:5 \fr*\fq goodness \fq*\ft - or, mercy\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 By the word of the \nd LORD\nd* were the heavens made; and all the host of them by the breath of his mouth.
\p
\v 7 He gathereth the waters of the sea together as an heap: he layeth up the depth in storehouses.
\p
\v 8 Let all the earth fear the \nd LORD\nd*: let all the inhabitants of the world stand in awe of him.
\p
\v 9 For he spake, and it was \add done;\add* he commanded, and it stood fast.
\p
\v 10 The \nd LORD\nd* bringeth the counsel of the heathen to nought: he maketh the devices of the people of none effect.\f + \fr 33:10 \fr*\fq bringeth \fq*\ft - Heb. maketh frustrate\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 The counsel of the \nd LORD\nd* standeth for ever, the thoughts of his heart to all generations.\f + \fr 33:11 \fr*\fq to all… \fq*\ft - Heb. to generation and generation\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 Blessed \add is\add* the nation whose God \add is\add* the \nd LORD\nd*; \add and\add* the people \add whom\add* he hath chosen for his own inheritance.
\p
\v 13 The \nd LORD\nd* looketh from heaven; he beholdeth all the sons of men.
\p
\v 14 From the place of his habitation he looketh upon all the inhabitants of the earth.
\p
\v 15 He fashioneth their hearts alike; he considereth all their works.
\p
\v 16 There is no king saved by the multitude of an host: a mighty man is not delivered by much strength.
\p
\v 17 An horse \add is\add* a vain thing for safety: neither shall he deliver \add any\add* by his great strength.
\p
\v 18 Behold, the eye of the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* upon them that fear him, upon them that hope in his mercy;
\p
\v 19 To deliver their soul from death, and to keep them alive in famine.
\p
\v 20 Our soul waiteth for the \nd LORD\nd*: he \add is\add* our help and our shield.
\p
\v 21 For our heart shall rejoice in him, because we have trusted in his holy name.
\p
\v 22 Let thy mercy, O \nd LORD\nd*, be upon us, according as we hope in thee.
\c 34
\d \add A Psalm\add* of David, when he changed his behaviour before Abimelech; who drove him away, and he departed.
\p
\v 1 I will bless the \nd LORD\nd* at all times: his praise \add shall\add* continually \add be\add* in my mouth.\f + \fr 34:1 \fr*\fq Abimelech \fq*\ft - or, Achish\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 My soul shall make her boast in the \nd LORD\nd*: the humble shall hear \add thereof\add*, and be glad.
\p
\v 3 O magnify the \nd LORD\nd* with me, and let us exalt his name together.
\p
\v 4 I sought the \nd LORD\nd*, and he heard me, and delivered me from all my fears.
\p
\v 5 They looked unto him, and were lightened: and their faces were not ashamed.\f + \fr 34:5 \fr*\fq were lightened \fq*\ft - or, they flowed unto him\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 This poor man cried, and the \nd LORD\nd* heard \add him\add*, and saved him out of all his troubles.
\p
\v 7 The angel of the \nd LORD\nd* encampeth round about them that fear him, and delivereth them.
\p
\v 8 O taste and see that the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* good: blessed \add is\add* the man \add that\add* trusteth in him.
\p
\v 9 O fear the \nd LORD\nd*, ye his saints: for \add there is\add* no want to them that fear him.
\p
\v 10 The young lions do lack, and suffer hunger: but they that seek the \nd LORD\nd* shall not want any good \add thing\add*.
\p
\v 11 Come, ye children, hearken unto me: I will teach you the fear of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 12 What man \add is he that\add* desireth life, \add and\add* loveth \add many\add* days, that he may see good?
\p
\v 13 Keep thy tongue from evil, and thy lips from speaking guile.
\p
\v 14 Depart from evil, and do good; seek peace, and pursue it.
\p
\v 15 The eyes of the \nd LORD\nd* \add are\add* upon the righteous, and his ears \add are open\add* unto their cry.
\p
\v 16 The face of the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* against them that do evil, to cut off the remembrance of them from the earth.
\p
\v 17 \add The righteous\add* cry, and the \nd LORD\nd* heareth, and delivereth them out of all their troubles.
\p
\v 18 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* nigh unto them that are of a broken heart; and saveth such as be of a contrite spirit.\f + \fr 34:18 \fr*\fq unto… \fq*\ft - Heb. to the broken of heart\ft*\f*\f + \fr 34:18 \fr*\fq of a contrite… \fq*\ft - Heb. contrite of spirit\ft*\f*
\p
\v 19 Many \add are\add* the afflictions of the righteous: but the \nd LORD\nd* delivereth him out of them all.
\p
\v 20 He keepeth all his bones: not one of them is broken.
\p
\v 21 Evil shall slay the wicked: and they that hate the righteous shall be desolate.\f + \fr 34:21 \fr*\fq desolate \fq*\ft - or, guilty\ft*\f*
\p
\v 22 The \nd LORD\nd* redeemeth the soul of his servants: and none of them that trust in him shall be desolate.\f + \fr 34:22 \fr*\fq desolate \fq*\ft - or, guilty\ft*\f*
\c 35
\d \add A Psalm\add* of David.
\p
\v 1 Plead \add my cause\add*, O \nd LORD\nd*, with them that strive with me: fight against them that fight against me.
\p
\v 2 Take hold of shield and buckler, and stand up for mine help.
\p
\v 3 Draw out also the spear, and stop \add the way\add* against them that persecute me: say unto my soul, I \add am\add* thy salvation.
\p
\v 4 Let them be confounded and put to shame that seek after my soul: let them be turned back and brought to confusion that devise my hurt.
\p
\v 5 Let them be as chaff before the wind: and let the angel of the \nd LORD\nd* chase \add them\add*.
\p
\v 6 Let their way be dark and slippery: and let the angel of the \nd LORD\nd* persecute them.\f + \fr 35:6 \fr*\fq dark… \fq*\ft - Heb. darkness and slipperiness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 For without cause have they hid for me their net \add in\add* a pit, \add which\add* without cause they have digged for my soul.
\p
\v 8 Let destruction come upon him at unawares; and let his net that he hath hid catch himself: into that very destruction let him fall.\f + \fr 35:8 \fr*\fq at… \fq*\ft - Heb. which he knoweth not of\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 And my soul shall be joyful in the \nd LORD\nd*: it shall rejoice in his salvation.
\p
\v 10 All my bones shall say, \nd LORD\nd*, who \add is\add* like unto thee, which deliverest the poor from him that is too strong for him, yea, the poor and the needy from him that spoileth him?
\p
\v 11 False witnesses did rise up; they laid to my charge \add things\add* that I knew not.\f + \fr 35:11 \fr*\fq False… \fq*\ft - Heb. Witnesses of wrong\ft*\f*\f + \fr 35:11 \fr*\fq they… \fq*\ft - Heb. they asked me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 They rewarded me evil for good \add to\add* the spoiling of my soul.\f + \fr 35:12 \fr*\fq spoiling \fq*\ft - Heb. depriving\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 But as for me, when they were sick, my clothing \add was\add* sackcloth: I humbled my soul with fasting; and my prayer returned into mine own bosom.\f + \fr 35:13 \fr*\fq humbled \fq*\ft - or, afflicted\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 I behaved myself as though \add he had been\add* my friend \add or\add* brother: I bowed down heavily, as one that mourneth \add for his\add* mother.\f + \fr 35:14 \fr*\fq behaved myself \fq*\ft - Heb. walked\ft*\f*\f + \fr 35:14 \fr*\fq as though… \fq*\ft - Heb. as a friend, as a brother to me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 But in mine adversity they rejoiced, and gathered themselves together: \add yea\add*, the abjects gathered themselves together against me, and I knew \add it\add* not; they did tear \add me\add*, and ceased not:\f + \fr 35:15 \fr*\fq adversity \fq*\ft - Heb. halting\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 With hypocritical mockers in feasts, they gnashed upon me with their teeth.
\p
\v 17 Lord, how long wilt thou look on? rescue my soul from their destructions, my darling from the lions.\f + \fr 35:17 \fr*\fq darling \fq*\ft - Heb. only one\ft*\f*
\p
\v 18 I will give thee thanks in the great congregation: I will praise thee among much people.\f + \fr 35:18 \fr*\fq much \fq*\ft - Heb. strong\ft*\f*
\p
\v 19 Let not them that are mine enemies wrongfully rejoice over me: \add neither\add* let them wink with the eye that hate me without a cause.\f + \fr 35:19 \fr*\fq wrongfully \fq*\ft - Heb. falsely\ft*\f*
\p
\v 20 For they speak not peace: but they devise deceitful matters against \add them that are\add* quiet in the land.
\p
\v 21 Yea, they opened their mouth wide against me, \add and\add* said, Aha, aha, our eye hath seen \add it\add*.
\p
\v 22 \add This\add* thou hast seen, O \nd LORD\nd*: keep not silence: O Lord, be not far from me.
\p
\v 23 Stir up thyself, and awake to my judgment, \add even\add* unto my cause, my God and my Lord.
\p
\v 24 Judge me, O \nd LORD\nd* my God, according to thy righteousness; and let them not rejoice over me.
\p
\v 25 Let them not say in their hearts, Ah, so would we have it: let them not say, We have swallowed him up.\f + \fr 35:25 \fr*\fq Ah… \fq*\ft - Heb. Ah, ah, our soul\ft*\f*
\p
\v 26 Let them be ashamed and brought to confusion together that rejoice at mine hurt: let them be clothed with shame and dishonour that magnify \add themselves\add* against me.
\p
\v 27 Let them shout for joy, and be glad, that favour my righteous cause: yea, let them say continually, Let the \nd LORD\nd* be magnified, which hath pleasure in the prosperity of his servant.\f + \fr 35:27 \fr*\fq righteous… \fq*\ft - Heb. righteousness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 28 And my tongue shall speak of thy righteousness \add and\add* of thy praise all the day long.
\c 36
\d To the chief Musician, \add A Psalm\add* of David the servant of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 1 The transgression of the wicked saith within my heart, \add that there is\add* no fear of God before his eyes.
\p
\v 2 For he flattereth himself in his own eyes, until his iniquity be found to be hateful.\f + \fr 36:2 \fr*\fq until… \fq*\ft - Heb. to find his iniquity to hate\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 The words of his mouth \add are\add* iniquity and deceit: he hath left off to be wise, \add and\add* to do good.
\p
\v 4 He deviseth mischief upon his bed; he setteth himself in a way \add that is\add* not good; he abhorreth not evil.\f + \fr 36:4 \fr*\fq mischief \fq*\ft - or, vanity\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 Thy mercy, O \nd LORD\nd*, \add is\add* in the heavens; \add and\add* thy faithfulness \add reacheth\add* unto the clouds.
\p
\v 6 Thy righteousness \add is\add* like the great mountains; thy judgments \add are\add* a great deep: O \nd LORD\nd*, thou preservest man and beast.\f + \fr 36:6 \fr*\fq the… \fq*\ft - Heb. the mountains of God\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 How excellent \add is\add* thy lovingkindness, O God! therefore the children of men put their trust under the shadow of thy wings.\f + \fr 36:7 \fr*\fq excellent \fq*\ft - Heb. precious\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 They shall be abundantly satisfied with the fatness of thy house; and thou shalt make them drink of the river of thy pleasures.\f + \fr 36:8 \fr*\fq abundantly… \fq*\ft - Heb. watered\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 For with thee \add is\add* the fountain of life: in thy light shall we see light.
\p
\v 10 O continue thy lovingkindness unto them that know thee; and thy righteousness to the upright in heart.\f + \fr 36:10 \fr*\fq continue \fq*\ft - Heb. draw out at length\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 Let not the foot of pride come against me, and let not the hand of the wicked remove me.
\p
\v 12 There are the workers of iniquity fallen: they are cast down, and shall not be able to rise.
\c 37
\d \add A Psalm\add* of David.
\p
\v 1 Fret not thyself because of evildoers, neither be thou envious against the workers of iniquity.
\p
\v 2 For they shall soon be cut down like the grass, and wither as the green herb.
\p
\v 3 Trust in the \nd LORD\nd*, and do good; \add so\add* shalt thou dwell in the land, and verily thou shalt be fed.\f + \fr 37:3 \fr*\fq verily \fq*\ft - Heb. in truth, or, stableness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Delight thyself also in the \nd LORD\nd*; and he shall give thee the desires of thine heart.
\p
\v 5 Commit thy way unto the \nd LORD\nd*; trust also in him; and he shall bring \add it\add* to pass.\f + \fr 37:5 \fr*\fq Commit… \fq*\ft - Heb. Roll thy way upon\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 And he shall bring forth thy righteousness as the light, and thy judgment as the noonday.
\p
\v 7 Rest in the \nd LORD\nd*, and wait patiently for him: fret not thyself because of him who prospereth in his way, because of the man who bringeth wicked devices to pass.\f + \fr 37:7 \fr*\fq Rest in \fq*\ft - Heb. Be silent to\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 Cease from anger, and forsake wrath: fret not thyself in any wise to do evil.
\p
\v 9 For evildoers shall be cut off: but those that wait upon the \nd LORD\nd*, they shall inherit the earth.
\p
\v 10 For yet a little while, and the wicked \add shall\add* not \add be:\add* yea, thou shalt diligently consider his place, and it \add shall\add* not \add be\add*.
\p
\v 11 But the meek shall inherit the earth; and shall delight themselves in the abundance of peace.
\p
\v 12 The wicked plotteth against the just, and gnasheth upon him with his teeth.\f + \fr 37:12 \fr*\fq plotteth \fq*\ft - or, practiseth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 The Lord shall laugh at him: for he seeth that his day is coming.
\p
\v 14 The wicked have drawn out the sword, and have bent their bow, to cast down the poor and needy, \add and\add* to slay such as be of upright conversation.\f + \fr 37:14 \fr*\fq such… \fq*\ft - Heb. the upright of way\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 Their sword shall enter into their own heart, and their bows shall be broken.
\p
\v 16 A little that a righteous man hath \add is\add* better than the riches of many wicked.
\p
\v 17 For the arms of the wicked shall be broken: but the \nd LORD\nd* upholdeth the righteous.
\p
\v 18 The \nd LORD\nd* knoweth the days of the upright: and their inheritance shall be for ever.
\p
\v 19 They shall not be ashamed in the evil time: and in the days of famine they shall be satisfied.
\p
\v 20 But the wicked shall perish, and the enemies of the \nd LORD\nd* \add shall be\add* as the fat of lambs: they shall consume; into smoke shall they consume away.\f + \fr 37:20 \fr*\fq the fat \fq*\ft - Heb. the preciousness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 21 The wicked borroweth, and payeth not again: but the righteous sheweth mercy, and giveth.
\p
\v 22 For \add such as be\add* blessed of him shall inherit the earth; and \add they that be\add* cursed of him shall be cut off.
\p
\v 23 The steps of a \add good\add* man are ordered by the \nd LORD\nd*: and he delighteth in his way.\f + \fr 37:23 \fr*\fq ordered \fq*\ft - or, established\ft*\f*
\p
\v 24 Though he fall, he shall not be utterly cast down: for the \nd LORD\nd* upholdeth \add him with\add* his hand.
\p
\v 25 I have been young, and \add now\add* am old; yet have I not seen the righteous forsaken, nor his seed begging bread.
\p
\v 26 \add He is\add* ever merciful, and lendeth; and his seed \add is\add* blessed.\f + \fr 37:26 \fr*\fq ever \fq*\ft - Heb. all the day\ft*\f*
\p
\v 27 Depart from evil, and do good; and dwell for evermore.
\p
\v 28 For the \nd LORD\nd* loveth judgment, and forsaketh not his saints; they are preserved for ever: but the seed of the wicked shall be cut off.
\p
\v 29 The righteous shall inherit the land, and dwell therein for ever.
\p
\v 30 The mouth of the righteous speaketh wisdom, and his tongue talketh of judgment.
\p
\v 31 The law of his God \add is\add* in his heart; none of his steps shall slide.\f + \fr 37:31 \fr*\fq steps \fq*\ft - or, goings\ft*\f*
\p
\v 32 The wicked watcheth the righteous, and seeketh to slay him.
\p
\v 33 The \nd LORD\nd* will not leave him in his hand, nor condemn him when he is judged.
\p
\v 34 Wait on the \nd LORD\nd*, and keep his way, and he shall exalt thee to inherit the land: when the wicked are cut off, thou shalt see \add it\add*.
\p
\v 35 I have seen the wicked in great power, and spreading himself like a green bay tree.\f + \fr 37:35 \fr*\fq a green… \fq*\ft - or, a green tree that groweth in his own soil\ft*\f*
\p
\v 36 Yet he passed away, and, lo, he \add was\add* not: yea, I sought him, but he could not be found.
\p
\v 37 Mark the perfect \add man\add*, and behold the upright: for the end of \add that\add* man \add is\add* peace.
\p
\v 38 But the transgressors shall be destroyed together: the end of the wicked shall be cut off.
\p
\v 39 But the salvation of the righteous \add is\add* of the \nd LORD\nd*: \add he is\add* their strength in the time of trouble.
\p
\v 40 And the \nd LORD\nd* shall help them, and deliver them: he shall deliver them from the wicked, and save them, because they trust in him.
\c 38
\d A Psalm of David, to bring to remembrance.
\p
\v 1 O \nd LORD\nd*, rebuke me not in thy wrath: neither chasten me in thy hot displeasure.
\p
\v 2 For thine arrows stick fast in me, and thy hand presseth me sore.
\p
\v 3 \add There is\add* no soundness in my flesh because of thine anger; neither \add is there any\add* rest in my bones because of my sin.\f + \fr 38:3 \fr*\fq rest \fq*\ft - Heb. peace, or, health\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 For mine iniquities are gone over mine head: as an heavy burden they are too heavy for me.
\p
\v 5 My wounds stink \add and\add* are corrupt because of my foolishness.
\p
\v 6 I am troubled; I am bowed down greatly; I go mourning all the day long.\f + \fr 38:6 \fr*\fq troubled \fq*\ft - Heb. wried\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 For my loins are filled with a loathsome \add disease:\add* and \add there is\add* no soundness in my flesh.
\p
\v 8 I am feeble and sore broken: I have roared by reason of the disquietness of my heart.
\p
\v 9 Lord, all my desire \add is\add* before thee; and my groaning is not hid from thee.
\p
\v 10 My heart panteth, my strength faileth me: as for the light of mine eyes, it also is gone from me.\f + \fr 38:10 \fr*\fq is gone… \fq*\ft - Heb. is not with me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 My lovers and my friends stand aloof from my sore; and my kinsmen stand afar off.\f + \fr 38:11 \fr*\fq sore \fq*\ft - Heb. stroke\ft*\f*\f + \fr 38:11 \fr*\fq my kinsmen \fq*\ft - or, my neighbours\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 They also that seek after my life lay snares \add for me:\add* and they that seek my hurt speak mischievous things, and imagine deceits all the day long.
\p
\v 13 But I, as a deaf \add man\add*, heard not; and \add I was\add* as a dumb man \add that\add* openeth not his mouth.
\p
\v 14 Thus I was as a man that heareth not, and in whose mouth \add are\add* no reproofs.
\p
\v 15 For in thee, O \nd LORD\nd*, do I hope: thou wilt hear, O Lord my God.\f + \fr 38:15 \fr*\fq in… \fq*\ft - or, thee do I wait for\ft*\f*\f + \fr 38:15 \fr*\fq hear \fq*\ft - or, answer\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 For I said, \add Hear me\add*, lest \add otherwise\add* they should rejoice over me: when my foot slippeth, they magnify \add themselves\add* against me.
\p
\v 17 For I \add am\add* ready to halt, and my sorrow \add is\add* continually before me.\f + \fr 38:17 \fr*\fq to halt \fq*\ft - Heb. for halting\ft*\f*
\p
\v 18 For I will declare mine iniquity; I will be sorry for my sin.
\p
\v 19 But mine enemies \add are\add* lively, \add and\add* they are strong: and they that hate me wrongfully are multiplied.\f + \fr 38:19 \fr*\fq are lively… \fq*\ft - Heb. being living, are strong\ft*\f*
\p
\v 20 They also that render evil for good are mine adversaries; because I follow \add the thing that\add* good \add is\add*.
\p
\v 21 Forsake me not, O \nd LORD\nd*: O my God, be not far from me.
\p
\v 22 Make haste to help me, O Lord my salvation.\f + \fr 38:22 \fr*\fq to… \fq*\ft - Heb. for my help\ft*\f*
\c 39
\d To the chief Musician, \add even\add* to Jeduthun, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 I said, I will take heed to my ways, that I sin not with my tongue: I will keep my mouth with a bridle, while the wicked is before me.\f + \fr 39:1 \fr*\fq my mouth… \fq*\ft - Heb. a bridle, or, muzzle for my mouth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 I was dumb with silence, I held my peace, \add even\add* from good; and my sorrow was stirred.\f + \fr 39:2 \fr*\fq stirred \fq*\ft - Heb. troubled\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 My heart was hot within me, while I was musing the fire burned: \add then\add* spake I with my tongue,
\p
\v 4 \nd LORD\nd*, make me to know mine end, and the measure of my days, what it \add is; that\add* I may know how frail I \add am\add*.\f + \fr 39:4 \fr*\fq how… \fq*\ft - or, what time I have here\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 Behold, thou hast made my days \add as\add* an handbreadth; and mine age \add is\add* as nothing before thee: verily every man at his best state \add is\add* altogether vanity. Selah.\f + \fr 39:5 \fr*\fq at… \fq*\ft - Heb. settled\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Surely every man walketh in a vain shew: surely they are disquieted in vain: he heapeth up \add riches\add*, and knoweth not who shall gather them.\f + \fr 39:6 \fr*\fq a vain… \fq*\ft - Heb. an image\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 And now, Lord, what wait I for? my hope \add is\add* in thee.
\p
\v 8 Deliver me from all my transgressions: make me not the reproach of the foolish.
\p
\v 9 I was dumb, I opened not my mouth; because thou didst \add it\add*.
\p
\v 10 Remove thy stroke away from me: I am consumed by the blow of thine hand.\f + \fr 39:10 \fr*\fq blow \fq*\ft - Heb. conflict\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 When thou with rebukes dost correct man for iniquity, thou makest his beauty to consume away like a moth: surely every man \add is\add* vanity. Selah.\f + \fr 39:11 \fr*\fq his… \fq*\ft - Heb. that which is to be desired in him to melt away\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 Hear my prayer, O \nd LORD\nd*, and give ear unto my cry; hold not thy peace at my tears: for I \add am\add* a stranger with thee, \add and\add* a sojourner, as all my fathers \add were\add*.
\p
\v 13 O spare me, that I may recover strength, before I go hence, and be no more.
\c 40
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 I waited patiently for the \nd LORD\nd*; and he inclined unto me, and heard my cry.\f + \fr 40:1 \fr*\fq I waited… \fq*\ft - Heb. In waiting I waited\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 He brought me up also out of an horrible pit, out of the miry clay, and set my feet upon a rock, \add and\add* established my goings.\f + \fr 40:2 \fr*\fq an… \fq*\ft - Heb. a pit of noise\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 And he hath put a new song in my mouth, \add even\add* praise unto our God: many shall see \add it\add*, and fear, and shall trust in the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 4 Blessed \add is\add* that man that maketh the \nd LORD\nd* his trust, and respecteth not the proud, nor such as turn aside to lies.
\p
\v 5 Many, O \nd LORD\nd* my God, \add are\add* thy wonderful works \add which\add* thou hast done, and thy thoughts \add which are\add* to us-ward: they cannot be reckoned up in order unto thee: \add if\add* I would declare and speak \add of them\add*, they are more than can be numbered.\f + \fr 40:5 \fr*\fq they cannot… \fq*\ft - or, none can order them unto thee\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Sacrifice and offering thou didst not desire; mine ears hast thou opened: burnt offering and sin offering hast thou not required.\f + \fr 40:6 \fr*\fq opened \fq*\ft - Heb. digged\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 Then said I, Lo, I come: in the volume of the book \add it is\add* written of me,
\p
\v 8 I delight to do thy will, O my God: yea, thy law \add is\add* within my heart.\f + \fr 40:8 \fr*\fq within… \fq*\ft - Heb. in the midst of my bowels\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 I have preached righteousness in the great congregation: lo, I have not refrained my lips, O \nd LORD\nd*, thou knowest.
\p
\v 10 I have not hid thy righteousness within my heart; I have declared thy faithfulness and thy salvation: I have not concealed thy lovingkindness and thy truth from the great congregation.
\p
\v 11 Withhold not thou thy tender mercies from me, O \nd LORD\nd*: let thy lovingkindness and thy truth continually preserve me.
\p
\v 12 For innumerable evils have compassed me about: mine iniquities have taken hold upon me, so that I am not able to look up; they are more than the hairs of mine head: therefore my heart faileth me.\f + \fr 40:12 \fr*\fq faileth \fq*\ft - Heb. forsaketh\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 Be pleased, O \nd LORD\nd*, to deliver me: O \nd LORD\nd*, make haste to help me.
\p
\v 14 Let them be ashamed and confounded together that seek after my soul to destroy it; let them be driven backward and put to shame that wish me evil.
\p
\v 15 Let them be desolate for a reward of their shame that say unto me, Aha, aha.
\p
\v 16 Let all those that seek thee rejoice and be glad in thee: let such as love thy salvation say continually, The \nd LORD\nd* be magnified.
\p
\v 17 But I \add am\add* poor and needy; \add yet\add* the Lord thinketh upon me: thou \add art\add* my help and my deliverer; make no tarrying, O my God.
\c 41
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 Blessed \add is\add* he that considereth the poor: the \nd LORD\nd* will deliver him in time of trouble.\f + \fr 41:1 \fr*\fq the poor \fq*\ft - or, the weak, or, sick\ft*\f*\f + \fr 41:1 \fr*\fq in time… \fq*\ft - Heb. in the day of evil\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 The \nd LORD\nd* will preserve him, and keep him alive; \add and\add* he shall be blessed upon the earth: and thou wilt not deliver him unto the will of his enemies.\f + \fr 41:2 \fr*\fq thou… \fq*\ft - or, do not thou deliver\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 The \nd LORD\nd* will strengthen him upon the bed of languishing: thou wilt make all his bed in his sickness.\f + \fr 41:3 \fr*\fq make \fq*\ft - Heb. turn\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 I said, \nd LORD\nd*, be merciful unto me: heal my soul; for I have sinned against thee.
\p
\v 5 Mine enemies speak evil of me, When shall he die, and his name perish?
\p
\v 6 And if he come to see \add me\add*, he speaketh vanity: his heart gathereth iniquity to itself; \add when\add* he goeth abroad, he telleth \add it\add*.
\p
\v 7 All that hate me whisper together against me: against me do they devise my hurt.\f + \fr 41:7 \fr*\fq my… \fq*\ft - Heb. evil to me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 An evil disease, \add say they\add*, cleaveth fast unto him: and \add now\add* that he lieth he shall rise up no more.\f + \fr 41:8 \fr*\fq An… \fq*\ft - Heb. A thing of Belial\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 Yea, mine own familiar friend, in whom I trusted, which did eat of my bread, hath lifted up \add his\add* heel against me.\f + \fr 41:9 \fr*\fq mine… \fq*\ft - Heb. the man of my peace\ft*\f*\f + \fr 41:9 \fr*\fq lifted… \fq*\ft - Heb. magnified\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 But thou, O \nd LORD\nd*, be merciful unto me, and raise me up, that I may requite them.
\p
\v 11 By this I know that thou favourest me, because mine enemy doth not triumph over me.
\p
\v 12 And as for me, thou upholdest me in mine integrity, and settest me before thy face for ever.
\p
\v 13 Blessed \add be\add* the \nd LORD\nd* God of Israel from everlasting, and to everlasting. Amen, and Amen.
\c 42
\d To the chief Musician, Maschil, for the sons of Korah.
\p
\v 1 As the hart panteth after the water brooks, so panteth my soul after thee, O God.\f + \fr 42:1 \fr*\fq Maschil… \fq*\ft - or, A Psalm giving instruction of the sons, etc\ft*\f*\f + \fr 42:1 \fr*\fq panteth \fq*\ft - Heb. brayeth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 My soul thirsteth for God, for the living God: when shall I come and appear before God?
\p
\v 3 My tears have been my meat day and night, while they continually say unto me, Where \add is\add* thy God?
\p
\v 4 When I remember these \add things\add*, I pour out my soul in me: for I had gone with the multitude, I went with them to the house of God, with the voice of joy and praise, with a multitude that kept holyday.
\p
\v 5 Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and \add why\add* art thou disquieted in me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him \add for\add* the help of his countenance.\f + \fr 42:5 \fr*\fq cast \fq*\ft - Heb. bowed\ft*\f*\f + \fr 42:5 \fr*\fq praise \fq*\ft - or, give thanks\ft*\f*\f + \fr 42:5 \fr*\fq for the… \fq*\ft - or, his presence is salvation\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 O my God, my soul is cast down within me: therefore will I remember thee from the land of Jordan, and of the Hermonites, from the hill Mizar.\f + \fr 42:6 \fr*\fq the hill… \fq*\ft - or, the little hill\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 Deep calleth unto deep at the noise of thy waterspouts: all thy waves and thy billows are gone over me.
\p
\v 8 \add Yet\add* the \nd LORD\nd* will command his lovingkindness in the daytime, and in the night his song \add shall be\add* with me, \add and\add* my prayer unto the God of my life.
\p
\v 9 I will say unto God my rock, Why hast thou forgotten me? why go I mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?
\p
\v 10 \add As\add* with a sword in my bones, mine enemies reproach me; while they say daily unto me, Where \add is\add* thy God?\f + \fr 42:10 \fr*\fq sword \fq*\ft - or, killing\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him, \add who is\add* the health of my countenance, and my God.
\c 43
\p
\v 1 Judge me, O God, and plead my cause against an ungodly nation: O deliver me from the deceitful and unjust man.\f + \fr 43:1 \fr*\fq ungodly \fq*\ft - or, unmerciful\ft*\f*\f + \fr 43:1 \fr*\fq the deceitful… \fq*\ft - Heb. a man of deceit and iniquity\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 For thou \add art\add* the God of my strength: why dost thou cast me off? why go I mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?
\p
\v 3 O send out thy light and thy truth: let them lead me; let them bring me unto thy holy hill, and to thy tabernacles.
\p
\v 4 Then will I go unto the altar of God, unto God my exceeding joy: yea, upon the harp will I praise thee, O God my God.\f + \fr 43:4 \fr*\fq my exceeding… \fq*\ft - Heb. the gladness of my joy\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope in God: for I shall yet praise him, \add who is\add* the health of my countenance, and my God.
\c 44
\d To the chief Musician for the sons of Korah, Maschil.
\p
\v 1 We have heard with our ears, O God, our fathers have told us, \add what\add* work thou didst in their days, in the times of old.\f + \fr 44:1 \fr*\fq Maschil \fq*\ft - or, of instruction\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 \add How\add* thou didst drive out the heathen with thy hand, and plantedst them; \add how\add* thou didst afflict the people, and cast them out.
\p
\v 3 For they got not the land in possession by their own sword, neither did their own arm save them: but thy right hand, and thine arm, and the light of thy countenance, because thou hadst a favour unto them.
\p
\v 4 Thou art my King, O God: command deliverances for Jacob.
\p
\v 5 Through thee will we push down our enemies: through thy name will we tread them under that rise up against us.
\p
\v 6 For I will not trust in my bow, neither shall my sword save me.
\p
\v 7 But thou hast saved us from our enemies, and hast put them to shame that hated us.
\p
\v 8 In God we boast all the day long, and praise thy name for ever. Selah.
\p
\v 9 But thou hast cast off, and put us to shame; and goest not forth with our armies.
\p
\v 10 Thou makest us to turn back from the enemy: and they which hate us spoil for themselves.
\p
\v 11 Thou hast given us like sheep \add appointed\add* for meat; and hast scattered us among the heathen.\f + \fr 44:11 \fr*\fq like… \fq*\ft - Heb. as sheep of meat\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 Thou sellest thy people for nought, and dost not increase \add thy wealth\add* by their price.\f + \fr 44:12 \fr*\fq for… \fq*\ft - Heb. without riches\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 Thou makest us a reproach to our neighbours, a scorn and a derision to them that are round about us.
\p
\v 14 Thou makest us a byword among the heathen, a shaking of the head among the people.
\p
\v 15 My confusion \add is\add* continually before me, and the shame of my face hath covered me,
\p
\v 16 For the voice of him that reproacheth and blasphemeth; by reason of the enemy and avenger.
\p
\v 17 All this is come upon us; yet have we not forgotten thee, neither have we dealt falsely in thy covenant.
\p
\v 18 Our heart is not turned back, neither have our steps declined from thy way;\f + \fr 44:18 \fr*\fq steps \fq*\ft - or, goings\ft*\f*
\p
\v 19 Though thou hast sore broken us in the place of dragons, and covered us with the shadow of death.
\p
\v 20 If we have forgotten the name of our God, or stretched out our hands to a strange god;
\p
\v 21 Shall not God search this out? for he knoweth the secrets of the heart.
\p
\v 22 Yea, for thy sake are we killed all the day long; we are counted as sheep for the slaughter.
\p
\v 23 Awake, why sleepest thou, O Lord? arise, cast \add us\add* not off for ever.
\p
\v 24 Wherefore hidest thou thy face, \add and\add* forgettest our affliction and our oppression?
\p
\v 25 For our soul is bowed down to the dust: our belly cleaveth unto the earth.
\p
\v 26 Arise for our help, and redeem us for thy mercies’ sake.\f + \fr 44:26 \fr*\fq for our… \fq*\ft - Heb. a help for us\ft*\f*
\c 45
\d To the chief Musician upon Shoshannim, for the sons of Korah, Maschil, A Song of loves.
\p
\v 1 My heart is inditing a good matter: I speak of the things which I have made touching the king: my tongue \add is\add* the pen of a ready writer.\f + \fr 45:1 \fr*\fq Maschil \fq*\ft - or, of instruction\ft*\f*\f + \fr 45:1 \fr*\fq is inditing \fq*\ft - Heb. boileth, or, bubbleth up\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Thou art fairer than the children of men: grace is poured into thy lips: therefore God hath blessed thee for ever.
\p
\v 3 Gird thy sword upon \add thy\add* thigh, O \add most\add* mighty, with thy glory and thy majesty.
\p
\v 4 And in thy majesty ride prosperously because of truth and meekness \add and\add* righteousness; and thy right hand shall teach thee terrible things.\f + \fr 45:4 \fr*\fq ride… \fq*\ft - Heb. prosper thou, ride thou\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 Thine arrows \add are\add* sharp in the heart of the king’s enemies; \add whereby\add* the people fall under thee.
\p
\v 6 Thy throne, O God, \add is\add* for ever and ever: the sceptre of thy kingdom \add is\add* a right sceptre.
\p
\v 7 Thou lovest righteousness, and hatest wickedness: therefore God, thy God, hath anointed thee with the oil of gladness above thy fellows.
\p
\v 8 All thy garments \add smell\add* of myrrh, and aloes, \add and\add* cassia, out of the ivory palaces, whereby they have made thee glad.
\p
\v 9 Kings’ daughters \add were\add* among thy honourable women: upon thy right hand did stand the queen in gold of Ophir.
\p
\v 10 Hearken, O daughter, and consider, and incline thine ear; forget also thine own people, and thy father’s house;
\p
\v 11 So shall the king greatly desire thy beauty: for he \add is\add* thy Lord; and worship thou him.
\p
\v 12 And the daughter of Tyre \add shall be there\add* with a gift; \add even\add* the rich among the people shall intreat thy favour.\f + \fr 45:12 \fr*\fq favour \fq*\ft - Heb. face\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 The king’s daughter \add is\add* all glorious within: her clothing \add is\add* of wrought gold.
\p
\v 14 She shall be brought unto the king in raiment of needlework: the virgins her companions that follow her shall be brought unto thee.
\p
\v 15 With gladness and rejoicing shall they be brought: they shall enter into the king’s palace.
\p
\v 16 Instead of thy fathers shall be thy children, whom thou mayest make princes in all the earth.
\p
\v 17 I will make thy name to be remembered in all generations: therefore shall the people praise thee for ever and ever.
\c 46
\d To the chief Musician for the sons of Korah, A Song upon Alamoth.
\p
\v 1 God \add is\add* our refuge and strength, a very present help in trouble.\f + \fr 46:1 \fr*\fq for \fq*\ft - or, of\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Therefore will not we fear, though the earth be removed, and though the mountains be carried into the midst of the sea;\f + \fr 46:2 \fr*\fq midst… \fq*\ft - Heb. heart of the seas\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 \add Though\add* the waters thereof roar \add and\add* be troubled, \add though\add* the mountains shake with the swelling thereof. Selah.
\p
\v 4 \add There is\add* a river, the streams whereof shall make glad the city of God, the holy \add place\add* of the tabernacles of the most High.
\p
\v 5 God \add is\add* in the midst of her; she shall not be moved: God shall help her, \add and that\add* right early.\f + \fr 46:5 \fr*\fq and… \fq*\ft - Heb. when the morning appeareth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 The heathen raged, the kingdoms were moved: he uttered his voice, the earth melted.
\p
\v 7 The \nd LORD\nd* of hosts \add is\add* with us; the God of Jacob \add is\add* our refuge. Selah.\f + \fr 46:7 \fr*\fq our… \fq*\ft - Heb. an high place for us\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 Come, behold the works of the \nd LORD\nd*, what desolations he hath made in the earth.
\p
\v 9 He maketh wars to cease unto the end of the earth; he breaketh the bow, and cutteth the spear in sunder; he burneth the chariot in the fire.
\p
\v 10 Be still, and know that I \add am\add* God: I will be exalted among the heathen, I will be exalted in the earth.
\p
\v 11 The \nd LORD\nd* of hosts \add is\add* with us; the God of Jacob \add is\add* our refuge. Selah.
\c 47
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm for the sons of Korah.
\p
\v 1 O clap your hands, all ye people; shout unto God with the voice of triumph.\f + \fr 47:1 \fr*\fq for \fq*\ft - or, of\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 For the \nd LORD\nd* most high \add is\add* terrible; \add he is\add* a great King over all the earth.
\p
\v 3 He shall subdue the people under us, and the nations under our feet.
\p
\v 4 He shall choose our inheritance for us, the excellency of Jacob whom he loved. Selah.
\p
\v 5 God is gone up with a shout, the \nd LORD\nd* with the sound of a trumpet.
\p
\v 6 Sing praises to God, sing praises: sing praises unto our King, sing praises.
\p
\v 7 For God \add is\add* the King of all the earth: sing ye praises with understanding.\f + \fr 47:7 \fr*\fq with \fq*\ft - or, every one that hath\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 God reigneth over the heathen: God sitteth upon the throne of his holiness.
\p
\v 9 The princes of the people are gathered together, \add even\add* the people of the God of Abraham: for the shields of the earth \add belong\add* unto God: he is greatly exalted.\f + \fr 47:9 \fr*\fq princes… \fq*\ft - or, voluntary of the people are gathered unto the people of the God of Abraham\ft*\f*
\c 48
\d A Song \add and\add* Psalm for the sons of Korah.
\p
\v 1 Great \add is\add* the \nd LORD\nd*, and greatly to be praised in the city of our God, \add in\add* the mountain of his holiness.\f + \fr 48:1 \fr*\fq for \fq*\ft - or, of\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Beautiful for situation, the joy of the whole earth, \add is\add* mount Zion, \add on\add* the sides of the north, the city of the great King.
\p
\v 3 God is known in her palaces for a refuge.
\p
\v 4 For, lo, the kings were assembled, they passed by together.
\p
\v 5 They saw \add it, and\add* so they marvelled; they were troubled, \add and\add* hasted away.
\p
\v 6 Fear took hold upon them there, \add and\add* pain, as of a woman in travail.
\p
\v 7 Thou breakest the ships of Tarshish with an east wind.
\p
\v 8 As we have heard, so have we seen in the city of the \nd LORD\nd* of hosts, in the city of our God: God will establish it for ever. Selah.
\p
\v 9 We have thought of thy lovingkindness, O God, in the midst of thy temple.
\p
\v 10 According to thy name, O God, so \add is\add* thy praise unto the ends of the earth: thy right hand is full of righteousness.
\p
\v 11 Let mount Zion rejoice, let the daughters of Judah be glad, because of thy judgments.
\p
\v 12 Walk about Zion, and go round about her: tell the towers thereof.
\p
\v 13 Mark ye well her bulwarks, consider her palaces; that ye may tell \add it\add* to the generation following.\f + \fr 48:13 \fr*\fq Mark… \fq*\ft - Heb. Set your heart to\ft*\f*\f + \fr 48:13 \fr*\fq consider \fq*\ft - or, raise up\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 For this God \add is\add* our God for ever and ever: he will be our guide \add even\add* unto death.
\c 49
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm for the sons of Korah.
\p
\v 1 Hear this, all \add ye\add* people; give ear, all \add ye\add* inhabitants of the world:\f + \fr 49:1 \fr*\fq for \fq*\ft - or, of\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Both low and high, rich and poor, together.
\p
\v 3 My mouth shall speak of wisdom; and the meditation of my heart \add shall be\add* of understanding.
\p
\v 4 I will incline mine ear to a parable: I will open my dark saying upon the harp.
\p
\v 5 Wherefore should I fear in the days of evil, \add when\add* the iniquity of my heels shall compass me about?
\p
\v 6 They that trust in their wealth, and boast themselves in the multitude of their riches;
\p
\v 7 None \add of them\add* can by any means redeem his brother, nor give to God a ransom for him:
\p
\v 8 (For the redemption of their soul \add is\add* precious, and it ceaseth for ever:)
\p
\v 9 That he should still live for ever, \add and\add* not see corruption.
\p
\v 10 For he seeth \add that\add* wise men die, likewise the fool and the brutish person perish, and leave their wealth to others.
\p
\v 11 Their inward thought \add is, that\add* their houses \add shall continue\add* for ever, \add and\add* their dwelling places to all generations; they call \add their\add* lands after their own names.\f + \fr 49:11 \fr*\fq all… \fq*\ft - Heb. generation and generation\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 Nevertheless man \add being\add* in honour abideth not: he is like the beasts \add that\add* perish.
\p
\v 13 This their way \add is\add* their folly: yet their posterity approve their sayings. Selah.\f + \fr 49:13 \fr*\fq approve… \fq*\ft - Heb. delight in their mouth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 Like sheep they are laid in the grave; death shall feed on them; and the upright shall have dominion over them in the morning; and their beauty shall consume in the grave from their dwelling.\f + \fr 49:14 \fr*\fq beauty \fq*\ft - or, strength\ft*\f*\f + \fr 49:14 \fr*\fq in the grave from… \fq*\ft - or, the grave being an habitation to every one of them\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 But God will redeem my soul from the power of the grave: for he shall receive me. Selah.\f + \fr 49:15 \fr*\fq power \fq*\ft - Heb. hand\ft*\f*\f + \fr 49:15 \fr*\fq the grave \fq*\ft - or, hell\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 Be not thou afraid when one is made rich, when the glory of his house is increased;
\p
\v 17 For when he dieth he shall carry nothing away: his glory shall not descend after him.
\p
\v 18 Though while he lived he blessed his soul: and \add men\add* will praise thee, when thou doest well to thyself.\f + \fr 49:18 \fr*\fq while… \fq*\ft - Heb. in his life\ft*\f*
\p
\v 19 He shall go to the generation of his fathers; they shall never see light.\f + \fr 49:19 \fr*\fq He… \fq*\ft - Heb. The soul shall\ft*\f*
\p
\v 20 Man \add that is\add* in honour, and understandeth not, is like the beasts \add that\add* perish.
\c 50
\d A Psalm of Asaph.
\p
\v 1 The mighty God, \add even\add* the \nd LORD\nd*, hath spoken, and called the earth from the rising of the sun unto the going down thereof.\f + \fr 50:1 \fr*\fq of… \fq*\ft - or, for Asaph\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Out of Zion, the perfection of beauty, God hath shined.
\p
\v 3 Our God shall come, and shall not keep silence: a fire shall devour before him, and it shall be very tempestuous round about him.
\p
\v 4 He shall call to the heavens from above, and to the earth, that he may judge his people.
\p
\v 5 Gather my saints together unto me; those that have made a covenant with me by sacrifice.
\p
\v 6 And the heavens shall declare his righteousness: for God \add is\add* judge himself. Selah.
\p
\v 7 Hear, O my people, and I will speak; O Israel, and I will testify against thee: I \add am\add* God, \add even\add* thy God.
\p
\v 8 I will not reprove thee for thy sacrifices or thy burnt offerings, \add to have been\add* continually before me.
\p
\v 9 I will take no bullock out of thy house, \add nor\add* he goats out of thy folds.
\p
\v 10 For every beast of the forest \add is\add* mine, \add and\add* the cattle upon a thousand hills.
\p
\v 11 I know all the fowls of the mountains: and the wild beasts of the field \add are\add* mine.\f + \fr 50:11 \fr*\fq mine \fq*\ft - Heb. with me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 If I were hungry, I would not tell thee: for the world \add is\add* mine, and the fulness thereof.
\p
\v 13 Will I eat the flesh of bulls, or drink the blood of goats?
\p
\v 14 Offer unto God thanksgiving; and pay thy vows unto the most High:
\p
\v 15 And call upon me in the day of trouble: I will deliver thee, and thou shalt glorify me.
\p
\v 16 But unto the wicked God saith, What hast thou to do to declare my statutes, or \add that\add* thou shouldest take my covenant in thy mouth?
\p
\v 17 Seeing thou hatest instruction, and castest my words behind thee.
\p
\v 18 When thou sawest a thief, then thou consentedst with him, and hast been partaker with adulterers.\f + \fr 50:18 \fr*\fq hast… \fq*\ft - Heb. thy portion was with\ft*\f*
\p
\v 19 Thou givest thy mouth to evil, and thy tongue frameth deceit.\f + \fr 50:19 \fr*\fq givest \fq*\ft - Heb. sendest\ft*\f*
\p
\v 20 Thou sittest \add and\add* speakest against thy brother; thou slanderest thine own mother’s son.
\p
\v 21 These \add things\add* hast thou done, and I kept silence; thou thoughtest that I was altogether \add such an one\add* as thyself: \add but\add* I will reprove thee, and set \add them\add* in order before thine eyes.
\p
\v 22 Now consider this, ye that forget God, lest I tear \add you\add* in pieces, and \add there be\add* none to deliver.
\p
\v 23 Whoso offereth praise glorifieth me: and to him that ordereth \add his\add* conversation \add aright\add* will I shew the salvation of God.\f + \fr 50:23 \fr*\fq that… \fq*\ft - Heb. that disposeth his way\ft*\f*
\c 51
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David, when Nathan the prophet came unto him, after he had gone in to Bath-sheba.
\p
\v 1 Have mercy upon me, O God, according to thy lovingkindness: according unto the multitude of thy tender mercies blot out my transgressions.
\p
\v 2 Wash me throughly from mine iniquity, and cleanse me from my sin.
\p
\v 3 For I acknowledge my transgressions: and my sin \add is\add* ever before me.
\p
\v 4 Against thee, thee only, have I sinned, and done \add this\add* evil in thy sight: that thou mightest be justified when thou speakest, \add and\add* be clear when thou judgest.
\p
\v 5 Behold, I was shapen in iniquity; and in sin did my mother conceive me.\f + \fr 51:5 \fr*\fq conceive… \fq*\ft - Heb. warm me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Behold, thou desirest truth in the inward parts: and in the hidden \add part\add* thou shalt make me to know wisdom.
\p
\v 7 Purge me with hyssop, and I shall be clean: wash me, and I shall be whiter than snow.
\p
\v 8 Make me to hear joy and gladness; \add that\add* the bones \add which\add* thou hast broken may rejoice.
\p
\v 9 Hide thy face from my sins, and blot out all mine iniquities.
\p
\v 10 Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me.\f + \fr 51:10 \fr*\fq right \fq*\ft - or, constant\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 Cast me not away from thy presence; and take not thy holy spirit from me.
\p
\v 12 Restore unto me the joy of thy salvation; and uphold me \add with thy\add* free spirit.
\p
\v 13 \add Then\add* will I teach transgressors thy ways; and sinners shall be converted unto thee.
\p
\v 14 Deliver me from bloodguiltiness, O God, thou God of my salvation: \add and\add* my tongue shall sing aloud of thy righteousness.\f + \fr 51:14 \fr*\fq bloodguiltiness \fq*\ft - Heb. bloods\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 O Lord, open thou my lips; and my mouth shall shew forth thy praise.
\p
\v 16 For thou desirest not sacrifice; else would I give \add it:\add* thou delightest not in burnt offering.\f + \fr 51:16 \fr*\fq else… \fq*\ft - or, that I should\ft*\f*
\p
\v 17 The sacrifices of God \add are\add* a broken spirit: a broken and a contrite heart, O God, thou wilt not despise.
\p
\v 18 Do good in thy good pleasure unto Zion: build thou the walls of Jerusalem.
\p
\v 19 Then shalt thou be pleased with the sacrifices of righteousness, with burnt offering and whole burnt offering: then shall they offer bullocks upon thine altar.
\c 52
\d To the chief Musician, Maschil, \add A Psalm\add* of David, when Doeg the Edomite came and told Saul, and said unto him, David is come to the house of Ahimelech.
\p
\v 1 Why boastest thou thyself in mischief, O mighty man? the goodness of God \add endureth\add* continually.\f + \fr 52:1 \fr*\fq Maschil \fq*\ft - or, of instruction\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Thy tongue deviseth mischiefs; like a sharp razor, working deceitfully.
\p
\v 3 Thou lovest evil more than good; \add and\add* lying rather than to speak righteousness. Selah.
\p
\v 4 Thou lovest all devouring words, O \add thou\add* deceitful tongue.\f + \fr 52:4 \fr*\fq O thou… \fq*\ft - or, and the deceitful tongue\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 God shall likewise destroy thee for ever, he shall take thee away, and pluck thee out of \add thy\add* dwelling place, and root thee out of the land of the living. Selah.\f + \fr 52:5 \fr*\fq destroy… \fq*\ft - Heb. beat thee down\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 The righteous also shall see, and fear, and shall laugh at him:
\p
\v 7 Lo, \add this is\add* the man \add that\add* made not God his strength; but trusted in the abundance of his riches, \add and\add* strengthened himself in his wickedness.\f + \fr 52:7 \fr*\fq wickedness \fq*\ft - or, substance\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 But I \add am\add* like a green olive tree in the house of God: I trust in the mercy of God for ever and ever.
\p
\v 9 I will praise thee for ever, because thou hast done \add it:\add* and I will wait on thy name; for \add it is\add* good before thy saints.
\c 53
\d To the chief Musician upon Mahalath, Maschil, \add A Psalm\add* of David.
\p
\v 1 The fool hath said in his heart, \add There is\add* no God. Corrupt are they, and have done abominable iniquity: \add there is\add* none that doeth good.\f + \fr 53:1 \fr*\fq Maschil \fq*\ft - or, of instruction\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 God looked down from heaven upon the children of men, to see if there were \add any\add* that did understand, that did seek God.
\p
\v 3 Every one of them is gone back: they are altogether become filthy; \add there is\add* none that doeth good, no, not one.
\p
\v 4 Have the workers of iniquity no knowledge? who eat up my people \add as\add* they eat bread: they have not called upon God.
\p
\v 5 There were they in great fear, \add where\add* no fear was: for God hath scattered the bones of him that encampeth \add against\add* thee: thou hast put \add them\add* to shame, because God hath despised them.\f + \fr 53:5 \fr*\fq were… \fq*\ft - Heb. they feared a fear\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Oh that the salvation of Israel \add were come\add* out of Zion! When God bringeth back the captivity of his people, Jacob shall rejoice, \add and\add* Israel shall be glad.\f + \fr 53:6 \fr*\fq Oh that… \fq*\ft - Heb. Who will give salvation, etc\ft*\f*
\c 54
\d To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, \add A Psalm\add* of David, when the Ziphims came and said to Saul, Doth not David hide himself with us?
\p
\v 1 Save me, O God, by thy name, and judge me by thy strength.\f + \fr 54:1 \fr*\fq chief… \fq*\ft - or, overseer\ft*\f*\f + \fr 54:1 \fr*\fq Maschil \fq*\ft - or, of instruction\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Hear my prayer, O God; give ear to the words of my mouth.
\p
\v 3 For strangers are risen up against me, and oppressors seek after my soul: they have not set God before them. Selah.
\p
\v 4 Behold, God \add is\add* mine helper: the Lord \add is\add* with them that uphold my soul.
\p
\v 5 He shall reward evil unto mine enemies: cut them off in thy truth.\f + \fr 54:5 \fr*\fq mine… \fq*\ft - Heb. those that observe me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 I will freely sacrifice unto thee: I will praise thy name, O \nd LORD\nd*; for \add it is\add* good.
\p
\v 7 For he hath delivered me out of all trouble: and mine eye hath seen \add his desire\add* upon mine enemies.
\c 55
\d To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, \add A Psalm\add* of David.
\p
\v 1 Give ear to my prayer, O God; and hide not thyself from my supplication.\f + \fr 55:1 \fr*\fq chief… \fq*\ft - or, overseer\ft*\f*\f + \fr 55:1 \fr*\fq Maschil \fq*\ft - or, of instruction\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Attend unto me, and hear me: I mourn in my complaint, and make a noise;
\p
\v 3 Because of the voice of the enemy, because of the oppression of the wicked: for they cast iniquity upon me, and in wrath they hate me.
\p
\v 4 My heart is sore pained within me: and the terrors of death are fallen upon me.
\p
\v 5 Fearfulness and trembling are come upon me, and horror hath overwhelmed me.\f + \fr 55:5 \fr*\fq overwhelmed \fq*\ft - Heb. covered\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 And I said, Oh that I had wings like a dove! \add for then\add* would I fly away, and be at rest.
\p
\v 7 Lo, \add then\add* would I wander far off, \add and\add* remain in the wilderness. Selah.
\p
\v 8 I would hasten my escape from the windy storm \add and\add* tempest.
\p
\v 9 Destroy, O Lord, \add and\add* divide their tongues: for I have seen violence and strife in the city.
\p
\v 10 Day and night they go about it upon the walls thereof: mischief also and sorrow \add are\add* in the midst of it.
\p
\v 11 Wickedness \add is\add* in the midst thereof: deceit and guile depart not from her streets.
\p
\v 12 For \add it was\add* not an enemy \add that\add* reproached me; then I could have borne \add it:\add* neither \add was it\add* he that hated me \add that\add* did magnify \add himself\add* against me; then I would have hid myself from him:
\p
\v 13 But \add it was\add* thou, a man mine equal, my guide, and mine acquaintance.\f + \fr 55:13 \fr*\fq mine equal \fq*\ft - Heb. according to my rank\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 We took sweet counsel together, \add and\add* walked unto the house of God in company.\f + \fr 55:14 \fr*\fq We… \fq*\ft - Heb. Who sweetened counsel\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 Let death seize upon them, \add and\add* let them go down quick into hell: for wickedness \add is\add* in their dwellings, \add and\add* among them.\f + \fr 55:15 \fr*\fq hell \fq*\ft - or, the grave\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 As for me, I will call upon God; and the \nd LORD\nd* shall save me.
\p
\v 17 Evening, and morning, and at noon, will I pray, and cry aloud: and he shall hear my voice.
\p
\v 18 He hath delivered my soul in peace from the battle \add that was\add* against me: for there were many with me.
\p
\v 19 God shall hear, and afflict them, even he that abideth of old. Selah. Because they have no changes, therefore they fear not God.\f + \fr 55:19 \fr*\fq Because… \fq*\ft - or, With whom also there be no changes, yet they\ft*\f*
\p
\v 20 He hath put forth his hands against such as be at peace with him: he hath broken his covenant.\f + \fr 55:20 \fr*\fq broken \fq*\ft - Heb. profaned\ft*\f*
\p
\v 21 \add The words\add* of his mouth were smoother than butter, but war \add was\add* in his heart: his words were softer than oil, yet \add were\add* they drawn swords.
\p
\v 22 Cast thy burden upon the \nd LORD\nd*, and he shall sustain thee: he shall never suffer the righteous to be moved.\f + \fr 55:22 \fr*\fq burden \fq*\ft - or, gift\ft*\f*
\p
\v 23 But thou, O God, shalt bring them down into the pit of destruction: bloody and deceitful men shall not live out half their days; but I will trust in thee.\f + \fr 55:23 \fr*\fq bloody… \fq*\ft - Heb. men of bloods and deceit\ft*\f*\f + \fr 55:23 \fr*\fq shall… \fq*\ft - Heb. shall not half their days\ft*\f*
\c 56
\d To the chief Musician upon Jonath-elem-rechokim, Michtam of David, when the Philistines took him in Gath.
\p
\v 1 Be merciful unto me, O God: for man would swallow me up; he fighting daily oppresseth me.\f + \fr 56:1 \fr*\fq Michtam… \fq*\ft - or, A golden Psalm of David\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Mine enemies would daily swallow \add me\add* up: for \add they be\add* many that fight against me, O thou most High.\f + \fr 56:2 \fr*\fq enemies \fq*\ft - Heb. observers\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 What time I am afraid, I will trust in thee.
\p
\v 4 In God I will praise his word, in God I have put my trust; I will not fear what flesh can do unto me.
\p
\v 5 Every day they wrest my words: all their thoughts \add are\add* against me for evil.
\p
\v 6 They gather themselves together, they hide themselves, they mark my steps, when they wait for my soul.
\p
\v 7 Shall they escape by iniquity? in \add thine\add* anger cast down the people, O God.
\p
\v 8 Thou tellest my wanderings: put thou my tears into thy bottle: \add are they\add* not in thy book?
\p
\v 9 When I cry \add unto thee\add*, then shall mine enemies turn back: this I know; for God \add is\add* for me.
\p
\v 10 In God will I praise \add his\add* word: in the \nd LORD\nd* will I praise \add his\add* word.
\p
\v 11 In God have I put my trust: I will not be afraid what man can do unto me.
\p
\v 12 Thy vows \add are\add* upon me, O God: I will render praises unto thee.
\p
\v 13 For thou hast delivered my soul from death: \add wilt\add* not \add thou deliver\add* my feet from falling, that I may walk before God in the light of the living?
\c 57
\d To the chief Musician, Al-taschith, Michtam of David, when he fled from Saul in the cave.
\p
\v 1 Be merciful unto me, O God, be merciful unto me: for my soul trusteth in thee: yea, in the shadow of thy wings will I make my refuge, until \add these\add* calamities be overpast.\f + \fr 57:1 \fr*\fq Al-taschith \fq*\ft - or, Destroy not\ft*\f*\f + \fr 57:1 \fr*\fq Michtam \fq*\ft - or, A golden Psalm\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 I will cry unto God most high; unto God that performeth \add all things\add* for me.
\p
\v 3 He shall send from heaven, and save me \add from\add* the reproach of him that would swallow me up. Selah. God shall send forth his mercy and his truth.\f + \fr 57:3 \fr*\fq from the… \fq*\ft - or, he reproacheth him that\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 My soul \add is\add* among lions: \add and\add* I lie \add even among\add* them that are set on fire, \add even\add* the sons of men, whose teeth \add are\add* spears and arrows, and their tongue a sharp sword.
\p
\v 5 Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens; \add let\add* thy glory \add be\add* above all the earth.
\p
\v 6 They have prepared a net for my steps; my soul is bowed down: they have digged a pit before me, into the midst whereof they are fallen \add themselves\add*. Selah.
\p
\v 7 My heart is fixed, O God, my heart is fixed: I will sing and give praise.\f + \fr 57:7 \fr*\fq fixed \fq*\ft - or, prepared\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 Awake up, my glory; awake, psaltery and harp: I \add myself\add* will awake early.
\p
\v 9 I will praise thee, O Lord, among the people: I will sing unto thee among the nations.
\p
\v 10 For thy mercy \add is\add* great unto the heavens, and thy truth unto the clouds.
\p
\v 11 Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens: \add let\add* thy glory \add be\add* above all the earth.
\c 58
\d To the chief Musician, Al-taschith, Michtam of David.
\p
\v 1 Do ye indeed speak righteousness, O congregation? do ye judge uprightly, O ye sons of men?\f + \fr 58:1 \fr*\fq Al-taschith… \fq*\ft - or, Destroy not\ft*\f*\f + \fr 58:1 \fr*\fq Michtam \fq*\ft - or, A golden Psalm\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Yea, in heart ye work wickedness; ye weigh the violence of your hands in the earth.
\p
\v 3 The wicked are estranged from the womb: they go astray as soon as they be born, speaking lies.\f + \fr 58:3 \fr*\fq as soon… \fq*\ft - Heb. from the belly\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Their poison \add is\add* like the poison of a serpent: \add they are\add* like the deaf adder \add that\add* stoppeth her ear;\f + \fr 58:4 \fr*\fq like the poison \fq*\ft - Heb. according to the likeness, etc\ft*\f*\f + \fr 58:4 \fr*\fq adder \fq*\ft - or, asp\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 Which will not hearken to the voice of charmers, charming never so wisely.\f + \fr 58:5 \fr*\fq charming… \fq*\ft - or, be the charmer never so cunning\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Break their teeth, O God, in their mouth: break out the great teeth of the young lions, O \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 7 Let them melt away as waters \add which\add* run continually: \add when\add* he bendeth \add his bow to shoot\add* his arrows, let them be as cut in pieces.
\p
\v 8 As a snail \add which\add* melteth, let \add every one of them\add* pass away: \add like\add* the untimely birth of a woman, \add that\add* they may not see the sun.
\p
\v 9 Before your pots can feel the thorns, he shall take them away as with a whirlwind, both living, and in \add his\add* wrath.\f + \fr 58:9 \fr*\fq both… \fq*\ft - Heb. as living as wrath\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 The righteous shall rejoice when he seeth the vengeance: he shall wash his feet in the blood of the wicked.
\p
\v 11 So that a man shall say, Verily \add there is\add* a reward for the righteous: verily he is a God that judgeth in the earth.\f + \fr 58:11 \fr*\fq a reward… \fq*\ft - Heb. fruit of the, etc\ft*\f*
\c 59
\d To the chief Musician, Al-taschith, Michtam of David; when Saul sent, and they watched the house to kill him.
\p
\v 1 Deliver me from mine enemies, O my God: defend me from them that rise up against me.\f + \fr 59:1 \fr*\fq Al-taschith… \fq*\ft - or, Destroy not\ft*\f*\f + \fr 59:1 \fr*\fq Michtam \fq*\ft - or, A golden Psalm\ft*\f*\f + \fr 59:1 \fr*\fq defend… \fq*\ft - Heb. set me on high\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Deliver me from the workers of iniquity, and save me from bloody men.
\p
\v 3 For, lo, they lie in wait for my soul: the mighty are gathered against me; not \add for\add* my transgression, nor \add for\add* my sin, O \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 4 They run and prepare themselves without \add my\add* fault: awake to help me, and behold.\f + \fr 59:4 \fr*\fq help \fq*\ft - Heb. meet\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 Thou therefore, O \nd LORD\nd* God of hosts, the God of Israel, awake to visit all the heathen: be not merciful to any wicked transgressors. Selah.
\p
\v 6 They return at evening: they make a noise like a dog, and go round about the city.
\p
\v 7 Behold, they belch out with their mouth: swords \add are\add* in their lips: for who, \add say they\add*, doth hear?
\p
\v 8 But thou, O \nd LORD\nd*, shalt laugh at them; thou shalt have all the heathen in derision.
\p
\v 9 \add Because of\add* his strength will I wait upon thee: for God \add is\add* my defence.\f + \fr 59:9 \fr*\fq defence \fq*\ft - Heb. high place\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 The God of my mercy shall prevent me: God shall let me see \add my desire\add* upon mine enemies.\f + \fr 59:10 \fr*\fq enemies \fq*\ft - Heb. observers\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 Slay them not, lest my people forget: scatter them by thy power; and bring them down, O Lord our shield.
\p
\v 12 \add For\add* the sin of their mouth \add and\add* the words of their lips let them even be taken in their pride: and for cursing and lying \add which\add* they speak.
\p
\v 13 Consume \add them\add* in wrath, consume \add them\add*, that they \add may\add* not \add be:\add* and let them know that God ruleth in Jacob unto the ends of the earth. Selah.
\p
\v 14 And at evening let them return; \add and\add* let them make a noise like a dog, and go round about the city.
\p
\v 15 Let them wander up and down for meat, and grudge if they be not satisfied.\f + \fr 59:15 \fr*\fq for meat \fq*\ft - Heb. to eat\ft*\f*\f + \fr 59:15 \fr*\fq and grudge… \fq*\ft - or, if they be not satisfied, then they will stay all night\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 But I will sing of thy power; yea, I will sing aloud of thy mercy in the morning: for thou hast been my defence and refuge in the day of my trouble.
\p
\v 17 Unto thee, O my strength, will I sing: for God \add is\add* my defence, \add and\add* the God of my mercy.
\c 60
\d To the chief Musician upon Shushan-eduth, Michtam of David, to teach; when he strove with Aram-naharaim and with Aram-zobah, when Joab returned, and smote of Edom in the valley of salt twelve thousand.
\p
\v 1 O God, thou hast cast us off, thou hast scattered us, thou hast been displeased; O turn thyself to us again.\f + \fr 60:1 \fr*\fq Michtam \fq*\ft - or, A golden Psalm\ft*\f*\f + \fr 60:1 \fr*\fq scattered \fq*\ft - Heb. broken\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Thou hast made the earth to tremble; thou hast broken it: heal the breaches thereof; for it shaketh.
\p
\v 3 Thou hast shewed thy people hard things: thou hast made us to drink the wine of astonishment.
\p
\v 4 Thou hast given a banner to them that fear thee, that it may be displayed because of the truth. Selah.
\p
\v 5 That thy beloved may be delivered; save \add with\add* thy right hand, and hear me.
\p
\v 6 God hath spoken in his holiness; I will rejoice, I will divide Shechem, and mete out the valley of Succoth.
\p
\v 7 Gilead \add is\add* mine, and Manasseh \add is\add* mine; Ephraim also \add is\add* the strength of mine head; Judah \add is\add* my lawgiver;
\p
\v 8 Moab \add is\add* my washpot; over Edom will I cast out my shoe: Philistia, triumph thou because of me.\f + \fr 60:8 \fr*\fq triumph… \fq*\ft - or, triumph thou over me: (by an irony)\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 Who will bring me \add into\add* the strong city? who will lead me into Edom?\f + \fr 60:9 \fr*\fq strong… \fq*\ft - Heb. city of strength?\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 \add Wilt\add* not thou, O God, \add which\add* hadst cast us off? and \add thou\add*, O God, \add which\add* didst not go out with our armies?
\p
\v 11 Give us help from trouble: for vain \add is\add* the help of man.\f + \fr 60:11 \fr*\fq help of man \fq*\ft - Heb. salvation, etc\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 Through God we shall do valiantly: for he \add it is that\add* shall tread down our enemies.
\c 61
\d To the chief Musician upon Neginah, \add A Psalm\add* of David.
\p
\v 1 Hear my cry, O God; attend unto my prayer.
\p
\v 2 From the end of the earth will I cry unto thee, when my heart is overwhelmed: lead me to the rock \add that\add* is higher than I.
\p
\v 3 For thou hast been a shelter for me, \add and\add* a strong tower from the enemy.
\p
\v 4 I will abide in thy tabernacle for ever: I will trust in the covert of thy wings. Selah.\f + \fr 61:4 \fr*\fq trust \fq*\ft - or, make my refuge\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 For thou, O God, hast heard my vows: thou hast given \add me\add* the heritage of those that fear thy name.
\p
\v 6 Thou wilt prolong the king’s life: \add and\add* his years as many generations.\f + \fr 61:6 \fr*\fq Thou… \fq*\ft - Heb. Thou shalt add days to the days of the king\ft*\f*\f + \fr 61:6 \fr*\fq as… \fq*\ft - Heb. as generation and generation\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 He shall abide before God for ever: O prepare mercy and truth, \add which\add* may preserve him.
\p
\v 8 So will I sing praise unto thy name for ever, that I may daily perform my vows.
\c 62
\d To the chief Musician, to Jeduthun, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 Truly my soul waiteth upon God: from him \add cometh\add* my salvation.\f + \fr 62:1 \fr*\fq Truly \fq*\ft - or, Only\ft*\f*\f + \fr 62:1 \fr*\fq waiteth \fq*\ft - Heb. is silent\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 He only \add is\add* my rock and my salvation; \add he is\add* my defence; I shall not be greatly moved.\f + \fr 62:2 \fr*\fq defence \fq*\ft - Heb. high place\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 How long will ye imagine mischief against a man? ye shall be slain all of you: as a bowing wall \add shall ye be, and as\add* a tottering fence.
\p
\v 4 They only consult to cast \add him\add* down from his excellency: they delight in lies: they bless with their mouth, but they curse inwardly. Selah.\f + \fr 62:4 \fr*\fq inwardly \fq*\ft - Heb. in their inward parts\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 My soul, wait thou only upon God; for my expectation \add is\add* from him.
\p
\v 6 He only \add is\add* my rock and my salvation: \add he is\add* my defence; I shall not be moved.
\p
\v 7 In God \add is\add* my salvation and my glory: the rock of my strength, \add and\add* my refuge, \add is\add* in God.
\p
\v 8 Trust in him at all times; \add ye\add* people, pour out your heart before him: God \add is\add* a refuge for us. Selah.
\p
\v 9 Surely men of low degree \add are\add* vanity, \add and\add* men of high degree \add are\add* a lie: to be laid in the balance, they \add are\add* altogether \add lighter\add* than vanity.\f + \fr 62:9 \fr*\fq altogether \fq*\ft - or, alike\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 Trust not in oppression, and become not vain in robbery: if riches increase, set not your heart \add upon them\add*.
\p
\v 11 God hath spoken once; twice have I heard this; that power \add belongeth\add* unto God.\f + \fr 62:11 \fr*\fq power \fq*\ft - or, strength\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 Also unto thee, O Lord, \add belongeth\add* mercy: for thou renderest to every man according to his work.
\c 63
\d A Psalm of David, when he was in the wilderness of Judah.
\p
\v 1 O God, thou \add art\add* my God; early will I seek thee: my soul thirsteth for thee, my flesh longeth for thee in a dry and thirsty land, where no water is;\f + \fr 63:1 \fr*\fq thirsty \fq*\ft - Heb. weary\ft*\f*\f + \fr 63:1 \fr*\fq where… \fq*\ft - without water\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 To see thy power and thy glory, so \add as\add* I have seen thee in the sanctuary.
\p
\v 3 Because thy lovingkindness \add is\add* better than life, my lips shall praise thee.
\p
\v 4 Thus will I bless thee while I live: I will lift up my hands in thy name.
\p
\v 5 My soul shall be satisfied as \add with\add* marrow and fatness; and my mouth shall praise \add thee\add* with joyful lips:\f + \fr 63:5 \fr*\fq marrow \fq*\ft - Heb. fatness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 When I remember thee upon my bed, \add and\add* meditate on thee in the \add night\add* watches.
\p
\v 7 Because thou hast been my help, therefore in the shadow of thy wings will I rejoice.
\p
\v 8 My soul followeth hard after thee: thy right hand upholdeth me.
\p
\v 9 But those \add that\add* seek my soul, to destroy \add it\add*, shall go into the lower parts of the earth.
\p
\v 10 They shall fall by the sword: they shall be a portion for foxes.\f + \fr 63:10 \fr*\fq They shall fall… \fq*\ft - Heb. They shall make him run out like water by the hands of\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 But the king shall rejoice in God; every one that sweareth by him shall glory: but the mouth of them that speak lies shall be stopped.
\c 64
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 Hear my voice, O God, in my prayer: preserve my life from fear of the enemy.
\p
\v 2 Hide me from the secret counsel of the wicked; from the insurrection of the workers of iniquity:
\p
\v 3 Who whet their tongue like a sword, \add and\add* bend \add their bows to shoot\add* their arrows, \add even\add* bitter words:
\p
\v 4 That they may shoot in secret at the perfect: suddenly do they shoot at him, and fear not.
\p
\v 5 They encourage themselves \add in\add* an evil matter: they commune of laying snares privily; they say, Who shall see them?\f + \fr 64:5 \fr*\fq matter \fq*\ft - or, speech\ft*\f*\f + \fr 64:5 \fr*\fq of… \fq*\ft - Heb. to hide his snares\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 They search out iniquities; they accomplish a diligent search: both the inward \add thought\add* of every one \add of them\add*, and the heart, \add is\add* deep.\f + \fr 64:6 \fr*\fq they… \fq*\ft - or, we are consumed by that which they have throughly searched\ft*\f*\f + \fr 64:6 \fr*\fq a diligent… \fq*\ft - Heb. a search searched\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 But God shall shoot at them \add with\add* an arrow; suddenly shall they be wounded.\f + \fr 64:7 \fr*\fq shall they… \fq*\ft - Heb. their wound shall be\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 So they shall make their own tongue to fall upon themselves: all that see them shall flee away.
\p
\v 9 And all men shall fear, and shall declare the work of God; for they shall wisely consider of his doing.
\p
\v 10 The righteous shall be glad in the \nd LORD\nd*, and shall trust in him; and all the upright in heart shall glory.
\c 65
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm \add and\add* Song of David.
\p
\v 1 Praise waiteth for thee, O God, in Sion: and unto thee shall the vow be performed.\f + \fr 65:1 \fr*\fq waiteth \fq*\ft - Heb. is silent\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 O thou that hearest prayer, unto thee shall all flesh come.
\p
\v 3 Iniquities prevail against me: \add as for\add* our transgressions, thou shalt purge them away.\f + \fr 65:3 \fr*\fq Iniquities \fq*\ft - Heb. Words, or, Matters of iniquities\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Blessed \add is the man whom\add* thou choosest, and causest to approach \add unto thee, that\add* he may dwell in thy courts: we shall be satisfied with the goodness of thy house, \add even\add* of thy holy temple.
\p
\v 5 \add By\add* terrible things in righteousness wilt thou answer us, O God of our salvation; \add who art\add* the confidence of all the ends of the earth, and of them that are afar off \add upon\add* the sea:
\p
\v 6 Which by his strength setteth fast the mountains; \add being\add* girded with power:
\p
\v 7 Which stilleth the noise of the seas, the noise of their waves, and the tumult of the people.
\p
\v 8 They also that dwell in the uttermost parts are afraid at thy tokens: thou makest the outgoings of the morning and evening to rejoice.\f + \fr 65:8 \fr*\fq rejoice \fq*\ft - or, sing\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 Thou visitest the earth, and waterest it: thou greatly enrichest it with the river of God, \add which\add* is full of water: thou preparest them corn, when thou hast so provided for it.\f + \fr 65:9 \fr*\fq and… \fq*\ft - or, after thou hadst made it to desire rain\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 Thou waterest the ridges thereof abundantly: thou settlest the furrows thereof: thou makest it soft with showers: thou blessest the springing thereof.\f + \fr 65:10 \fr*\fq settlest \fq*\ft - or, causest rain to descend into\ft*\f*\f + \fr 65:10 \fr*\fq makest… \fq*\ft - Heb. dissolvest it\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 Thou crownest the year with thy goodness; and thy paths drop fatness.\f + \fr 65:11 \fr*\fq with \fq*\ft - Heb. of\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 They drop \add upon\add* the pastures of the wilderness: and the little hills rejoice on every side.\f + \fr 65:12 \fr*\fq rejoice… \fq*\ft - Heb. are girded with joy\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 The pastures are clothed with flocks; the valleys also are covered over with corn; they shout for joy, they also sing.
\c 66
\d To the chief Musician, A Song \add or\add* Psalm.
\p
\v 1 Make a joyful noise unto God, all ye lands:\f + \fr 66:1 \fr*\fq all… \fq*\ft - Heb. all the earth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Sing forth the honour of his name: make his praise glorious.
\p
\v 3 Say unto God, How terrible \add art thou in\add* thy works! through the greatness of thy power shall thine enemies submit themselves unto thee.\f + \fr 66:3 \fr*\fq submit… \fq*\ft - or, yield feigned obedience: Heb. lie\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 All the earth shall worship thee, and shall sing unto thee; they shall sing \add to\add* thy name. Selah.
\p
\v 5 Come and see the works of God: \add he is\add* terrible \add in his\add* doing toward the children of men.
\p
\v 6 He turned the sea into dry \add land:\add* they went through the flood on foot: there did we rejoice in him.
\p
\v 7 He ruleth by his power for ever; his eyes behold the nations: let not the rebellious exalt themselves. Selah.
\p
\v 8 O bless our God, ye people, and make the voice of his praise to be heard:
\p
\v 9 Which holdeth our soul in life, and suffereth not our feet to be moved.\f + \fr 66:9 \fr*\fq holdeth \fq*\ft - Heb. putteth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 For thou, O God, hast proved us: thou hast tried us, as silver is tried.
\p
\v 11 Thou broughtest us into the net; thou laidst affliction upon our loins.
\p
\v 12 Thou hast caused men to ride over our heads; we went through fire and through water: but thou broughtest us out into a wealthy \add place\add*.\f + \fr 66:12 \fr*\fq wealthy \fq*\ft - Heb. moist\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 I will go into thy house with burnt offerings: I will pay thee my vows,
\p
\v 14 Which my lips have uttered, and my mouth hath spoken, when I was in trouble.\f + \fr 66:14 \fr*\fq uttered \fq*\ft - Heb. opened\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 I will offer unto thee burnt sacrifices of fatlings, with the incense of rams; I will offer bullocks with goats. Selah.\f + \fr 66:15 \fr*\fq fatlings \fq*\ft - Heb. marrow\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 Come \add and\add* hear, all ye that fear God, and I will declare what he hath done for my soul.
\p
\v 17 I cried unto him with my mouth, and he was extolled with my tongue.
\p
\v 18 If I regard iniquity in my heart, the Lord will not hear \add me:\add*
\p
\v 19 \add But\add* verily God hath heard \add me;\add* he hath attended to the voice of my prayer.
\p
\v 20 Blessed \add be\add* God, which hath not turned away my prayer, nor his mercy from me.
\c 67
\d To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm \add or\add* Song.
\p
\v 1 God be merciful unto us, and bless us; \add and\add* cause his face to shine upon us; Selah.\f + \fr 67:1 \fr*\fq chief… \fq*\ft - or, overseer\ft*\f*\f + \fr 67:1 \fr*\fq upon \fq*\ft - Heb. with\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 That thy way may be known upon earth, thy saving health among all nations.
\p
\v 3 Let the people praise thee, O God; let all the people praise thee.
\p
\v 4 O let the nations be glad and sing for joy: for thou shalt judge the people righteously, and govern the nations upon earth. Selah.\f + \fr 67:4 \fr*\fq govern \fq*\ft - Heb. lead\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 Let the people praise thee, O God; let all the people praise thee.
\p
\v 6 \add Then\add* shall the earth yield her increase; \add and\add* God, \add even\add* our own God, shall bless us.
\p
\v 7 God shall bless us; and all the ends of the earth shall fear him.
\c 68
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm \add or\add* Song of David.
\p
\v 1 Let God arise, let his enemies be scattered: let them also that hate him flee before him.\f + \fr 68:1 \fr*\fq before… \fq*\ft - Heb. from his face\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 As smoke is driven away, \add so\add* drive \add them\add* away: as wax melteth before the fire, \add so\add* let the wicked perish at the presence of God.
\p
\v 3 But let the righteous be glad; let them rejoice before God: yea, let them exceedingly rejoice.\f + \fr 68:3 \fr*\fq exceedingly… \fq*\ft - Heb. rejoice with gladness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Sing unto God, sing praises to his name: extol him that rideth upon the heavens by his name \nd Jah\nd*, and rejoice before him.
\p
\v 5 A father of the fatherless, and a judge of the widows, \add is\add* God in his holy habitation.
\p
\v 6 God setteth the solitary in families: he bringeth out those which are bound with chains: but the rebellious dwell in a dry \add land\add*.\f + \fr 68:6 \fr*\fq in families \fq*\ft - Heb. in a house\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 O God, when thou wentest forth before thy people, when thou didst march through the wilderness; Selah:
\p
\v 8 The earth shook, the heavens also dropped at the presence of God: \add even\add* Sinai itself \add was moved\add* at the presence of God, the God of Israel.
\p
\v 9 Thou, O God, didst send a plentiful rain, whereby thou didst confirm thine inheritance, when it was weary.\f + \fr 68:9 \fr*\fq send \fq*\ft - Heb. shake out\ft*\f*\f + \fr 68:9 \fr*\fq confirm \fq*\ft - Heb. confirm it\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 Thy congregation hath dwelt therein: thou, O God, hast prepared of thy goodness for the poor.
\p
\v 11 The Lord gave the word: great \add was\add* the company of those that published \add it\add*.\f + \fr 68:11 \fr*\fq company \fq*\ft - Heb. army\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 Kings of armies did flee apace: and she that tarried at home divided the spoil.\f + \fr 68:12 \fr*\fq did… \fq*\ft - Heb. did flee, did flee\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 Though ye have lien among the pots, \add yet shall ye be as\add* the wings of a dove covered with silver, and her feathers with yellow gold.
\p
\v 14 When the Almighty scattered kings in it, it was \add white\add* as snow in Salmon.\f + \fr 68:14 \fr*\fq in it… \fq*\ft - or, for her, she\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 The hill of God \add is as\add* the hill of Bashan; an high hill \add as\add* the hill of Bashan.
\p
\v 16 Why leap ye, ye high hills? \add this is\add* the hill \add which\add* God desireth to dwell in; yea, the \nd LORD\nd* will dwell \add in it\add* for ever.
\p
\v 17 The chariots of God \add are\add* twenty thousand, \add even\add* thousands of angels: the Lord \add is\add* among them, \add as in\add* Sinai, in the holy \add place\add*.\f + \fr 68:17 \fr*\fq even… \fq*\ft - or, even many thousands\ft*\f*
\p
\v 18 Thou hast ascended on high, thou hast led captivity captive: thou hast received gifts for men; yea, \add for\add* the rebellious also, that the \nd LORD\nd* God might dwell \add among them\add*.\f + \fr 68:18 \fr*\fq for men \fq*\ft - Heb. in the man\ft*\f*
\p
\v 19 Blessed \add be\add* the Lord, \add who\add* daily loadeth us \add with benefits, even\add* the God of our salvation. Selah.
\p
\v 20 \add He that is\add* our God \add is\add* the God of salvation; and unto \nd GOD\nd* the Lord \add belong\add* the issues from death.
\p
\v 21 But God shall wound the head of his enemies, \add and\add* the hairy scalp of such an one as goeth on still in his trespasses.
\p
\v 22 The Lord said, I will bring again from Bashan, I will bring \add my people\add* again from the depths of the sea:
\p
\v 23 That thy foot may be dipped in the blood of \add thine\add* enemies, \add and\add* the tongue of thy dogs in the same.\f + \fr 68:23 \fr*\fq dipped \fq*\ft - or, red\ft*\f*
\p
\v 24 They have seen thy goings, O God; \add even\add* the goings of my God, my King, in the sanctuary.
\p
\v 25 The singers went before, the players on instruments \add followed\add* after; among \add them were\add* the damsels playing with timbrels.
\p
\v 26 Bless ye God in the congregations, \add even\add* the Lord, from the fountain of Israel.\f + \fr 68:26 \fr*\fq from… \fq*\ft - or, ye that are of the fountain of Israel\ft*\f*
\p
\v 27 There \add is\add* little Benjamin \add with\add* their ruler, the princes of Judah \add and\add* their council, the princes of Zebulun, \add and\add* the princes of Naphtali.\f + \fr 68:27 \fr*\fq and their… \fq*\ft - or, with their company\ft*\f*
\p
\v 28 Thy God hath commanded thy strength: strengthen, O God, that which thou hast wrought for us.
\p
\v 29 Because of thy temple at Jerusalem shall kings bring presents unto thee.
\p
\v 30 Rebuke the company of spearmen, the multitude of the bulls, with the calves of the people, \add till every one\add* submit himself with pieces of silver: scatter thou the people \add that\add* delight in war.\f + \fr 68:30 \fr*\fq the company… \fq*\ft - or, the beasts of the reeds\ft*\f*\f + \fr 68:30 \fr*\fq scatter… \fq*\ft - or, he scattereth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 31 Princes shall come out of Egypt; Ethiopia shall soon stretch out her hands unto God.
\p
\v 32 Sing unto God, ye kingdoms of the earth; O sing praises unto the Lord; Selah:
\p
\v 33 To him that rideth upon the heavens of heavens, \add which were\add* of old; lo, he doth send out his voice, \add and that\add* a mighty voice.\f + \fr 68:33 \fr*\fq send… \fq*\ft - Heb. give\ft*\f*
\p
\v 34 Ascribe ye strength unto God: his excellency \add is\add* over Israel, and his strength \add is\add* in the clouds.\f + \fr 68:34 \fr*\fq clouds \fq*\ft - or, heavens\ft*\f*
\p
\v 35 O God, \add thou art\add* terrible out of thy holy places: the God of Israel \add is\add* he that giveth strength and power unto \add his\add* people. Blessed \add be\add* God.
\c 69
\d To the chief Musician upon Shoshannim, \add A Psalm\add* of David.
\p
\v 1 Save me, O God; for the waters are come in unto \add my\add* soul.
\p
\v 2 I sink in deep mire, where \add there is\add* no standing: I am come into deep waters, where the floods overflow me.\f + \fr 69:2 \fr*\fq deep mire \fq*\ft - Heb. the mire of depth\ft*\f*\f + \fr 69:2 \fr*\fq deep waters \fq*\ft - Heb. depth of waters\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 I am weary of my crying: my throat is dried: mine eyes fail while I wait for my God.
\p
\v 4 They that hate me without a cause are more than the hairs of mine head: they that would destroy me, \add being\add* mine enemies wrongfully, are mighty: then I restored \add that\add* which I took not away.
\p
\v 5 O God, thou knowest my foolishness; and my sins are not hid from thee.\f + \fr 69:5 \fr*\fq sins \fq*\ft - Heb. guiltiness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Let not them that wait on thee, O Lord \nd GOD\nd* of hosts, be ashamed for my sake: let not those that seek thee be confounded for my sake, O God of Israel.
\p
\v 7 Because for thy sake I have borne reproach; shame hath covered my face.
\p
\v 8 I am become a stranger unto my brethren, and an alien unto my mother’s children.
\p
\v 9 For the zeal of thine house hath eaten me up; and the reproaches of them that reproached thee are fallen upon me.
\p
\v 10 When I wept, \add and chastened\add* my soul with fasting, that was to my reproach.
\p
\v 11 I made sackcloth also my garment; and I became a proverb to them.
\p
\v 12 They that sit in the gate speak against me; and I \add was\add* the song of the drunkards.\f + \fr 69:12 \fr*\fq drunkards \fq*\ft - Heb. drinkers of strong drink\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 But as for me, my prayer \add is\add* unto thee, O \nd LORD\nd*, \add in\add* an acceptable time: O God, in the multitude of thy mercy hear me, in the truth of thy salvation.
\p
\v 14 Deliver me out of the mire, and let me not sink: let me be delivered from them that hate me, and out of the deep waters.
\p
\v 15 Let not the waterflood overflow me, neither let the deep swallow me up, and let not the pit shut her mouth upon me.
\p
\v 16 Hear me, O \nd LORD\nd*; for thy lovingkindness \add is\add* good: turn unto me according to the multitude of thy tender mercies.
\p
\v 17 And hide not thy face from thy servant; for I am in trouble: hear me speedily.\f + \fr 69:17 \fr*\fq hear… \fq*\ft - Heb. make haste to hear me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 18 Draw nigh unto my soul, \add and\add* redeem it: deliver me because of mine enemies.
\p
\v 19 Thou hast known my reproach, and my shame, and my dishonour: mine adversaries \add are\add* all before thee.
\p
\v 20 Reproach hath broken my heart; and I am full of heaviness: and I looked \add for some\add* to take pity, but \add there was\add* none; and for comforters, but I found none.\f + \fr 69:20 \fr*\fq to take… \fq*\ft - Heb. to lament with me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 21 They gave me also gall for my meat; and in my thirst they gave me vinegar to drink.
\p
\v 22 Let their table become a snare before them: and \add that which should have been\add* for \add their\add* welfare, \add let it become\add* a trap.
\p
\v 23 Let their eyes be darkened, that they see not; and make their loins continually to shake.
\p
\v 24 Pour out thine indignation upon them, and let thy wrathful anger take hold of them.
\p
\v 25 Let their habitation be desolate; \add and\add* let none dwell in their tents.\f + \fr 69:25 \fr*\fq their habitation \fq*\ft - Heb. their palace\ft*\f*\f + \fr 69:25 \fr*\fq let none… \fq*\ft - Heb. let there not be a dweller\ft*\f*
\p
\v 26 For they persecute \add him\add* whom thou hast smitten; and they talk to the grief of those whom thou hast wounded.\f + \fr 69:26 \fr*\fq those… \fq*\ft - Heb. thy wounded\ft*\f*
\p
\v 27 Add iniquity unto their iniquity: and let them not come into thy righteousness.\f + \fr 69:27 \fr*\fq iniquity unto… \fq*\ft - or, punishment of iniquity, etc\ft*\f*
\p
\v 28 Let them be blotted out of the book of the living, and not be written with the righteous.
\p
\v 29 But I \add am\add* poor and sorrowful: let thy salvation, O God, set me up on high.
\p
\v 30 I will praise the name of God with a song, and will magnify him with thanksgiving.
\p
\v 31 \add This\add* also shall please the \nd LORD\nd* better than an ox \add or\add* bullock that hath horns and hoofs.
\p
\v 32 The humble shall see \add this, and\add* be glad: and your heart shall live that seek God.\f + \fr 69:32 \fr*\fq humble \fq*\ft - or, meek\ft*\f*
\p
\v 33 For the \nd LORD\nd* heareth the poor, and despiseth not his prisoners.
\p
\v 34 Let the heaven and earth praise him, the seas, and every thing that moveth therein.\f + \fr 69:34 \fr*\fq moveth \fq*\ft - Heb. creepeth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 35 For God will save Zion, and will build the cities of Judah: that they may dwell there, and have it in possession.
\p
\v 36 The seed also of his servants shall inherit it: and they that love his name shall dwell therein.
\c 70
\d To the chief Musician, \add A Psalm\add* of David, to bring to remembrance.
\p
\v 1 \add Make haste\add*, O God, to deliver me; make haste to help me, O \nd LORD\nd*.\f + \fr 70:1 \fr*\fq to help… \fq*\ft - Heb. to my help\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Let them be ashamed and confounded that seek after my soul: let them be turned backward, and put to confusion, that desire my hurt.
\p
\v 3 Let them be turned back for a reward of their shame that say, Aha, aha.
\p
\v 4 Let all those that seek thee rejoice and be glad in thee: and let such as love thy salvation say continually, Let God be magnified.
\p
\v 5 But I \add am\add* poor and needy: make haste unto me, O God: thou \add art\add* my help and my deliverer; O \nd LORD\nd*, make no tarrying.
\c 71
\p
\v 1 In thee, O \nd LORD\nd*, do I put my trust: let me never be put to confusion.
\p
\v 2 Deliver me in thy righteousness, and cause me to escape: incline thine ear unto me, and save me.
\p
\v 3 Be thou my strong habitation, whereunto I may continually resort: thou hast given commandment to save me; for thou \add art\add* my rock and my fortress.\f + \fr 71:3 \fr*\fq Be… \fq*\ft - Heb. Be thou to me for a rock of habitation\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Deliver me, O my God, out of the hand of the wicked, out of the hand of the unrighteous and cruel man.
\p
\v 5 For thou \add art\add* my hope, O Lord \nd GOD\nd*: \add thou art\add* my trust from my youth.
\p
\v 6 By thee have I been holden up from the womb: thou art he that took me out of my mother’s bowels: my praise \add shall be\add* continually of thee.
\p
\v 7 I am as a wonder unto many; but thou \add art\add* my strong refuge.
\p
\v 8 Let my mouth be filled \add with\add* thy praise \add and with\add* thy honour all the day.
\p
\v 9 Cast me not off in the time of old age; forsake me not when my strength faileth.
\p
\v 10 For mine enemies speak against me; and they that lay wait for my soul take counsel together,\f + \fr 71:10 \fr*\fq lay… \fq*\ft - Heb. watch, or, observe\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 Saying, God hath forsaken him: persecute and take him; for \add there is\add* none to deliver \add him\add*.
\p
\v 12 O God, be not far from me: O my God, make haste for my help.
\p
\v 13 Let them be confounded \add and\add* consumed that are adversaries to my soul; let them be covered \add with\add* reproach and dishonour that seek my hurt.
\p
\v 14 But I will hope continually, and will yet praise thee more and more.
\p
\v 15 My mouth shall shew forth thy righteousness \add and\add* thy salvation all the day; for I know not the numbers \add thereof\add*.
\p
\v 16 I will go in the strength of the Lord \nd GOD\nd*: I will make mention of thy righteousness, \add even\add* of thine only.
\p
\v 17 O God, thou hast taught me from my youth: and hitherto have I declared thy wondrous works.
\p
\v 18 Now also when I am old and grayheaded, O God, forsake me not; until I have shewed thy strength unto \add this\add* generation, \add and\add* thy power to every one \add that\add* is to come.\f + \fr 71:18 \fr*\fq when… \fq*\ft - Heb. unto old age and gray hairs\ft*\f*\f + \fr 71:18 \fr*\fq thy strength \fq*\ft - Heb. thine arm\ft*\f*
\p
\v 19 Thy righteousness also, O God, \add is\add* very high, who hast done great things: O God, who \add is\add* like unto thee!
\p
\v 20 \add Thou\add*, which hast shewed me great and sore troubles, shalt quicken me again, and shalt bring me up again from the depths of the earth.
\p
\v 21 Thou shalt increase my greatness, and comfort me on every side.
\p
\v 22 I will also praise thee with the psaltery, \add even\add* thy truth, O my God: unto thee will I sing with the harp, O thou Holy One of Israel.\f + \fr 71:22 \fr*\fq the psaltery \fq*\ft - Heb. the instrument of psaltery\ft*\f*
\p
\v 23 My lips shall greatly rejoice when I sing unto thee; and my soul, which thou hast redeemed.
\p
\v 24 My tongue also shall talk of thy righteousness all the day long: for they are confounded, for they are brought unto shame, that seek my hurt.
\c 72
\d \add A Psalm\add* for Solomon.
\p
\v 1 Give the king thy judgments, O God, and thy righteousness unto the king’s son.\f + \fr 72:1 \fr*\fq for \fq*\ft - or, of\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 He shall judge thy people with righteousness, and thy poor with judgment.
\p
\v 3 The mountains shall bring peace to the people, and the little hills, by righteousness.
\p
\v 4 He shall judge the poor of the people, he shall save the children of the needy, and shall break in pieces the oppressor.
\p
\v 5 They shall fear thee as long as the sun and moon endure, throughout all generations.
\p
\v 6 He shall come down like rain upon the mown grass: as showers \add that\add* water the earth.
\p
\v 7 In his days shall the righteous flourish; and abundance of peace so long as the moon endureth.\f + \fr 72:7 \fr*\fq so long… \fq*\ft - Heb. till there be no moon\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 He shall have dominion also from sea to sea, and from the river unto the ends of the earth.
\p
\v 9 They that dwell in the wilderness shall bow before him; and his enemies shall lick the dust.
\p
\v 10 The kings of Tarshish and of the isles shall bring presents: the kings of Sheba and Seba shall offer gifts.
\p
\v 11 Yea, all kings shall fall down before him: all nations shall serve him.
\p
\v 12 For he shall deliver the needy when he crieth; the poor also, and \add him\add* that hath no helper.
\p
\v 13 He shall spare the poor and needy, and shall save the souls of the needy.
\p
\v 14 He shall redeem their soul from deceit and violence: and precious shall their blood be in his sight.
\p
\v 15 And he shall live, and to him shall be given of the gold of Sheba: prayer also shall be made for him continually; \add and\add* daily shall he be praised.\f + \fr 72:15 \fr*\fq shall be given \fq*\ft - Heb. one shall give\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 There shall be an handful of corn in the earth upon the top of the mountains; the fruit thereof shall shake like Lebanon: and \add they\add* of the city shall flourish like grass of the earth.
\p
\v 17 His name shall endure for ever: his name shall be continued as long as the sun: and \add men\add* shall be blessed in him: all nations shall call him blessed.\f + \fr 72:17 \fr*\fq endure \fq*\ft - Heb. be\ft*\f*\f + \fr 72:17 \fr*\fq his name shall be… \fq*\ft - Heb. shall be as a son to continue his father’s name for ever\ft*\f*
\p
\v 18 Blessed \add be\add* the \nd LORD\nd* God, the God of Israel, who only doeth wondrous things.
\p
\v 19 And blessed \add be\add* his glorious name for ever: and let the whole earth be filled \add with\add* his glory; Amen, and Amen.
\p
\v 20 The prayers of David the son of Jesse are ended.
\c 73
\d A Psalm of Asaph.
\p
\v 1 Truly God \add is\add* good to Israel, \add even\add* to such as are of a clean heart.\f + \fr 73:1 \fr*\fq of \fq*\ft - or, for\ft*\f*\f + \fr 73:1 \fr*\fq Truly \fq*\ft - or, Yet\ft*\f*\f + \fr 73:1 \fr*\fq of… \fq*\ft - Heb. clean of heart\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 But as for me, my feet were almost gone; my steps had well nigh slipped.
\p
\v 3 For I was envious at the foolish, \add when\add* I saw the prosperity of the wicked.
\p
\v 4 For \add there are\add* no bands in their death: but their strength \add is\add* firm.\f + \fr 73:4 \fr*\fq firm \fq*\ft - Heb. fat\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 They \add are\add* not in trouble \add as other\add* men; neither are they plagued like \add other\add* men.\f + \fr 73:5 \fr*\fq in… \fq*\ft - Heb. in the trouble of other men\ft*\f*\f + \fr 73:5 \fr*\fq like \fq*\ft - Heb. with\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Therefore pride compasseth them about as a chain; violence covereth them \add as\add* a garment.
\p
\v 7 Their eyes stand out with fatness: they have more than heart could wish.\f + \fr 73:7 \fr*\fq have… \fq*\ft - Heb. pass the thoughts of the heart\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 They are corrupt, and speak wickedly \add concerning\add* oppression: they speak loftily.
\p
\v 9 They set their mouth against the heavens, and their tongue walketh through the earth.
\p
\v 10 Therefore his people return hither: and waters of a full \add cup\add* are wrung out to them.
\p
\v 11 And they say, How doth God know? and is there knowledge in the most High?
\p
\v 12 Behold, these \add are\add* the ungodly, who prosper in the world; they increase \add in\add* riches.
\p
\v 13 Verily I have cleansed my heart \add in\add* vain, and washed my hands in innocency.
\p
\v 14 For all the day long have I been plagued, and chastened every morning.\f + \fr 73:14 \fr*\fq chastened \fq*\ft - Heb. my chastisement was\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 If I say, I will speak thus; behold, I should offend \add against\add* the generation of thy children.
\p
\v 16 When I thought to know this, it \add was\add* too painful for me;\f + \fr 73:16 \fr*\fq too… \fq*\ft - Heb. labour in mine eyes\ft*\f*
\p
\v 17 Until I went into the sanctuary of God; \add then\add* understood I their end.
\p
\v 18 Surely thou didst set them in slippery places: thou castedst them down into destruction.
\p
\v 19 How are they \add brought\add* into desolation, as in a moment! they are utterly consumed with terrors.
\p
\v 20 As a dream when \add one\add* awaketh; \add so\add*, O Lord, when thou awakest, thou shalt despise their image.
\p
\v 21 Thus my heart was grieved, and I was pricked in my reins.
\p
\v 22 So foolish \add was\add* I, and ignorant: I was \add as\add* a beast before thee.\f + \fr 73:22 \fr*\fq ignorant \fq*\ft - Heb. I knew not\ft*\f*\f + \fr 73:22 \fr*\fq before \fq*\ft - Heb. with\ft*\f*
\p
\v 23 Nevertheless I \add am\add* continually with thee: thou hast holden \add me\add* by my right hand.
\p
\v 24 Thou shalt guide me with thy counsel, and afterward receive me \add to\add* glory.
\p
\v 25 Whom have I in heaven \add but thee\add*? and \add there is\add* none upon earth \add that\add* I desire beside thee.
\p
\v 26 My flesh and my heart faileth: \add but\add* God \add is\add* the strength of my heart, and my portion for ever.\f + \fr 73:26 \fr*\fq strength \fq*\ft - Heb. rock\ft*\f*
\p
\v 27 For, lo, they that are far from thee shall perish: thou hast destroyed all them that go a whoring from thee.
\p
\v 28 But \add it is\add* good for me to draw near to God: I have put my trust in the Lord \nd GOD\nd*, that I may declare all thy works.
\c 74
\d Maschil of Asaph.
\p
\v 1 O God, why hast thou cast \add us\add* off for ever? \add why\add* doth thine anger smoke against the sheep of thy pasture?\f + \fr 74:1 \fr*\fq Maschil… \fq*\ft - or, A Psalm for Asaph to give instruction\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Remember thy congregation, \add which\add* thou hast purchased of old; the rod of thine inheritance, \add which\add* thou hast redeemed; this mount Zion, wherein thou hast dwelt.\f + \fr 74:2 \fr*\fq rod \fq*\ft - or, tribe\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 Lift up thy feet unto the perpetual desolations; \add even\add* all \add that\add* the enemy hath done wickedly in the sanctuary.
\p
\v 4 Thine enemies roar in the midst of thy congregations; they set up their ensigns \add for\add* signs.
\p
\v 5 \add A man\add* was famous according as he had lifted up axes upon the thick trees.
\p
\v 6 But now they break down the carved work thereof at once with axes and hammers.
\p
\v 7 They have cast fire into thy sanctuary, they have defiled \add by casting down\add* the dwelling place of thy name to the ground.\f + \fr 74:7 \fr*\fq They have cast… \fq*\ft - Heb. They have sent thy sanctuary unto the fire\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 They said in their hearts, Let us destroy them together: they have burned up all the synagogues of God in the land.\f + \fr 74:8 \fr*\fq destroy \fq*\ft - Heb. break\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 We see not our signs: \add there is\add* no more any prophet: neither \add is there\add* among us any that knoweth how long.
\p
\v 10 O God, how long shall the adversary reproach? shall the enemy blaspheme thy name for ever?
\p
\v 11 Why withdrawest thou thy hand, even thy right hand? pluck \add it\add* out of thy bosom.
\p
\v 12 For God \add is\add* my King of old, working salvation in the midst of the earth.
\p
\v 13 Thou didst divide the sea by thy strength: thou brakest the heads of the dragons in the waters.\f + \fr 74:13 \fr*\fq divide \fq*\ft - Heb. break\ft*\f*\f + \fr 74:13 \fr*\fq dragons \fq*\ft - or, whales\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 Thou brakest the heads of leviathan in pieces, \add and\add* gavest him \add to be\add* meat to the people inhabiting the wilderness.
\p
\v 15 Thou didst cleave the fountain and the flood: thou driedst up mighty rivers.\f + \fr 74:15 \fr*\fq mighty… \fq*\ft - Heb. rivers of strength\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 The day \add is\add* thine, the night also \add is\add* thine: thou hast prepared the light and the sun.
\p
\v 17 Thou hast set all the borders of the earth: thou hast made summer and winter.\f + \fr 74:17 \fr*\fq made \fq*\ft - Heb. made them\ft*\f*
\p
\v 18 Remember this, \add that\add* the enemy hath reproached, O \nd LORD\nd*, and \add that\add* the foolish people have blasphemed thy name.
\p
\v 19 O deliver not the soul of thy turtledove unto the multitude \add of the wicked:\add* forget not the congregation of thy poor for ever.
\p
\v 20 Have respect unto the covenant: for the dark places of the earth are full of the habitations of cruelty.
\p
\v 21 O let not the oppressed return ashamed: let the poor and needy praise thy name.
\p
\v 22 Arise, O God, plead thine own cause: remember how the foolish man reproacheth thee daily.
\p
\v 23 Forget not the voice of thine enemies: the tumult of those that rise up against thee increaseth continually.\f + \fr 74:23 \fr*\fq increaseth \fq*\ft - Heb. ascendeth\ft*\f*
\c 75
\d To the chief Musician, Al-taschith, A Psalm \add or\add* Song of Asaph.
\p
\v 1 Unto thee, O God, do we give thanks, \add unto thee\add* do we give thanks: for \add that\add* thy name is near thy wondrous works declare.\f + \fr 75:1 \fr*\fq Al-taschith \fq*\ft - or, Destroy not\ft*\f*\f + \fr 75:1 \fr*\fq of \fq*\ft - or, for\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 When I shall receive the congregation I will judge uprightly.\f + \fr 75:2 \fr*\fq receive… \fq*\ft - or, take a set time\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 The earth and all the inhabitants thereof are dissolved: I bear up the pillars of it. Selah.
\p
\v 4 I said unto the fools, Deal not foolishly: and to the wicked, Lift not up the horn:
\p
\v 5 Lift not up your horn on high: speak \add not with\add* a stiff neck.
\p
\v 6 For promotion \add cometh\add* neither from the east, nor from the west, nor from the south.\f + \fr 75:6 \fr*\fq south \fq*\ft - Heb. desert\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 But God \add is\add* the judge: he putteth down one, and setteth up another.
\p
\v 8 For in the hand of the \nd LORD\nd* \add there is\add* a cup, and the wine is red; it is full of mixture; and he poureth out of the same: but the dregs thereof, all the wicked of the earth shall wring \add them\add* out, \add and\add* drink \add them\add*.
\p
\v 9 But I will declare for ever; I will sing praises to the God of Jacob.
\p
\v 10 All the horns of the wicked also will I cut off; \add but\add* the horns of the righteous shall be exalted.
\c 76
\d To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm \add or\add* Song of Asaph.
\p
\v 1 In Judah \add is\add* God known: his name \add is\add* great in Israel.\f + \fr 76:1 \fr*\fq chief… \fq*\ft - or, overseer\ft*\f*\f + \fr 76:1 \fr*\fq of \fq*\ft - or, for\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 In Salem also is his tabernacle, and his dwelling place in Zion.
\p
\v 3 There brake he the arrows of the bow, the shield, and the sword, and the battle. Selah.
\p
\v 4 Thou \add art\add* more glorious \add and\add* excellent than the mountains of prey.
\p
\v 5 The stouthearted are spoiled, they have slept their sleep: and none of the men of might have found their hands.
\p
\v 6 At thy rebuke, O God of Jacob, both the chariot and horse are cast into a dead sleep.
\p
\v 7 Thou, \add even\add* thou, \add art\add* to be feared: and who may stand in thy sight when once thou art angry?
\p
\v 8 Thou didst cause judgment to be heard from heaven; the earth feared, and was still,
\p
\v 9 When God arose to judgment, to save all the meek of the earth. Selah.
\p
\v 10 Surely the wrath of man shall praise thee: the remainder of wrath shalt thou restrain.
\p
\v 11 Vow, and pay unto the \nd LORD\nd* your God: let all that be round about him bring presents unto him that ought to be feared.\f + \fr 76:11 \fr*\fq unto him… \fq*\ft - Heb. to fear\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 He shall cut off the spirit of princes: \add he is\add* terrible to the kings of the earth.
\c 77
\d To the chief Musician, to Jeduthun, A Psalm of Asaph.
\p
\v 1 I cried unto God with my voice, \add even\add* unto God with my voice; and he gave ear unto me.\f + \fr 77:1 \fr*\fq of \fq*\ft - or, for\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 In the day of my trouble I sought the Lord: my sore ran in the night, and ceased not: my soul refused to be comforted.\f + \fr 77:2 \fr*\fq sore \fq*\ft - Heb. hand\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 I remembered God, and was troubled: I complained, and my spirit was overwhelmed. Selah.
\p
\v 4 Thou holdest mine eyes waking: I am so troubled that I cannot speak.
\p
\v 5 I have considered the days of old, the years of ancient times.
\p
\v 6 I call to remembrance my song in the night: I commune with mine own heart: and my spirit made diligent search.
\p
\v 7 Will the Lord cast off for ever? and will he be favourable no more?
\p
\v 8 Is his mercy clean gone for ever? doth \add his\add* promise fail for evermore?\f + \fr 77:8 \fr*\fq for evermore \fq*\ft - Heb. to generation and generation?\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 Hath God forgotten to be gracious? hath he in anger shut up his tender mercies? Selah.
\p
\v 10 And I said, This \add is\add* my infirmity: \add but I will remember\add* the years of the right hand of the most High.
\p
\v 11 I will remember the works of the \nd LORD\nd*: surely I will remember thy wonders of old.
\p
\v 12 I will meditate also of all thy work, and talk of thy doings.
\p
\v 13 Thy way, O God, \add is\add* in the sanctuary: who \add is so\add* great a God as \add our\add* God?
\p
\v 14 Thou \add art\add* the God that doest wonders: thou hast declared thy strength among the people.
\p
\v 15 Thou hast with \add thine\add* arm redeemed thy people, the sons of Jacob and Joseph. Selah.
\p
\v 16 The waters saw thee, O God, the waters saw thee; they were afraid: the depths also were troubled.
\p
\v 17 The clouds poured out water: the skies sent out a sound: thine arrows also went abroad.\f + \fr 77:17 \fr*\fq poured… \fq*\ft - Heb. were poured forth with water\ft*\f*
\p
\v 18 The voice of thy thunder \add was\add* in the heaven: the lightnings lightened the world: the earth trembled and shook.
\p
\v 19 Thy way \add is\add* in the sea, and thy path in the great waters, and thy footsteps are not known.
\p
\v 20 Thou leddest thy people like a flock by the hand of Moses and Aaron.
\c 78
\d Maschil of Asaph.
\p
\v 1 Give ear, O my people, \add to\add* my law: incline your ears to the words of my mouth.\f + \fr 78:1 \fr*\fq Maschil… \fq*\ft - or, A Psalm for Asaph to give instruction\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 I will open my mouth in a parable: I will utter dark sayings of old:
\p
\v 3 Which we have heard and known, and our fathers have told us.
\p
\v 4 We will not hide \add them\add* from their children, shewing to the generation to come the praises of the \nd LORD\nd*, and his strength, and his wonderful works that he hath done.
\p
\v 5 For he established a testimony in Jacob, and appointed a law in Israel, which he commanded our fathers, that they should make them known to their children:
\p
\v 6 That the generation to come might know \add them, even\add* the children \add which\add* should be born; \add who\add* should arise and declare \add them\add* to their children:
\p
\v 7 That they might set their hope in God, and not forget the works of God, but keep his commandments:
\p
\v 8 And might not be as their fathers, a stubborn and rebellious generation; a generation \add that\add* set not their heart aright, and whose spirit was not stedfast with God.\f + \fr 78:8 \fr*\fq that… \fq*\ft - Heb. that prepared not their heart\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 The children of Ephraim, \add being\add* armed, \add and\add* carrying bows, turned back in the day of battle.\f + \fr 78:9 \fr*\fq carrying \fq*\ft - Heb. throwing forth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 They kept not the covenant of God, and refused to walk in his law;
\p
\v 11 And forgat his works, and his wonders that he had shewed them.
\p
\v 12 Marvellous things did he in the sight of their fathers, in the land of Egypt, \add in\add* the field of Zoan.
\p
\v 13 He divided the sea, and caused them to pass through; and he made the waters to stand as an heap.
\p
\v 14 In the daytime also he led them with a cloud, and all the night with a light of fire.
\p
\v 15 He clave the rocks in the wilderness, and gave \add them\add* drink as \add out of\add* the great depths.
\p
\v 16 He brought streams also out of the rock, and caused waters to run down like rivers.
\p
\v 17 And they sinned yet more against him by provoking the most High in the wilderness.
\p
\v 18 And they tempted God in their heart by asking meat for their lust.
\p
\v 19 Yea, they spake against God; they said, Can God furnish a table in the wilderness?\f + \fr 78:19 \fr*\fq furnish \fq*\ft - Heb. order\ft*\f*
\p
\v 20 Behold, he smote the rock, that the waters gushed out, and the streams overflowed; can he give bread also? can he provide flesh for his people?
\p
\v 21 Therefore the \nd LORD\nd* heard \add this\add*, and was wroth: so a fire was kindled against Jacob, and anger also came up against Israel;
\p
\v 22 Because they believed not in God, and trusted not in his salvation:
\p
\v 23 Though he had commanded the clouds from above, and opened the doors of heaven,
\p
\v 24 And had rained down manna upon them to eat, and had given them of the corn of heaven.
\p
\v 25 Man did eat angels’ food: he sent them meat to the full.\f + \fr 78:25 \fr*\fq Man… \fq*\ft - or, Every one did eat the bread of the mighty\ft*\f*
\p
\v 26 He caused an east wind to blow in the heaven: and by his power he brought in the south wind.\f + \fr 78:26 \fr*\fq to blow \fq*\ft - Heb. to go\ft*\f*
\p
\v 27 He rained flesh also upon them as dust, and feathered fowls like as the sand of the sea:\f + \fr 78:27 \fr*\fq feathered… \fq*\ft - Heb. fowl of wing\ft*\f*
\p
\v 28 And he let \add it\add* fall in the midst of their camp, round about their habitations.
\p
\v 29 So they did eat, and were well filled: for he gave them their own desire;
\p
\v 30 They were not estranged from their lust. But while their meat \add was\add* yet in their mouths,
\p
\v 31 The wrath of God came upon them, and slew the fattest of them, and smote down the chosen \add men\add* of Israel.\f + \fr 78:31 \fr*\fq smote… \fq*\ft - Heb. made to bow\ft*\f*\f + \fr 78:31 \fr*\fq chosen… \fq*\ft - or, young men\ft*\f*
\p
\v 32 For all this they sinned still, and believed not for his wondrous works.
\p
\v 33 Therefore their days did he consume in vanity, and their years in trouble.
\p
\v 34 When he slew them, then they sought him: and they returned and enquired early after God.
\p
\v 35 And they remembered that God \add was\add* their rock, and the high God their redeemer.
\p
\v 36 Nevertheless they did flatter him with their mouth, and they lied unto him with their tongues.
\p
\v 37 For their heart was not right with him, neither were they stedfast in his covenant.
\p
\v 38 But he, \add being\add* full of compassion, forgave \add their\add* iniquity, and destroyed \add them\add* not: yea, many a time turned he his anger away, and did not stir up all his wrath.
\p
\v 39 For he remembered that they \add were but\add* flesh; a wind that passeth away, and cometh not again.
\p
\v 40 How oft did they provoke him in the wilderness, \add and\add* grieve him in the desert!\f + \fr 78:40 \fr*\fq provoke \fq*\ft - or, rebel against\ft*\f*
\p
\v 41 Yea, they turned back and tempted God, and limited the Holy One of Israel.
\p
\v 42 They remembered not his hand, \add nor\add* the day when he delivered them from the enemy.\f + \fr 78:42 \fr*\fq from… \fq*\ft - or, from affliction\ft*\f*
\p
\v 43 How he had wrought his signs in Egypt, and his wonders in the field of Zoan:\f + \fr 78:43 \fr*\fq wrought \fq*\ft - Heb. set\ft*\f*
\p
\v 44 And had turned their rivers into blood; and their floods, that they could not drink.
\p
\v 45 He sent divers sorts of flies among them, which devoured them; and frogs, which destroyed them.
\p
\v 46 He gave also their increase unto the caterpiller, and their labour unto the locust.
\p
\v 47 He destroyed their vines with hail, and their sycomore trees with frost.\f + \fr 78:47 \fr*\fq destroyed \fq*\ft - Heb. killed\ft*\f*\f + \fr 78:47 \fr*\fq frost \fq*\ft - or, great hailstones\ft*\f*
\p
\v 48 He gave up their cattle also to the hail, and their flocks to hot thunderbolts.\f + \fr 78:48 \fr*\fq gave… \fq*\ft - Heb. shut up\ft*\f*\f + \fr 78:48 \fr*\fq hot… \fq*\ft - or, lightnings\ft*\f*
\p
\v 49 He cast upon them the fierceness of his anger, wrath, and indignation, and trouble, by sending evil angels \add among them\add*.
\p
\v 50 He made a way to his anger; he spared not their soul from death, but gave their life over to the pestilence;\f + \fr 78:50 \fr*\fq He made… \fq*\ft - Heb. He weighed a path\ft*\f*\f + \fr 78:50 \fr*\fq life… \fq*\ft - or, beasts to the murrain\ft*\f*
\p
\v 51 And smote all the firstborn in Egypt; the chief of \add their\add* strength in the tabernacles of Ham:
\p
\v 52 But made his own people to go forth like sheep, and guided them in the wilderness like a flock.
\p
\v 53 And he led them on safely, so that they feared not: but the sea overwhelmed their enemies.\f + \fr 78:53 \fr*\fq overwhelmed \fq*\ft - Heb. covered\ft*\f*
\p
\v 54 And he brought them to the border of his sanctuary, \add even to\add* this mountain, \add which\add* his right hand had purchased.
\p
\v 55 He cast out the heathen also before them, and divided them an inheritance by line, and made the tribes of Israel to dwell in their tents.
\p
\v 56 Yet they tempted and provoked the most high God, and kept not his testimonies:
\p
\v 57 But turned back, and dealt unfaithfully like their fathers: they were turned aside like a deceitful bow.
\p
\v 58 For they provoked him to anger with their high places, and moved him to jealousy with their graven images.
\p
\v 59 When God heard \add this\add*, he was wroth, and greatly abhorred Israel:
\p
\v 60 So that he forsook the tabernacle of Shiloh, the tent \add which\add* he placed among men;
\p
\v 61 And delivered his strength into captivity, and his glory into the enemy’s hand.
\p
\v 62 He gave his people over also unto the sword; and was wroth with his inheritance.
\p
\v 63 The fire consumed their young men; and their maidens were not given to marriage.\f + \fr 78:63 \fr*\fq given… \fq*\ft - Heb. praised\ft*\f*
\p
\v 64 Their priests fell by the sword; and their widows made no lamentation.
\p
\v 65 Then the Lord awaked as one out of sleep, \add and\add* like a mighty man that shouteth by reason of wine.
\p
\v 66 And he smote his enemies in the hinder parts: he put them to a perpetual reproach.
\p
\v 67 Moreover he refused the tabernacle of Joseph, and chose not the tribe of Ephraim:
\p
\v 68 But chose the tribe of Judah, the mount Zion which he loved.
\p
\v 69 And he built his sanctuary like high \add palaces\add*, like the earth which he hath established for ever.\f + \fr 78:69 \fr*\fq established \fq*\ft - Heb. founded\ft*\f*
\p
\v 70 He chose David also his servant, and took him from the sheepfolds:
\p
\v 71 From following the ewes great with young he brought him to feed Jacob his people, and Israel his inheritance.\f + \fr 78:71 \fr*\fq following \fq*\ft - Heb. after\ft*\f*
\p
\v 72 So he fed them according to the integrity of his heart; and guided them by the skilfulness of his hands.
\c 79
\d A Psalm of Asaph.
\p
\v 1 O God, the heathen are come into thine inheritance; thy holy temple have they defiled; they have laid Jerusalem on heaps.\f + \fr 79:1 \fr*\fq of \fq*\ft - or, for\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 The dead bodies of thy servants have they given \add to be\add* meat unto the fowls of the heaven, the flesh of thy saints unto the beasts of the earth.
\p
\v 3 Their blood have they shed like water round about Jerusalem; and \add there was\add* none to bury \add them\add*.
\p
\v 4 We are become a reproach to our neighbours, a scorn and derision to them that are round about us.
\p
\v 5 How long, \nd LORD\nd*? wilt thou be angry for ever? shall thy jealousy burn like fire?
\p
\v 6 Pour out thy wrath upon the heathen that have not known thee, and upon the kingdoms that have not called upon thy name.
\p
\v 7 For they have devoured Jacob, and laid waste his dwelling place.
\p
\v 8 O remember not against us former iniquities: let thy tender mercies speedily prevent us: for we are brought very low.\f + \fr 79:8 \fr*\fq former… \fq*\ft - or, the iniquities of them that were before us\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 Help us, O God of our salvation, for the glory of thy name: and deliver us, and purge away our sins, for thy name’s sake.
\p
\v 10 Wherefore should the heathen say, Where \add is\add* their God? let him be known among the heathen in our sight \add by\add* the revenging of the blood of thy servants \add which is\add* shed.\f + \fr 79:10 \fr*\fq revenging \fq*\ft - Heb. vengeance\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 Let the sighing of the prisoner come before thee; according to the greatness of thy power preserve thou those that are appointed to die;\f + \fr 79:11 \fr*\fq thy… \fq*\ft - Heb. thine arm\ft*\f*\f + \fr 79:11 \fr*\fq preserve… \fq*\ft - Heb. reserve the children of death\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 And render unto our neighbours sevenfold into their bosom their reproach, wherewith they have reproached thee, O Lord.
\p
\v 13 So we thy people and sheep of thy pasture will give thee thanks for ever: we will shew forth thy praise to all generations.\f + \fr 79:13 \fr*\fq to all… \fq*\ft - Heb. to generation and generation\ft*\f*
\c 80
\d To the chief Musician upon Shoshannim-eduth, A Psalm of Asaph.
\p
\v 1 Give ear, O Shepherd of Israel, thou that leadest Joseph like a flock; thou that dwellest \add between\add* the cherubims, shine forth.\f + \fr 80:1 \fr*\fq of \fq*\ft - or, for\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Before Ephraim and Benjamin and Manasseh stir up thy strength, and come \add and\add* save us.\f + \fr 80:2 \fr*\fq come… \fq*\ft - Heb. come for salvation to us\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 Turn us again, O God, and cause thy face to shine; and we shall be saved.
\p
\v 4 O \nd LORD\nd* God of hosts, how long wilt thou be angry against the prayer of thy people?\f + \fr 80:4 \fr*\fq be… \fq*\ft - Heb. smoke\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 Thou feedest them with the bread of tears; and givest them tears to drink in great measure.
\p
\v 6 Thou makest us a strife unto our neighbours: and our enemies laugh among themselves.
\p
\v 7 Turn us again, O God of hosts, and cause thy face to shine; and we shall be saved.
\p
\v 8 Thou hast brought a vine out of Egypt: thou hast cast out the heathen, and planted it.
\p
\v 9 Thou preparedst \add room\add* before it, and didst cause it to take deep root, and it filled the land.
\p
\v 10 The hills were covered with the shadow of it, and the boughs thereof \add were like\add* the goodly cedars.\f + \fr 80:10 \fr*\fq goodly… \fq*\ft - Heb. cedars of God\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 She sent out her boughs unto the sea, and her branches unto the river.
\p
\v 12 Why hast thou \add then\add* broken down her hedges, so that all they which pass by the way do pluck her?
\p
\v 13 The boar out of the wood doth waste it, and the wild beast of the field doth devour it.
\p
\v 14 Return, we beseech thee, O God of hosts: look down from heaven, and behold, and visit this vine;
\p
\v 15 And the vineyard which thy right hand hath planted, and the branch \add that\add* thou madest strong for thyself.
\p
\v 16 \add It is\add* burned with fire, \add it is\add* cut down: they perish at the rebuke of thy countenance.
\p
\v 17 Let thy hand be upon the man of thy right hand, upon the son of man \add whom\add* thou madest strong for thyself.
\p
\v 18 So will not we go back from thee: quicken us, and we will call upon thy name.
\p
\v 19 Turn us again, O \nd LORD\nd* God of hosts, cause thy face to shine; and we shall be saved.
\c 81
\d To the chief Musician upon Gittith, \add A Psalm\add* of Asaph.
\p
\v 1 Sing aloud unto God our strength: make a joyful noise unto the God of Jacob.\f + \fr 81:1 \fr*\fq of Asaph \fq*\ft - or, for Asaph\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Take a psalm, and bring hither the timbrel, the pleasant harp with the psaltery.
\p
\v 3 Blow up the trumpet in the new moon, in the time appointed, on our solemn feast day.
\p
\v 4 For this \add was\add* a statute for Israel, \add and\add* a law of the God of Jacob.
\p
\v 5 This he ordained in Joseph \add for\add* a testimony, when he went out through the land of Egypt: \add where\add* I heard a language \add that\add* I understood not.\f + \fr 81:5 \fr*\fq through \fq*\ft - or, against\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 I removed his shoulder from the burden: his hands were delivered from the pots.\f + \fr 81:6 \fr*\fq were… \fq*\ft - Heb. passed away\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 Thou calledst in trouble, and I delivered thee; I answered thee in the secret place of thunder: I proved thee at the waters of Meribah. Selah.\f + \fr 81:7 \fr*\fq Meribah \fq*\ft - or, Strife\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 Hear, O my people, and I will testify unto thee: O Israel, if thou wilt hearken unto me;
\p
\v 9 There shall no strange god be in thee; neither shalt thou worship any strange god.
\p
\v 10 I \add am\add* the \nd LORD\nd* thy God, which brought thee out of the land of Egypt: open thy mouth wide, and I will fill it.
\p
\v 11 But my people would not hearken to my voice; and Israel would none of me.
\p
\v 12 So I gave them up unto their own hearts’ lust: \add and\add* they walked in their own counsels.\f + \fr 81:12 \fr*\fq unto… \fq*\ft - or, to the hardness of their hearts, or, imagination\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 Oh that my people had hearkened unto me, \add and\add* Israel had walked in my ways!
\p
\v 14 I should soon have subdued their enemies, and turned my hand against their adversaries.
\p
\v 15 The haters of the \nd LORD\nd* should have submitted themselves unto him: but their time should have endured for ever.\f + \fr 81:15 \fr*\fq submitted… \fq*\ft - or, yielded feigned obedience: Heb. lied\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 He should have fed them also with the finest of the wheat: and with honey out of the rock should I have satisfied thee.\f + \fr 81:16 \fr*\fq finest… \fq*\ft - Heb. fat of wheat\ft*\f*
\c 82
\d A Psalm of Asaph.
\p
\v 1 God standeth in the congregation of the mighty; he judgeth among the gods.\f + \fr 82:1 \fr*\fq of Asaph \fq*\ft - or, for Asaph\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 How long will ye judge unjustly, and accept the persons of the wicked? Selah.
\p
\v 3 Defend the poor and fatherless: do justice to the afflicted and needy.\f + \fr 82:3 \fr*\fq Defend \fq*\ft - Heb. Judge\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Deliver the poor and needy: rid \add them\add* out of the hand of the wicked.
\p
\v 5 They know not, neither will they understand; they walk on in darkness: all the foundations of the earth are out of course.\f + \fr 82:5 \fr*\fq out… \fq*\ft - Heb. moved\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 I have said, Ye \add are\add* gods; and all of you \add are\add* children of the most High.
\p
\v 7 But ye shall die like men, and fall like one of the princes.
\p
\v 8 Arise, O God, judge the earth: for thou shalt inherit all nations.
\c 83
\d A Song \add or\add* Psalm of Asaph.
\p
\v 1 Keep not thou silence, O God: hold not thy peace, and be not still, O God.\f + \fr 83:1 \fr*\fq of Asaph \fq*\ft - or, for Asaph\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 For, lo, thine enemies make a tumult: and they that hate thee have lifted up the head.
\p
\v 3 They have taken crafty counsel against thy people, and consulted against thy hidden ones.
\p
\v 4 They have said, Come, and let us cut them off from \add being\add* a nation; that the name of Israel may be no more in remembrance.
\p
\v 5 For they have consulted together with one consent: they are confederate against thee:\f + \fr 83:5 \fr*\fq consent \fq*\ft - Heb. heart\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 The tabernacles of Edom, and the Ishmaelites; of Moab, and the Hagarenes;
\p
\v 7 Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalek; the Philistines with the inhabitants of Tyre;
\p
\v 8 Assur also is joined with them: they have holpen the children of Lot. Selah.\f + \fr 83:8 \fr*\fq holpen \fq*\ft - Heb. been an arm to\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 Do unto them as \add unto\add* the Midianites; as \add to\add* Sisera, as \add to\add* Jabin, at the brook of Kison:
\p
\v 10 \add Which\add* perished at Endor: they became \add as\add* dung for the earth.
\p
\v 11 Make their nobles like Oreb, and like Zeeb: yea, all their princes as Zebah, and as Zalmunna:
\p
\v 12 Who said, Let us take to ourselves the houses of God in possession.
\p
\v 13 O my God, make them like a wheel; as the stubble before the wind.
\p
\v 14 As the fire burneth a wood, and as the flame setteth the mountains on fire;
\p
\v 15 So persecute them with thy tempest, and make them afraid with thy storm.
\p
\v 16 Fill their faces with shame; that they may seek thy name, O \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 17 Let them be confounded and troubled for ever; yea, let them be put to shame, and perish:
\p
\v 18 That \add men\add* may know that thou, whose name alone \add is\add* \nd JEHOVAH\nd*, \add art\add* the most high over all the earth.
\c 84
\d To the chief Musician upon Gittith, A Psalm for the sons of Korah.
\p
\v 1 How amiable \add are\add* thy tabernacles, O \nd LORD\nd* of hosts!\f + \fr 84:1 \fr*\fq for the sons \fq*\ft - or, of the sons\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 My soul longeth, yea, even fainteth for the courts of the \nd LORD\nd*: my heart and my flesh crieth out for the living God.
\p
\v 3 Yea, the sparrow hath found an house, and the swallow a nest for herself, where she may lay her young, \add even\add* thine altars, O \nd LORD\nd* of hosts, my King, and my God.
\p
\v 4 Blessed \add are\add* they that dwell in thy house: they will be still praising thee. Selah.
\p
\v 5 Blessed \add is\add* the man whose strength \add is\add* in thee; in whose heart \add are\add* the ways \add of them\add*.
\p
\v 6 \add Who\add* passing through the valley of Baca make it a well; the rain also filleth the pools.\f + \fr 84:6 \fr*\fq Baca… \fq*\ft - or, mulberry trees make him a well, etc\ft*\f*\f + \fr 84:6 \fr*\fq filleth \fq*\ft - Heb. covereth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 They go from strength to strength, \add every one of them\add* in Zion appeareth before God.\f + \fr 84:7 \fr*\fq strength to… \fq*\ft - or, company to company\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 O \nd LORD\nd* God of hosts, hear my prayer: give ear, O God of Jacob. Selah.
\p
\v 9 Behold, O God our shield, and look upon the face of thine anointed.
\p
\v 10 For a day in thy courts \add is\add* better than a thousand. I had rather be a doorkeeper in the house of my God, than to dwell in the tents of wickedness.\f + \fr 84:10 \fr*\fq I had… \fq*\ft - Heb. I would choose rather to sit at the threshold\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 For the \nd LORD\nd* God \add is\add* a sun and shield: the \nd LORD\nd* will give grace and glory: no good \add thing\add* will he withhold from them that walk uprightly.
\p
\v 12 O \nd LORD\nd* of hosts, blessed \add is\add* the man that trusteth in thee.
\c 85
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm for the sons of Korah.
\p
\v 1 \nd LORD\nd*, thou hast been favourable unto thy land: thou hast brought back the captivity of Jacob.\f + \fr 85:1 \fr*\fq for the sons \fq*\ft - or, of the sons\ft*\f*\f + \fr 85:1 \fr*\fq favourable \fq*\ft - or, well pleased\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Thou hast forgiven the iniquity of thy people, thou hast covered all their sin. Selah.
\p
\v 3 Thou hast taken away all thy wrath: thou hast turned \add thyself\add* from the fierceness of thine anger.\f + \fr 85:3 \fr*\fq thyself… \fq*\ft - or, thine anger from waxing hot\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Turn us, O God of our salvation, and cause thine anger toward us to cease.
\p
\v 5 Wilt thou be angry with us for ever? wilt thou draw out thine anger to all generations?
\p
\v 6 Wilt thou not revive us again: that thy people may rejoice in thee?
\p
\v 7 Shew us thy mercy, O \nd LORD\nd*, and grant us thy salvation.
\p
\v 8 I will hear what God the \nd LORD\nd* will speak: for he will speak peace unto his people, and to his saints: but let them not turn again to folly.
\p
\v 9 Surely his salvation \add is\add* nigh them that fear him; that glory may dwell in our land.
\p
\v 10 Mercy and truth are met together; righteousness and peace have kissed \add each other\add*.
\p
\v 11 Truth shall spring out of the earth; and righteousness shall look down from heaven.
\p
\v 12 Yea, the \nd LORD\nd* shall give \add that which is\add* good; and our land shall yield her increase.
\p
\v 13 Righteousness shall go before him; and shall set \add us\add* in the way of his steps.
\c 86
\d A Prayer of David.
\p
\v 1 Bow down thine ear, O \nd LORD\nd*, hear me: for I \add am\add* poor and needy.\f + \fr 86:1 \fr*\fq A Prayer… \fq*\ft - or, A Prayer, being a Psalm of David\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Preserve my soul; for I \add am\add* holy: O thou my God, save thy servant that trusteth in thee.\f + \fr 86:2 \fr*\fq holy \fq*\ft - or, one whom thou favourest\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 Be merciful unto me, O Lord: for I cry unto thee daily.\f + \fr 86:3 \fr*\fq daily \fq*\ft - or, all the day\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Rejoice the soul of thy servant: for unto thee, O Lord, do I lift up my soul.
\p
\v 5 For thou, Lord, \add art\add* good, and ready to forgive; and plenteous in mercy unto all them that call upon thee.
\p
\v 6 Give ear, O \nd LORD\nd*, unto my prayer; and attend to the voice of my supplications.
\p
\v 7 In the day of my trouble I will call upon thee: for thou wilt answer me.
\p
\v 8 Among the gods \add there is\add* none like unto thee, O Lord; neither \add are there any works\add* like unto thy works.
\p
\v 9 All nations whom thou hast made shall come and worship before thee, O Lord; and shall glorify thy name.
\p
\v 10 For thou \add art\add* great, and doest wondrous things: thou \add art\add* God alone.
\p
\v 11 Teach me thy way, O \nd LORD\nd*; I will walk in thy truth: unite my heart to fear thy name.
\p
\v 12 I will praise thee, O Lord my God, with all my heart: and I will glorify thy name for evermore.
\p
\v 13 For great \add is\add* thy mercy toward me: and thou hast delivered my soul from the lowest hell.\f + \fr 86:13 \fr*\fq hell \fq*\ft - or, grave\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 O God, the proud are risen against me, and the assemblies of violent \add men\add* have sought after my soul; and have not set thee before them.\f + \fr 86:14 \fr*\fq violent \fq*\ft - Heb. terrible\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 But thou, O Lord, \add art\add* a God full of compassion, and gracious, longsuffering, and plenteous in mercy and truth.
\p
\v 16 O turn unto me, and have mercy upon me; give thy strength unto thy servant, and save the son of thine handmaid.
\p
\v 17 Shew me a token for good; that they which hate me may see \add it\add*, and be ashamed: because thou, \nd LORD\nd*, hast holpen me, and comforted me.
\c 87
\d A Psalm \add or\add* Song for the sons of Korah.
\p
\v 1 His foundation \add is\add* in the holy mountains.\f + \fr 87:1 \fr*\fq for the sons \fq*\ft - or, of the sons\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 The \nd LORD\nd* loveth the gates of Zion more than all the dwellings of Jacob.
\p
\v 3 Glorious things are spoken of thee, O city of God. Selah.
\p
\v 4 I will make mention of Rahab and Babylon to them that know me: behold Philistia, and Tyre, with Ethiopia; this \add man\add* was born there.
\p
\v 5 And of Zion it shall be said, This and that man was born in her: and the highest himself shall establish her.
\p
\v 6 The \nd LORD\nd* shall count, when he writeth up the people, \add that\add* this \add man\add* was born there. Selah.
\p
\v 7 As well the singers as the players on instruments \add shall be there:\add* all my springs \add are\add* in thee.
\c 88
\d A Song \add or\add* Psalm for the sons of Korah, to the chief Musician upon Mahalath Leannoth, Maschil of Heman the Ezrahite.
\p
\v 1 O \nd LORD\nd* God of my salvation, I have cried day \add and\add* night before thee:\f + \fr 88:1 \fr*\fq for the sons \fq*\ft - or, of the sons\ft*\f*\f + \fr 88:1 \fr*\fq Maschil… \fq*\ft - or, A Psalm of Heman the Ezrahite, giving instruction\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Let my prayer come before thee: incline thine ear unto my cry;
\p
\v 3 For my soul is full of troubles: and my life draweth nigh unto the grave.
\p
\v 4 I am counted with them that go down into the pit: I am as a man \add that hath\add* no strength:
\p
\v 5 Free among the dead, like the slain that lie in the grave, whom thou rememberest no more: and they are cut off from thy hand.\f + \fr 88:5 \fr*\fq from \fq*\ft - or, by\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Thou hast laid me in the lowest pit, in darkness, in the deeps.
\p
\v 7 Thy wrath lieth hard upon me, and thou hast afflicted \add me\add* with all thy waves. Selah.
\p
\v 8 Thou hast put away mine acquaintance far from me; thou hast made me an abomination unto them: \add I am\add* shut up, and I cannot come forth.
\p
\v 9 Mine eye mourneth by reason of affliction: \nd LORD\nd*, I have called daily upon thee, I have stretched out my hands unto thee.
\p
\v 10 Wilt thou shew wonders to the dead? shall the dead arise \add and\add* praise thee? Selah.
\p
\v 11 Shall thy lovingkindness be declared in the grave? \add or\add* thy faithfulness in destruction?
\p
\v 12 Shall thy wonders be known in the dark? and thy righteousness in the land of forgetfulness?
\p
\v 13 But unto thee have I cried, O \nd LORD\nd*; and in the morning shall my prayer prevent thee.
\p
\v 14 \nd LORD\nd*, why castest thou off my soul? \add why\add* hidest thou thy face from me?
\p
\v 15 I \add am\add* afflicted and ready to die from \add my\add* youth up: \add while\add* I suffer thy terrors I am distracted.
\p
\v 16 Thy fierce wrath goeth over me; thy terrors have cut me off.
\p
\v 17 They came round about me daily like water; they compassed me about together.\f + \fr 88:17 \fr*\fq daily \fq*\ft - or, all the day\ft*\f*
\p
\v 18 Lover and friend hast thou put far from me, \add and\add* mine acquaintance into darkness.
\c 89
\d Maschil of Ethan the Ezrahite.
\p
\v 1 I will sing of the mercies of the \nd LORD\nd* for ever: with my mouth will I make known thy faithfulness to all generations.\f + \fr 89:1 \fr*\fq Maschil… \fq*\ft - or, A Psalm for Ethan the Ezrahite, to give instruction\ft*\f*\f + \fr 89:1 \fr*\fq to all… \fq*\ft - Heb. to generation and generation\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 For I have said, Mercy shall be built up for ever: thy faithfulness shalt thou establish in the very heavens.
\p
\v 3 I have made a covenant with my chosen, I have sworn unto David my servant,
\p
\v 4 Thy seed will I establish for ever, and build up thy throne to all generations. Selah.
\p
\v 5 And the heavens shall praise thy wonders, O \nd LORD\nd*: thy faithfulness also in the congregation of the saints.
\p
\v 6 For who in the heaven can be compared unto the \nd LORD\nd*? \add who\add* among the sons of the mighty can be likened unto the \nd LORD\nd*?
\p
\v 7 God is greatly to be feared in the assembly of the saints, and to be had in reverence of all \add them that are\add* about him.
\p
\v 8 O \nd LORD\nd* God of hosts, who \add is\add* a strong \nd LORD\nd* like unto thee? or to thy faithfulness round about thee?
\p
\v 9 Thou rulest the raging of the sea: when the waves thereof arise, thou stillest them.
\p
\v 10 Thou hast broken Rahab in pieces, as one that is slain; thou hast scattered thine enemies with thy strong arm.\f + \fr 89:10 \fr*\fq Rahab \fq*\ft - or, Egypt\ft*\f*\f + \fr 89:10 \fr*\fq thy… \fq*\ft - Heb. the arm of thy strength\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 The heavens \add are\add* thine, the earth also \add is\add* thine: \add as for\add* the world and the fulness thereof, thou hast founded them.\f + \fr 89:11 \fr*\fq the fulness… \fq*\ft - or, all it containeth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 The north and the south thou hast created them: Tabor and Hermon shall rejoice in thy name.
\p
\v 13 Thou hast a mighty arm: strong is thy hand, \add and\add* high is thy right hand.\f + \fr 89:13 \fr*\fq a… \fq*\ft - Heb. an arm with might\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 Justice and judgment \add are\add* the habitation of thy throne: mercy and truth shall go before thy face.\f + \fr 89:14 \fr*\fq habitation \fq*\ft - or, establishment\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 Blessed \add is\add* the people that know the joyful sound: they shall walk, O \nd LORD\nd*, in the light of thy countenance.
\p
\v 16 In thy name shall they rejoice all the day: and in thy righteousness shall they be exalted.
\p
\v 17 For thou \add art\add* the glory of their strength: and in thy favour our horn shall be exalted.
\p
\v 18 For the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* our defence; and the Holy One of Israel \add is\add* our king.\f + \fr 89:18 \fr*\ft the\ft*\f*
\p
\v 19 Then thou spakest in vision to thy holy one, and saidst, I have laid help upon \add one that is\add* mighty; I have exalted \add one\add* chosen out of the people.
\p
\v 20 I have found David my servant; with my holy oil have I anointed him:
\p
\v 21 With whom my hand shall be established: mine arm also shall strengthen him.
\p
\v 22 The enemy shall not exact upon him; nor the son of wickedness afflict him.
\p
\v 23 And I will beat down his foes before his face, and plague them that hate him.
\p
\v 24 But my faithfulness and my mercy \add shall be\add* with him: and in my name shall his horn be exalted.
\p
\v 25 I will set his hand also in the sea, and his right hand in the rivers.
\p
\v 26 He shall cry unto me, Thou \add art\add* my father, my God, and the rock of my salvation.
\p
\v 27 Also I will make him \add my\add* firstborn, higher than the kings of the earth.
\p
\v 28 My mercy will I keep for him for evermore, and my covenant shall stand fast with him.
\p
\v 29 His seed also will I make \add to endure\add* for ever, and his throne as the days of heaven.
\p
\v 30 If his children forsake my law, and walk not in my judgments;
\p
\v 31 If they break my statutes, and keep not my commandments;\f + \fr 89:31 \fr*\fq break \fq*\ft - Heb. profane\ft*\f*
\p
\v 32 Then will I visit their transgression with the rod, and their iniquity with stripes.
\p
\v 33 Nevertheless my lovingkindness will I not utterly take from him, nor suffer my faithfulness to fail.\f + \fr 89:33 \fr*\fq will… \fq*\ft - Heb. I will not make void from him\ft*\f*\f + \fr 89:33 \fr*\fq to fail \fq*\ft - Heb. to lie\ft*\f*
\p
\v 34 My covenant will I not break, nor alter the thing that is gone out of my lips.
\p
\v 35 Once have I sworn by my holiness that I will not lie unto David.\f + \fr 89:35 \fr*\fq that… \fq*\ft - Heb. if I lie\ft*\f*
\p
\v 36 His seed shall endure for ever, and his throne as the sun before me.
\p
\v 37 It shall be established for ever as the moon, and \add as\add* a faithful witness in heaven. Selah.
\p
\v 38 But thou hast cast off and abhorred, thou hast been wroth with thine anointed.
\p
\v 39 Thou hast made void the covenant of thy servant: thou hast profaned his crown \add by casting it\add* to the ground.
\p
\v 40 Thou hast broken down all his hedges; thou hast brought his strong holds to ruin.
\p
\v 41 All that pass by the way spoil him: he is a reproach to his neighbours.
\p
\v 42 Thou hast set up the right hand of his adversaries; thou hast made all his enemies to rejoice.
\p
\v 43 Thou hast also turned the edge of his sword, and hast not made him to stand in the battle.
\p
\v 44 Thou hast made his glory to cease, and cast his throne down to the ground.\f + \fr 89:44 \fr*\fq glory \fq*\ft - Heb. brightness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 45 The days of his youth hast thou shortened: thou hast covered him with shame. Selah.
\p
\v 46 How long, \nd LORD\nd*? wilt thou hide thyself for ever? shall thy wrath burn like fire?
\p
\v 47 Remember how short my time is: wherefore hast thou made all men in vain?
\p
\v 48 What man \add is he that\add* liveth, and shall not see death? shall he deliver his soul from the hand of the grave? Selah.
\p
\v 49 Lord, where \add are\add* thy former lovingkindnesses, \add which\add* thou swarest unto David in thy truth?
\p
\v 50 Remember, Lord, the reproach of thy servants; \add how\add* I do bear in my bosom \add the reproach of\add* all the mighty people;
\p
\v 51 Wherewith thine enemies have reproached, O \nd LORD\nd*; wherewith they have reproached the footsteps of thine anointed.
\p
\v 52 Blessed \add be\add* the \nd LORD\nd* for evermore. Amen, and Amen.
\c 90
\d A Prayer of Moses the man of God.
\p
\v 1 Lord, thou hast been our dwelling place in all generations.\f + \fr 90:1 \fr*\fq A Prayer… \fq*\ft - or, A Prayer, being a Psalm of Moses\ft*\f*\f + \fr 90:1 \fr*\fq in… \fq*\ft - Heb. in generation and generation\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Before the mountains were brought forth, or ever thou hadst formed the earth and the world, even from everlasting to everlasting, thou \add art\add* God.
\p
\v 3 Thou turnest man to destruction; and sayest, Return, ye children of men.
\p
\v 4 For a thousand years in thy sight \add are but\add* as yesterday when it is past, and \add as\add* a watch in the night.\f + \fr 90:4 \fr*\fq when… \fq*\ft - or, when he hath passed them\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 Thou carriest them away as with a flood; they are \add as\add* a sleep: in the morning \add they are\add* like grass \add which\add* groweth up.\f + \fr 90:5 \fr*\fq groweth… \fq*\ft - or, is changed\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 In the morning it flourisheth, and groweth up; in the evening it is cut down, and withereth.
\p
\v 7 For we are consumed by thine anger, and by thy wrath are we troubled.
\p
\v 8 Thou hast set our iniquities before thee, our secret \add sins\add* in the light of thy countenance.
\p
\v 9 For all our days are passed away in thy wrath: we spend our years as a tale \add that is told\add*.\f + \fr 90:9 \fr*\fq passed… \fq*\ft - Heb. turned away\ft*\f*\f + \fr 90:9 \fr*\fq as a… \fq*\ft - or, as a meditation\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 The days of our years \add are\add* threescore years and ten; and if by reason of strength \add they be\add* fourscore years, yet \add is\add* their strength labour and sorrow; for it is soon cut off, and we fly away.\f + \fr 90:10 \fr*\fq The days… \fq*\ft - Heb. As for the days of our years, in them are seventy years\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 Who knoweth the power of thine anger? even according to thy fear, \add so is\add* thy wrath.
\p
\v 12 So teach \add us\add* to number our days, that we may apply \add our\add* hearts unto wisdom.\f + \fr 90:12 \fr*\fq apply \fq*\ft - Heb. cause to come\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 Return, O \nd LORD\nd*, how long? and let it repent thee concerning thy servants.
\p
\v 14 O satisfy us early with thy mercy; that we may rejoice and be glad all our days.
\p
\v 15 Make us glad according to the days \add wherein\add* thou hast afflicted us, \add and\add* the years \add wherein\add* we have seen evil.
\p
\v 16 Let thy work appear unto thy servants, and thy glory unto their children.
\p
\v 17 And let the beauty of the \nd LORD\nd* our God be upon us: and establish thou the work of our hands upon us; yea, the work of our hands establish thou it.
\c 91
\p
\v 1 He that dwelleth in the secret place of the most High shall abide under the shadow of the Almighty.\f + \fr 91:1 \fr*\fq abide \fq*\ft - Heb. lodge\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 I will say of the \nd LORD\nd*, \add He is\add* my refuge and my fortress: my God; in him will I trust.
\p
\v 3 Surely he shall deliver thee from the snare of the fowler, \add and\add* from the noisome pestilence.
\p
\v 4 He shall cover thee with his feathers, and under his wings shalt thou trust: his truth \add shall be thy\add* shield and buckler.
\p
\v 5 Thou shalt not be afraid for the terror by night; \add nor\add* for the arrow \add that\add* flieth by day;
\p
\v 6 \add Nor\add* for the pestilence \add that\add* walketh in darkness; \add nor\add* for the destruction \add that\add* wasteth at noonday.
\p
\v 7 A thousand shall fall at thy side, and ten thousand at thy right hand; \add but\add* it shall not come nigh thee.
\p
\v 8 Only with thine eyes shalt thou behold and see the reward of the wicked.
\p
\v 9 Because thou hast made the \nd LORD\nd*, \add which is\add* my refuge, \add even\add* the most High, thy habitation;
\p
\v 10 There shall no evil befall thee, neither shall any plague come nigh thy dwelling.
\p
\v 11 For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways.
\p
\v 12 They shall bear thee up in \add their\add* hands, lest thou dash thy foot against a stone.
\p
\v 13 Thou shalt tread upon the lion and adder: the young lion and the dragon shalt thou trample under feet.\f + \fr 91:13 \fr*\fq adder \fq*\ft - or, asp\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 Because he hath set his love upon me, therefore will I deliver him: I will set him on high, because he hath known my name.
\p
\v 15 He shall call upon me, and I will answer him: I \add will be\add* with him in trouble; I will deliver him, and honour him.
\p
\v 16 With long life will I satisfy him, and shew him my salvation.\f + \fr 91:16 \fr*\fq long… \fq*\ft - Heb. length of days\ft*\f*
\c 92
\d A Psalm \add or\add* Song for the sabbath day.
\p
\v 1 \add It is a\add* good \add thing\add* to give thanks unto the \nd LORD\nd*, and to sing praises unto thy name, O most High:
\p
\v 2 To shew forth thy lovingkindness in the morning, and thy faithfulness every night,\f + \fr 92:2 \fr*\fq every… \fq*\ft - Heb. in the nights\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 Upon an instrument of ten strings, and upon the psaltery; upon the harp with a solemn sound.\f + \fr 92:3 \fr*\fq the harp… \fq*\ft - or, the solemn sound with the harp\ft*\f*\f + \fr 92:3 \fr*\fq a solemn… \fq*\ft - Heb. Higgaion\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 For thou, \nd LORD\nd*, hast made me glad through thy work: I will triumph in the works of thy hands.
\p
\v 5 O \nd LORD\nd*, how great are thy works! \add and\add* thy thoughts are very deep.
\p
\v 6 A brutish man knoweth not; neither doth a fool understand this.
\p
\v 7 When the wicked spring as the grass, and when all the workers of iniquity do flourish; \add it is\add* that they shall be destroyed for ever:
\p
\v 8 But thou, \nd LORD\nd*, \add art most\add* high for evermore.
\p
\v 9 For, lo, thine enemies, O \nd LORD\nd*, for, lo, thine enemies shall perish; all the workers of iniquity shall be scattered.
\p
\v 10 But my horn shalt thou exalt like \add the horn of\add* an unicorn: I shall be anointed with fresh oil.
\p
\v 11 Mine eye also shall see \add my desire\add* on mine enemies, \add and\add* mine ears shall hear \add my desire\add* of the wicked that rise up against me.
\p
\v 12 The righteous shall flourish like the palm tree: he shall grow like a cedar in Lebanon.
\p
\v 13 Those that be planted in the house of the \nd LORD\nd* shall flourish in the courts of our God.
\p
\v 14 They shall still bring forth fruit in old age; they shall be fat and flourishing;\f + \fr 92:14 \fr*\fq flourishing \fq*\ft - Heb. green\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 To shew that the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* upright: \add he is\add* my rock, and \add there is\add* no unrighteousness in him.
\c 93
\p
\v 1 The \nd LORD\nd* reigneth, he is clothed with majesty; the \nd LORD\nd* is clothed with strength, \add wherewith\add* he hath girded himself: the world also is stablished, that it cannot be moved.
\p
\v 2 Thy throne \add is\add* established of old: thou \add art\add* from everlasting.\f + \fr 93:2 \fr*\fq of old \fq*\ft - Heb. from then\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 The floods have lifted up, O \nd LORD\nd*, the floods have lifted up their voice; the floods lift up their waves.
\p
\v 4 The \nd LORD\nd* on high \add is\add* mightier than the noise of many waters, \add yea, than\add* the mighty waves of the sea.
\p
\v 5 Thy testimonies are very sure: holiness becometh thine house, O \nd LORD\nd*, for ever.\f + \fr 93:5 \fr*\fq for ever \fq*\ft - Heb. to length of days\ft*\f*
\c 94
\p
\v 1 O \nd LORD\nd* God, to whom vengeance belongeth; O God, to whom vengeance belongeth, shew thyself.\f + \fr 94:1 \fr*\fq God… \fq*\ft - Heb. God of revenges\ft*\f*\f + \fr 94:1 \fr*\fq shew… \fq*\ft - Heb. shine forth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Lift up thyself, thou judge of the earth: render a reward to the proud.
\p
\v 3 \nd LORD\nd*, how long shall the wicked, how long shall the wicked triumph?
\p
\v 4 \add How long\add* shall they utter \add and\add* speak hard things? \add and\add* all the workers of iniquity boast themselves?
\p
\v 5 They break in pieces thy people, O \nd LORD\nd*, and afflict thine heritage.
\p
\v 6 They slay the widow and the stranger, and murder the fatherless.
\p
\v 7 Yet they say, The \nd LORD\nd* shall not see, neither shall the God of Jacob regard \add it\add*.
\p
\v 8 Understand, ye brutish among the people: and \add ye\add* fools, when will ye be wise?
\p
\v 9 He that planted the ear, shall he not hear? he that formed the eye, shall he not see?
\p
\v 10 He that chastiseth the heathen, shall not he correct? he that teacheth man knowledge, \add shall not he know\add*?
\p
\v 11 The \nd LORD\nd* knoweth the thoughts of man, that they \add are\add* vanity.
\p
\v 12 Blessed \add is\add* the man whom thou chastenest, O \nd LORD\nd*, and teachest him out of thy law;
\p
\v 13 That thou mayest give him rest from the days of adversity, until the pit be digged for the wicked.
\p
\v 14 For the \nd LORD\nd* will not cast off his people, neither will he forsake his inheritance.
\p
\v 15 But judgment shall return unto righteousness: and all the upright in heart shall follow it.\f + \fr 94:15 \fr*\fq shall follow… \fq*\ft - Heb. shall be after it\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 Who will rise up for me against the evildoers? \add or\add* who will stand up for me against the workers of iniquity?
\p
\v 17 Unless the \nd LORD\nd* \add had been\add* my help, my soul had almost dwelt in silence.\f + \fr 94:17 \fr*\fq almost \fq*\ft - or, quickly\ft*\f*
\p
\v 18 When I said, My foot slippeth; thy mercy, O \nd LORD\nd*, held me up.
\p
\v 19 In the multitude of my thoughts within me thy comforts delight my soul.
\p
\v 20 Shall the throne of iniquity have fellowship with thee, which frameth mischief by a law?
\p
\v 21 They gather themselves together against the soul of the righteous, and condemn the innocent blood.
\p
\v 22 But the \nd LORD\nd* is my defence; and my God \add is\add* the rock of my refuge.
\p
\v 23 And he shall bring upon them their own iniquity, and shall cut them off in their own wickedness; \add yea\add*, the \nd LORD\nd* our God shall cut them off.
\c 95
\p
\v 1 O come, let us sing unto the \nd LORD\nd*: let us make a joyful noise to the rock of our salvation.
\p
\v 2 Let us come before his presence with thanksgiving, and make a joyful noise unto him with psalms.\f + \fr 95:2 \fr*\fq come… \fq*\ft - Heb. prevent his face\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 For the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* a great God, and a great King above all gods.
\p
\v 4 In his hand \add are\add* the deep places of the earth: the strength of the hills \add is\add* his also.\f + \fr 95:4 \fr*\fq In… \fq*\ft - Heb. In whose\ft*\f*\f + \fr 95:4 \fr*\fq the strength… \fq*\ft - or, the heights of the hills are his\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 The sea \add is\add* his, and he made it: and his hands formed the dry \add land\add*.\f + \fr 95:5 \fr*\fq The sea… \fq*\ft - Heb. Whose the sea is\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 O come, let us worship and bow down: let us kneel before the \nd LORD\nd* our maker.
\p
\v 7 For he \add is\add* our God; and we \add are\add* the people of his pasture, and the sheep of his hand. To day if ye will hear his voice,
\p
\v 8 Harden not your heart, as in the provocation, \add and\add* as \add in\add* the day of temptation in the wilderness:\f + \fr 95:8 \fr*\fq provocation \fq*\ft - Heb. contention\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 When your fathers tempted me, proved me, and saw my work.
\p
\v 10 Forty years long was I grieved with \add this\add* generation, and said, It \add is\add* a people that do err in their heart, and they have not known my ways:
\p
\v 11 Unto whom I sware in my wrath that they should not enter into my rest.\f + \fr 95:11 \fr*\fq that… \fq*\ft - Heb. if they enter into my rest\ft*\f*
\c 96
\p
\v 1 O sing unto the \nd LORD\nd* a new song: sing unto the \nd LORD\nd*, all the earth.
\p
\v 2 Sing unto the \nd LORD\nd*, bless his name; shew forth his salvation from day to day.
\p
\v 3 Declare his glory among the heathen, his wonders among all people.
\p
\v 4 For the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* great, and greatly to be praised: he \add is\add* to be feared above all gods.
\p
\v 5 For all the gods of the nations \add are\add* idols: but the \nd LORD\nd* made the heavens.
\p
\v 6 Honour and majesty \add are\add* before him: strength and beauty \add are\add* in his sanctuary.
\p
\v 7 Give unto the \nd LORD\nd*, O ye kindreds of the people, give unto the \nd LORD\nd* glory and strength.
\p
\v 8 Give unto the \nd LORD\nd* the glory \add due unto\add* his name: bring an offering, and come into his courts.\f + \fr 96:8 \fr*\fq due… \fq*\ft - Heb. of his name\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 O worship the \nd LORD\nd* in the beauty of holiness: fear before him, all the earth.\f + \fr 96:9 \fr*\fq in the… \fq*\ft - or, in the glorious sanctuary\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 Say among the heathen \add that\add* the \nd LORD\nd* reigneth: the world also shall be established that it shall not be moved: he shall judge the people righteously.
\p
\v 11 Let the heavens rejoice, and let the earth be glad; let the sea roar, and the fulness thereof.\f + \fr 96:11 \fr*\fq the fulness… \fq*\ft - or, all it containeth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 Let the field be joyful, and all that \add is\add* therein: then shall all the trees of the wood rejoice
\p
\v 13 Before the \nd LORD\nd*: for he cometh, for he cometh to judge the earth: he shall judge the world with righteousness, and the people with his truth.
\c 97
\p
\v 1 The \nd LORD\nd* reigneth; let the earth rejoice; let the multitude of isles be glad \add thereof\add*.\f + \fr 97:1 \fr*\fq multitude… \fq*\ft - Heb. many, or, great isles\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Clouds and darkness \add are\add* round about him: righteousness and judgment \add are\add* the habitation of his throne.\f + \fr 97:2 \fr*\fq habitation \fq*\ft - or, establishment\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 A fire goeth before him, and burneth up his enemies round about.
\p
\v 4 His lightnings enlightened the world: the earth saw, and trembled.
\p
\v 5 The hills melted like wax at the presence of the \nd LORD\nd*, at the presence of the Lord of the whole earth.
\p
\v 6 The heavens declare his righteousness, and all the people see his glory.
\p
\v 7 Confounded be all they that serve graven images, that boast themselves of idols: worship him, all \add ye\add* gods.
\p
\v 8 Zion heard, and was glad; and the daughters of Judah rejoiced because of thy judgments, O \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 9 For thou, \nd LORD\nd*, \add art\add* high above all the earth: thou art exalted far above all gods.
\p
\v 10 Ye that love the \nd LORD\nd*, hate evil: he preserveth the souls of his saints; he delivereth them out of the hand of the wicked.
\p
\v 11 Light is sown for the righteous, and gladness for the upright in heart.
\p
\v 12 Rejoice in the \nd LORD\nd*, ye righteous; and give thanks at the remembrance of his holiness.\f + \fr 97:12 \fr*\fq at… \fq*\ft - or, to the memorial\ft*\f*
\c 98
\d A Psalm.
\p
\v 1 O sing unto the \nd LORD\nd* a new song; for he hath done marvellous things: his right hand, and his holy arm, hath gotten him the victory.
\p
\v 2 The \nd LORD\nd* hath made known his salvation: his righteousness hath he openly shewed in the sight of the heathen.\f + \fr 98:2 \fr*\fq openly… \fq*\ft - or, revealed\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 He hath remembered his mercy and his truth toward the house of Israel: all the ends of the earth have seen the salvation of our God.
\p
\v 4 Make a joyful noise unto the \nd LORD\nd*, all the earth: make a loud noise, and rejoice, and sing praise.
\p
\v 5 Sing unto the \nd LORD\nd* with the harp; with the harp, and the voice of a psalm.
\p
\v 6 With trumpets and sound of cornet make a joyful noise before the \nd LORD\nd*, the King.
\p
\v 7 Let the sea roar, and the fulness thereof; the world, and they that dwell therein.\f + \fr 98:7 \fr*\fq the fulness… \fq*\ft - or, all it containeth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 Let the floods clap \add their\add* hands: let the hills be joyful together
\p
\v 9 Before the \nd LORD\nd*; for he cometh to judge the earth: with righteousness shall he judge the world, and the people with equity.
\c 99
\p
\v 1 The \nd LORD\nd* reigneth; let the people tremble: he sitteth \add between\add* the cherubims; let the earth be moved.\f + \fr 99:1 \fr*\fq be moved \fq*\ft - Heb. stagger\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* great in Zion; and he \add is\add* high above all the people.
\p
\v 3 Let them praise thy great and terrible name; \add for\add* it \add is\add* holy.
\p
\v 4 The king’s strength also loveth judgment; thou dost establish equity, thou executest judgment and righteousness in Jacob.
\p
\v 5 Exalt ye the \nd LORD\nd* our God, and worship at his footstool; \add for\add* he \add is\add* holy.\f + \fr 99:5 \fr*\fq he is… \fq*\ft - or, it is holy\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Moses and Aaron among his priests, and Samuel among them that call upon his name; they called upon the \nd LORD\nd*, and he answered them.
\p
\v 7 He spake unto them in the cloudy pillar: they kept his testimonies, and the ordinance \add that\add* he gave them.
\p
\v 8 Thou answeredst them, O \nd LORD\nd* our God: thou wast a God that forgavest them, though thou tookest vengeance of their inventions.
\p
\v 9 Exalt the \nd LORD\nd* our God, and worship at his holy hill; for the \nd LORD\nd* our God \add is\add* holy.
\c 100
\d A Psalm of praise.
\p
\v 1 Make a joyful noise unto the \nd LORD\nd*, all ye lands.\f + \fr 100:1 \fr*\fq praise \fq*\ft - or, thanksgiving\ft*\f*\f + \fr 100:1 \fr*\fq all… \fq*\ft - Heb. all the earth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Serve the \nd LORD\nd* with gladness: come before his presence with singing.
\p
\v 3 Know ye that the \nd LORD\nd* he \add is\add* God: \add it is\add* he \add that\add* hath made us, and not we ourselves; \add we are\add* his people, and the sheep of his pasture.\f + \fr 100:3 \fr*\fq and not… \fq*\ft - or, and his we are\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Enter into his gates with thanksgiving, \add and\add* into his courts with praise: be thankful unto him, \add and\add* bless his name.
\p
\v 5 For the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* good; his mercy \add is\add* everlasting; and his truth \add endureth\add* to all generations.\f + \fr 100:5 \fr*\fq to all… \fq*\ft - Heb. to generation and generation\ft*\f*
\c 101
\d A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 I will sing of mercy and judgment: unto thee, O \nd LORD\nd*, will I sing.
\p
\v 2 I will behave myself wisely in a perfect way. O when wilt thou come unto me? I will walk within my house with a perfect heart.
\p
\v 3 I will set no wicked thing before mine eyes: I hate the work of them that turn aside; \add it\add* shall not cleave to me.\f + \fr 101:3 \fr*\fq wicked… \fq*\ft - Heb. thing of Belial\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 A froward heart shall depart from me: I will not know a wicked \add person\add*.
\p
\v 5 Whoso privily slandereth his neighbour, him will I cut off: him that hath an high look and a proud heart will not I suffer.
\p
\v 6 Mine eyes \add shall be\add* upon the faithful of the land, that they may dwell with me: he that walketh in a perfect way, he shall serve me.\f + \fr 101:6 \fr*\fq in a… \fq*\ft - or, perfect in the way\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 He that worketh deceit shall not dwell within my house: he that telleth lies shall not tarry in my sight.\f + \fr 101:7 \fr*\fq shall not tarry \fq*\ft - Heb. shall not be established\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 I will early destroy all the wicked of the land; that I may cut off all wicked doers from the city of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 102
\d A Prayer of the afflicted, when he is overwhelmed, and poureth out his complaint before the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 1 Hear my prayer, O \nd LORD\nd*, and let my cry come unto thee.\f + \fr 102:1 \fr*\fq of \fq*\ft - or, for\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Hide not thy face from me in the day \add when\add* I am in trouble; incline thine ear unto me: in the day \add when\add* I call answer me speedily.
\p
\v 3 For my days are consumed like smoke, and my bones are burned as an hearth.\f + \fr 102:3 \fr*\fq like… \fq*\ft - or, (as some read) into smoke\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 My heart is smitten, and withered like grass; so that I forget to eat my bread.
\p
\v 5 By reason of the voice of my groaning my bones cleave to my skin.\f + \fr 102:5 \fr*\fq skin \fq*\ft - or, flesh\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 I am like a pelican of the wilderness: I am like an owl of the desert.
\p
\v 7 I watch, and am as a sparrow alone upon the house top.
\p
\v 8 Mine enemies reproach me all the day; \add and\add* they that are mad against me are sworn against me.
\p
\v 9 For I have eaten ashes like bread, and mingled my drink with weeping,
\p
\v 10 Because of thine indignation and thy wrath: for thou hast lifted me up, and cast me down.
\p
\v 11 My days \add are\add* like a shadow that declineth; and I am withered like grass.
\p
\v 12 But thou, O \nd LORD\nd*, shalt endure for ever; and thy remembrance unto all generations.
\p
\v 13 Thou shalt arise, \add and\add* have mercy upon Zion: for the time to favour her, yea, the set time, is come.
\p
\v 14 For thy servants take pleasure in her stones, and favour the dust thereof.
\p
\v 15 So the heathen shall fear the name of the \nd LORD\nd*, and all the kings of the earth thy glory.
\p
\v 16 When the \nd LORD\nd* shall build up Zion, he shall appear in his glory.
\p
\v 17 He will regard the prayer of the destitute, and not despise their prayer.
\p
\v 18 This shall be written for the generation to come: and the people which shall be created shall praise the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 19 For he hath looked down from the height of his sanctuary; from heaven did the \nd LORD\nd* behold the earth;
\p
\v 20 To hear the groaning of the prisoner; to loose those that are appointed to death;\f + \fr 102:20 \fr*\fq those… \fq*\ft - Heb. the children of death\ft*\f*
\p
\v 21 To declare the name of the \nd LORD\nd* in Zion, and his praise in Jerusalem;
\p
\v 22 When the people are gathered together, and the kingdoms, to serve the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 23 He weakened my strength in the way; he shortened my days.\f + \fr 102:23 \fr*\fq weakened \fq*\ft - Heb. afflicted\ft*\f*
\p
\v 24 I said, O my God, take me not away in the midst of my days: thy years \add are\add* throughout all generations.
\p
\v 25 Of old hast thou laid the foundation of the earth: and the heavens \add are\add* the work of thy hands.
\p
\v 26 They shall perish, but thou shalt endure: yea, all of them shall wax old like a garment; as a vesture shalt thou change them, and they shall be changed:\f + \fr 102:26 \fr*\fq endure \fq*\ft - Heb. stand\ft*\f*
\p
\v 27 But thou \add art\add* the same, and thy years shall have no end.
\p
\v 28 The children of thy servants shall continue, and their seed shall be established before thee.
\c 103
\d \add A Psalm\add* of David.
\p
\v 1 Bless the \nd LORD\nd*, O my soul: and all that is within me, \add bless\add* his holy name.
\p
\v 2 Bless the \nd LORD\nd*, O my soul, and forget not all his benefits:
\p
\v 3 Who forgiveth all thine iniquities; who healeth all thy diseases;
\p
\v 4 Who redeemeth thy life from destruction; who crowneth thee with lovingkindness and tender mercies;
\p
\v 5 Who satisfieth thy mouth with good \add things; so that\add* thy youth is renewed like the eagle’s.
\p
\v 6 The \nd LORD\nd* executeth righteousness and judgment for all that are oppressed.
\p
\v 7 He made known his ways unto Moses, his acts unto the children of Israel.
\p
\v 8 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* merciful and gracious, slow to anger, and plenteous in mercy.\f + \fr 103:8 \fr*\fq plenteous… \fq*\ft - Heb. great in mercy\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 He will not always chide: neither will he keep \add his anger\add* for ever.
\p
\v 10 He hath not dealt with us after our sins; nor rewarded us according to our iniquities.
\p
\v 11 For as the heaven is high above the earth, \add so\add* great is his mercy toward them that fear him.\f + \fr 103:11 \fr*\fq as… \fq*\ft - Heb. according to the height of the heaven\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 As far as the east is from the west, \add so\add* far hath he removed our transgressions from us.
\p
\v 13 Like as a father pitieth \add his\add* children, \add so\add* the \nd LORD\nd* pitieth them that fear him.
\p
\v 14 For he knoweth our frame; he remembereth that we \add are\add* dust.
\p
\v 15 \add As for\add* man, his days \add are\add* as grass: as a flower of the field, so he flourisheth.
\p
\v 16 For the wind passeth over it, and it is gone; and the place thereof shall know it no more.\f + \fr 103:16 \fr*\fq it is… \fq*\ft - Heb. it is not\ft*\f*
\p
\v 17 But the mercy of the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* from everlasting to everlasting upon them that fear him, and his righteousness unto children’s children;
\p
\v 18 To such as keep his covenant, and to those that remember his commandments to do them.
\p
\v 19 The \nd LORD\nd* hath prepared his throne in the heavens; and his kingdom ruleth over all.
\p
\v 20 Bless the \nd LORD\nd*, ye his angels, that excel in strength, that do his commandments, hearkening unto the voice of his word.\f + \fr 103:20 \fr*\fq that excel… \fq*\ft - Heb. mighty in strength\ft*\f*
\p
\v 21 Bless ye the \nd LORD\nd*, all \add ye\add* his hosts; \add ye\add* ministers of his, that do his pleasure.
\p
\v 22 Bless the \nd LORD\nd*, all his works in all places of his dominion: bless the \nd LORD\nd*, O my soul.
\c 104
\p
\v 1 Bless the \nd LORD\nd*, O my soul. O \nd LORD\nd* my God, thou art very great; thou art clothed with honour and majesty.
\p
\v 2 Who coverest \add thyself\add* with light as \add with\add* a garment: who stretchest out the heavens like a curtain:
\p
\v 3 Who layeth the beams of his chambers in the waters: who maketh the clouds his chariot: who walketh upon the wings of the wind:
\p
\v 4 Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire:
\p
\v 5 \add Who\add* laid the foundations of the earth, \add that\add* it should not be removed for ever.\f + \fr 104:5 \fr*\fq Who… \fq*\ft - Heb. He hath founded the earth upon her bases\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Thou coveredst it with the deep as \add with\add* a garment: the waters stood above the mountains.
\p
\v 7 At thy rebuke they fled; at the voice of thy thunder they hasted away.
\p
\v 8 They go up by the mountains; they go down by the valleys unto the place which thou hast founded for them.\f + \fr 104:8 \fr*\fq They go up… \fq*\ft - or, The mountains ascend, the valleys descend\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 Thou hast set a bound that they may not pass over; that they turn not again to cover the earth.
\p
\v 10 He sendeth the springs into the valleys, \add which\add* run among the hills.\f + \fr 104:10 \fr*\fq He \fq*\ft - Heb. Who\ft*\f*\f + \fr 104:10 \fr*\fq run \fq*\ft - Heb. walk\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 They give drink to every beast of the field: the wild asses quench their thirst.\f + \fr 104:11 \fr*\fq quench \fq*\ft - Heb. break\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 By them shall the fowls of the heaven have their habitation, \add which\add* sing among the branches.\f + \fr 104:12 \fr*\fq sing \fq*\ft - Heb. give a voice\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 He watereth the hills from his chambers: the earth is satisfied with the fruit of thy works.
\p
\v 14 He causeth the grass to grow for the cattle, and herb for the service of man: that he may bring forth food out of the earth;
\p
\v 15 And wine \add that\add* maketh glad the heart of man, \add and\add* oil to make \add his\add* face to shine, and bread \add which\add* strengtheneth man’s heart.\f + \fr 104:15 \fr*\fq oil… \fq*\ft - Heb. to make his face shine with oil, or, more than oil\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 The trees of the \nd LORD\nd* are full \add of sap;\add* the cedars of Lebanon, which he hath planted;
\p
\v 17 Where the birds make their nests: \add as for\add* the stork, the fir trees \add are\add* her house.
\p
\v 18 The high hills \add are\add* a refuge for the wild goats; \add and\add* the rocks for the conies.
\p
\v 19 He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.
\p
\v 20 Thou makest darkness, and it is night: wherein all the beasts of the forest do creep \add forth\add*.\f + \fr 104:20 \fr*\fq beasts… \fq*\ft - Heb. beasts thereof do trample on the forest\ft*\f*
\p
\v 21 The young lions roar after their prey, and seek their meat from God.
\p
\v 22 The sun ariseth, they gather themselves together, and lay them down in their dens.
\p
\v 23 Man goeth forth unto his work and to his labour until the evening.
\p
\v 24 O \nd LORD\nd*, how manifold are thy works! in wisdom hast thou made them all: the earth is full of thy riches.
\p
\v 25 \add So is\add* this great and wide sea, wherein \add are\add* things creeping innumerable, both small and great beasts.
\p
\v 26 There go the ships: \add there is\add* that leviathan, \add whom\add* thou hast made to play therein.\f + \fr 104:26 \fr*\fq made \fq*\ft - Heb. formed\ft*\f*
\p
\v 27 These wait all upon thee; that thou mayest give \add them\add* their meat in due season.
\p
\v 28 \add That\add* thou givest them they gather: thou openest thine hand, they are filled with good.
\p
\v 29 Thou hidest thy face, they are troubled: thou takest away their breath, they die, and return to their dust.
\p
\v 30 Thou sendest forth thy spirit, they are created: and thou renewest the face of the earth.
\p
\v 31 The glory of the \nd LORD\nd* shall endure for ever: the \nd LORD\nd* shall rejoice in his works.\f + \fr 104:31 \fr*\fq endure \fq*\ft - Heb. be\ft*\f*
\p
\v 32 He looketh on the earth, and it trembleth: he toucheth the hills, and they smoke.
\p
\v 33 I will sing unto the \nd LORD\nd* as long as I live: I will sing praise to my God while I have my being.
\p
\v 34 My meditation of him shall be sweet: I will be glad in the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 35 Let the sinners be consumed out of the earth, and let the wicked be no more. Bless thou the \nd LORD\nd*, O my soul. Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 105
\p
\v 1 O give thanks unto the \nd LORD\nd*; call upon his name: make known his deeds among the people.
\p
\v 2 Sing unto him, sing psalms unto him: talk ye of all his wondrous works.
\p
\v 3 Glory ye in his holy name: let the heart of them rejoice that seek the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 4 Seek the \nd LORD\nd*, and his strength: seek his face evermore.
\p
\v 5 Remember his marvellous works that he hath done; his wonders, and the judgments of his mouth;
\p
\v 6 O ye seed of Abraham his servant, ye children of Jacob his chosen.
\p
\v 7 He \add is\add* the \nd LORD\nd* our God: his judgments \add are\add* in all the earth.
\p
\v 8 He hath remembered his covenant for ever, the word \add which\add* he commanded to a thousand generations.
\p
\v 9 Which \add covenant\add* he made with Abraham, and his oath unto Isaac;
\p
\v 10 And confirmed the same unto Jacob for a law, \add and\add* to Israel \add for\add* an everlasting covenant:
\p
\v 11 Saying, Unto thee will I give the land of Canaan, the lot of your inheritance:\f + \fr 105:11 \fr*\fq lot \fq*\ft - Heb. cord\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 When they were \add but\add* a few men in number; yea, very few, and strangers in it.
\p
\v 13 When they went from one nation to another, from \add one\add* kingdom to another people;
\p
\v 14 He suffered no man to do them wrong: yea, he reproved kings for their sakes;
\p
\v 15 \add Saying\add*, Touch not mine anointed, and do my prophets no harm.
\p
\v 16 Moreover he called for a famine upon the land: he brake the whole staff of bread.
\p
\v 17 He sent a man before them, \add even\add* Joseph, \add who\add* was sold for a servant:
\p
\v 18 Whose feet they hurt with fetters: he was laid in iron:\f + \fr 105:18 \fr*\fq he… \fq*\ft - Heb. his soul came into iron\ft*\f*
\p
\v 19 Until the time that his word came: the word of the \nd LORD\nd* tried him.
\p
\v 20 The king sent and loosed him; \add even\add* the ruler of the people, and let him go free.
\p
\v 21 He made him lord of his house, and ruler of all his substance:\f + \fr 105:21 \fr*\fq substance \fq*\ft - Heb. possession\ft*\f*
\p
\v 22 To bind his princes at his pleasure; and teach his senators wisdom.
\p
\v 23 Israel also came into Egypt; and Jacob sojourned in the land of Ham.
\p
\v 24 And he increased his people greatly; and made them stronger than their enemies.
\p
\v 25 He turned their heart to hate his people, to deal subtilly with his servants.
\p
\v 26 He sent Moses his servant; \add and\add* Aaron whom he had chosen.
\p
\v 27 They shewed his signs among them, and wonders in the land of Ham.\f + \fr 105:27 \fr*\fq his… \fq*\ft - Heb. words of his signs\ft*\f*
\p
\v 28 He sent darkness, and made it dark; and they rebelled not against his word.
\p
\v 29 He turned their waters into blood, and slew their fish.
\p
\v 30 Their land brought forth frogs in abundance, in the chambers of their kings.
\p
\v 31 He spake, and there came divers sorts of flies, \add and\add* lice in all their coasts.
\p
\v 32 He gave them hail for rain, \add and\add* flaming fire in their land.\f + \fr 105:32 \fr*\fq them… \fq*\ft - Heb. their rain hail\ft*\f*
\p
\v 33 He smote their vines also and their fig trees; and brake the trees of their coasts.
\p
\v 34 He spake, and the locusts came, and caterpillers, and that without number,
\p
\v 35 And did eat up all the herbs in their land, and devoured the fruit of their ground.
\p
\v 36 He smote also all the firstborn in their land, the chief of all their strength.
\p
\v 37 He brought them forth also with silver and gold: and \add there was\add* not one feeble \add person\add* among their tribes.
\p
\v 38 Egypt was glad when they departed: for the fear of them fell upon them.
\p
\v 39 He spread a cloud for a covering; and fire to give light in the night.
\p
\v 40 \add The people\add* asked, and he brought quails, and satisfied them with the bread of heaven.
\p
\v 41 He opened the rock, and the waters gushed out; they ran in the dry places \add like\add* a river.
\p
\v 42 For he remembered his holy promise, \add and\add* Abraham his servant.
\p
\v 43 And he brought forth his people with joy, \add and\add* his chosen with gladness:\f + \fr 105:43 \fr*\fq gladness \fq*\ft - Heb. singing\ft*\f*
\p
\v 44 And gave them the lands of the heathen: and they inherited the labour of the people;
\p
\v 45 That they might observe his statutes, and keep his laws. Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*.\f + \fr 105:45 \fr*\fq Praise… \fq*\ft - Heb. Hallelujah\ft*\f*
\c 106
\p
\v 1 Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*. O give thanks unto the \nd LORD\nd*; for \add he is\add* good: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.\f + \fr 106:1 \fr*\fq Praise… \fq*\ft - Heb. Hallelujah\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Who can utter the mighty acts of the \nd LORD\nd*? \add who\add* can shew forth all his praise?
\p
\v 3 Blessed \add are\add* they that keep judgment, \add and\add* he that doeth righteousness at all times.
\p
\v 4 Remember me, O \nd LORD\nd*, with the favour \add that thou bearest unto\add* thy people: O visit me with thy salvation;
\p
\v 5 That I may see the good of thy chosen, that I may rejoice in the gladness of thy nation, that I may glory with thine inheritance.
\p
\v 6 We have sinned with our fathers, we have committed iniquity, we have done wickedly.
\p
\v 7 Our fathers understood not thy wonders in Egypt; they remembered not the multitude of thy mercies; but provoked \add him\add* at the sea, \add even\add* at the Red sea.
\p
\v 8 Nevertheless he saved them for his name’s sake, that he might make his mighty power to be known.
\p
\v 9 He rebuked the Red sea also, and it was dried up: so he led them through the depths, as through the wilderness.
\p
\v 10 And he saved them from the hand of him that hated \add them\add*, and redeemed them from the hand of the enemy.
\p
\v 11 And the waters covered their enemies: there was not one of them left.
\p
\v 12 Then believed they his words; they sang his praise.
\p
\v 13 They soon forgat his works; they waited not for his counsel:\f + \fr 106:13 \fr*\fq They soon… \fq*\ft - Heb. They made haste, they forgat\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 But lusted exceedingly in the wilderness, and tempted God in the desert.\f + \fr 106:14 \fr*\fq lusted… \fq*\ft - Heb. lusted a lust\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 And he gave them their request; but sent leanness into their soul.
\p
\v 16 They envied Moses also in the camp, \add and\add* Aaron the saint of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 17 The earth opened and swallowed up Dathan, and covered the company of Abiram.
\p
\v 18 And a fire was kindled in their company; the flame burned up the wicked.
\p
\v 19 They made a calf in Horeb, and worshipped the molten image.
\p
\v 20 Thus they changed their glory into the similitude of an ox that eateth grass.
\p
\v 21 They forgat God their saviour, which had done great things in Egypt;
\p
\v 22 Wondrous works in the land of Ham, \add and\add* terrible things by the Red sea.
\p
\v 23 Therefore he said that he would destroy them, had not Moses his chosen stood before him in the breach, to turn away his wrath, lest he should destroy \add them\add*.
\p
\v 24 Yea, they despised the pleasant land, they believed not his word:\f + \fr 106:24 \fr*\fq the pleasant… \fq*\ft - Heb. a land of desire\ft*\f*
\p
\v 25 But murmured in their tents, \add and\add* hearkened not unto the voice of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 26 Therefore he lifted up his hand against them, to overthrow them in the wilderness:\f + \fr 106:26 \fr*\fq to overthrow \fq*\ft - Heb. to make them fall\ft*\f*
\p
\v 27 To overthrow their seed also among the nations, and to scatter them in the lands.\f + \fr 106:27 \fr*\fq To overthrow \fq*\ft - Heb. To make them fall\ft*\f*
\p
\v 28 They joined themselves also unto Baal-peor, and ate the sacrifices of the dead.
\p
\v 29 Thus they provoked \add him\add* to anger with their inventions: and the plague brake in upon them.
\p
\v 30 Then stood up Phinehas, and executed judgment: and \add so\add* the plague was stayed.
\p
\v 31 And that was counted unto him for righteousness unto all generations for evermore.
\p
\v 32 They angered \add him\add* also at the waters of strife, so that it went ill with Moses for their sakes:
\p
\v 33 Because they provoked his spirit, so that he spake unadvisedly with his lips.
\p
\v 34 They did not destroy the nations, concerning whom the \nd LORD\nd* commanded them:
\p
\v 35 But were mingled among the heathen, and learned their works.
\p
\v 36 And they served their idols: which were a snare unto them.
\p
\v 37 Yea, they sacrificed their sons and their daughters unto devils,
\p
\v 38 And shed innocent blood, \add even\add* the blood of their sons and of their daughters, whom they sacrificed unto the idols of Canaan: and the land was polluted with blood.
\p
\v 39 Thus were they defiled with their own works, and went a whoring with their own inventions.
\p
\v 40 Therefore was the wrath of the \nd LORD\nd* kindled against his people, insomuch that he abhorred his own inheritance.
\p
\v 41 And he gave them into the hand of the heathen; and they that hated them ruled over them.
\p
\v 42 Their enemies also oppressed them, and they were brought into subjection under their hand.
\p
\v 43 Many times did he deliver them; but they provoked \add him\add* with their counsel, and were brought low for their iniquity.\f + \fr 106:43 \fr*\fq brought… \fq*\ft - or, impoverished, or, weakened\ft*\f*
\p
\v 44 Nevertheless he regarded their affliction, when he heard their cry:
\p
\v 45 And he remembered for them his covenant, and repented according to the multitude of his mercies.
\p
\v 46 He made them also to be pitied of all those that carried them captives.
\p
\v 47 Save us, O \nd LORD\nd* our God, and gather us from among the heathen, to give thanks unto thy holy name, \add and\add* to triumph in thy praise.
\p
\v 48 Blessed \add be\add* the \nd LORD\nd* God of Israel from everlasting to everlasting: and let all the people say, Amen. Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*.\f + \fr 106:48 \fr*\fq Praise… \fq*\ft - Heb. Hallelujah\ft*\f*
\c 107
\p
\v 1 O give thanks unto the \nd LORD\nd*, for \add he is\add* good: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 2 Let the redeemed of the \nd LORD\nd* say \add so\add*, whom he hath redeemed from the hand of the enemy;
\p
\v 3 And gathered them out of the lands, from the east, and from the west, from the north, and from the south.\f + \fr 107:3 \fr*\fq south \fq*\ft - Heb. sea\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 They wandered in the wilderness in a solitary way; they found no city to dwell in.
\p
\v 5 Hungry and thirsty, their soul fainted in them.
\p
\v 6 Then they cried unto the \nd LORD\nd* in their trouble, \add and\add* he delivered them out of their distresses.
\p
\v 7 And he led them forth by the right way, that they might go to a city of habitation.
\p
\v 8 Oh that \add men\add* would praise the \nd LORD\nd* \add for\add* his goodness, and \add for\add* his wonderful works to the children of men!
\p
\v 9 For he satisfieth the longing soul, and filleth the hungry soul with goodness.
\p
\v 10 Such as sit in darkness and in the shadow of death, \add being\add* bound in affliction and iron;
\p
\v 11 Because they rebelled against the words of God, and contemned the counsel of the most High:
\p
\v 12 Therefore he brought down their heart with labour; they fell down, and \add there was\add* none to help.
\p
\v 13 Then they cried unto the \nd LORD\nd* in their trouble, \add and\add* he saved them out of their distresses.
\p
\v 14 He brought them out of darkness and the shadow of death, and brake their bands in sunder.
\p
\v 15 Oh that \add men\add* would praise the \nd LORD\nd* \add for\add* his goodness, and \add for\add* his wonderful works to the children of men!
\p
\v 16 For he hath broken the gates of brass, and cut the bars of iron in sunder.
\p
\v 17 Fools because of their transgression, and because of their iniquities, are afflicted.
\p
\v 18 Their soul abhorreth all manner of meat; and they draw near unto the gates of death.
\p
\v 19 Then they cry unto the \nd LORD\nd* in their trouble, \add and\add* he saveth them out of their distresses.
\p
\v 20 He sent his word, and healed them, and delivered \add them\add* from their destructions.
\p
\v 21 Oh that \add men\add* would praise the \nd LORD\nd* \add for\add* his goodness, and \add for\add* his wonderful works to the children of men!
\p
\v 22 And let them sacrifice the sacrifices of thanksgiving, and declare his works with rejoicing.\f + \fr 107:22 \fr*\fq rejoicing \fq*\ft - Heb. singing\ft*\f*
\p
\v 23 They that go down to the sea in ships, that do business in great waters;
\p
\v 24 These see the works of the \nd LORD\nd*, and his wonders in the deep.
\p
\v 25 For he commandeth, and raiseth the stormy wind, which lifteth up the waves thereof.\f + \fr 107:25 \fr*\fq raiseth \fq*\ft - Heb. maketh to stand\ft*\f*
\p
\v 26 They mount up to the heaven, they go down again to the depths: their soul is melted because of trouble.
\p
\v 27 They reel to and fro, and stagger like a drunken man, and are at their wits’ end. \f + \fr 107:27 \fr*\fq are… \fq*\ft - Heb. all their wisdom is swallowed up\ft*\f*
\p
\v 28 Then they cry unto the \nd LORD\nd* in their trouble, and he bringeth them out of their distresses.
\p
\v 29 He maketh the storm a calm, so that the waves thereof are still.
\p
\v 30 Then are they glad because they be quiet; so he bringeth them unto their desired haven.
\p
\v 31 Oh that \add men\add* would praise the \nd LORD\nd* \add for\add* his goodness, and \add for\add* his wonderful works to the children of men!
\p
\v 32 Let them exalt him also in the congregation of the people, and praise him in the assembly of the elders.
\p
\v 33 He turneth rivers into a wilderness, and the watersprings into dry ground;
\p
\v 34 A fruitful land into barrenness, for the wickedness of them that dwell therein.\f + \fr 107:34 \fr*\fq barrenness \fq*\ft - Heb. saltiness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 35 He turneth the wilderness into a standing water, and dry ground into watersprings.
\p
\v 36 And there he maketh the hungry to dwell, that they may prepare a city for habitation;
\p
\v 37 And sow the fields, and plant vineyards, which may yield fruits of increase.
\p
\v 38 He blesseth them also, so that they are multiplied greatly; and suffereth not their cattle to decrease.
\p
\v 39 Again, they are minished and brought low through oppression, affliction, and sorrow.
\p
\v 40 He poureth contempt upon princes, and causeth them to wander in the wilderness, \add where there is\add* no way.\f + \fr 107:40 \fr*\fq wilderness \fq*\ft - or, void place\ft*\f*
\p
\v 41 Yet setteth he the poor on high from affliction, and maketh \add him\add* families like a flock.\f + \fr 107:41 \fr*\fq from \fq*\ft - or, after\ft*\f*
\p
\v 42 The righteous shall see \add it\add*, and rejoice: and all iniquity shall stop her mouth.
\p
\v 43 Whoso \add is\add* wise, and will observe these \add things\add*, even they shall understand the lovingkindness of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 108
\d A Song \add or\add* Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 O God, my heart is fixed; I will sing and give praise, even with my glory.
\p
\v 2 Awake, psaltery and harp: I \add myself\add* will awake early.
\p
\v 3 I will praise thee, O \nd LORD\nd*, among the people: and I will sing praises unto thee among the nations.
\p
\v 4 For thy mercy \add is\add* great above the heavens: and thy truth \add reacheth\add* unto the clouds.\f + \fr 108:4 \fr*\fq clouds \fq*\ft - or, skies\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens: and thy glory above all the earth;
\p
\v 6 That thy beloved may be delivered: save \add with\add* thy right hand, and answer me.
\p
\v 7 God hath spoken in his holiness; I will rejoice, I will divide Shechem, and mete out the valley of Succoth.
\p
\v 8 Gilead \add is\add* mine; Manasseh \add is\add* mine; Ephraim also \add is\add* the strength of mine head; Judah \add is\add* my lawgiver;
\p
\v 9 Moab \add is\add* my washpot; over Edom will I cast out my shoe; over Philistia will I triumph.
\p
\v 10 Who will bring me into the strong city? who will lead me into Edom?
\p
\v 11 \add Wilt\add* not \add thou\add*, O God, \add who\add* hast cast us off? and wilt not thou, O God, go forth with our hosts?
\p
\v 12 Give us help from trouble: for vain \add is\add* the help of man.
\p
\v 13 Through God we shall do valiantly: for he \add it is that\add* shall tread down our enemies.
\c 109
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 Hold not thy peace, O God of my praise;
\p
\v 2 For the mouth of the wicked and the mouth of the deceitful are opened against me: they have spoken against me with a lying tongue.\f + \fr 109:2 \fr*\fq of the deceitful \fq*\ft - Heb. of deceit\ft*\f*\f + \fr 109:2 \fr*\fq are opened \fq*\ft - Heb. have opened themselves\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 They compassed me about also with words of hatred; and fought against me without a cause.
\p
\v 4 For my love they are my adversaries: but I \add give myself unto\add* prayer.
\p
\v 5 And they have rewarded me evil for good, and hatred for my love.
\p
\v 6 Set thou a wicked man over him: and let Satan stand at his right hand.\f + \fr 109:6 \fr*\fq Satan \fq*\ft - or, an adversary\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 When he shall be judged, let him be condemned: and let his prayer become sin.\f + \fr 109:7 \fr*\fq be condemned \fq*\ft - Heb. go out guilty, or, wicked\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 Let his days be few; \add and\add* let another take his office.\f + \fr 109:8 \fr*\fq office \fq*\ft - or, charge\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 Let his children be fatherless, and his wife a widow.
\p
\v 10 Let his children be continually vagabonds, and beg: let them seek \add their bread\add* also out of their desolate places.
\p
\v 11 Let the extortioner catch all that he hath; and let the strangers spoil his labour.
\p
\v 12 Let there be none to extend mercy unto him: neither let there be any to favour his fatherless children.
\p
\v 13 Let his posterity be cut off; \add and\add* in the generation following let their name be blotted out.
\p
\v 14 Let the iniquity of his fathers be remembered with the \nd LORD\nd*; and let not the sin of his mother be blotted out.
\p
\v 15 Let them be before the \nd LORD\nd* continually, that he may cut off the memory of them from the earth.
\p
\v 16 Because that he remembered not to shew mercy, but persecuted the poor and needy man, that he might even slay the broken in heart.
\p
\v 17 As he loved cursing, so let it come unto him: as he delighted not in blessing, so let it be far from him.
\p
\v 18 As he clothed himself with cursing like as with his garment, so let it come into his bowels like water, and like oil into his bones.\f + \fr 109:18 \fr*\fq into his bowels \fq*\ft - Heb. within him\ft*\f*
\p
\v 19 Let it be unto him as the garment \add which\add* covereth him, and for a girdle wherewith he is girded continually.
\p
\v 20 \add Let\add* this \add be\add* the reward of mine adversaries from the \nd LORD\nd*, and of them that speak evil against my soul.
\p
\v 21 But do thou for me, O \nd GOD\nd* the Lord, for thy name’s sake: because thy mercy \add is\add* good, deliver thou me.
\p
\v 22 For I \add am\add* poor and needy, and my heart is wounded within me.
\p
\v 23 I am gone like the shadow when it declineth: I am tossed up and down as the locust.
\p
\v 24 My knees are weak through fasting; and my flesh faileth of fatness.
\p
\v 25 I became also a reproach unto them: \add when\add* they looked upon me they shaked their heads.
\p
\v 26 Help me, O \nd LORD\nd* my God: O save me according to thy mercy:
\p
\v 27 That they may know that this \add is\add* thy hand; \add that\add* thou, \nd LORD\nd*, hast done it.
\p
\v 28 Let them curse, but bless thou: when they arise, let them be ashamed; but let thy servant rejoice.
\p
\v 29 Let mine adversaries be clothed with shame, and let them cover themselves with their own confusion, as with a mantle.
\p
\v 30 I will greatly praise the \nd LORD\nd* with my mouth; yea, I will praise him among the multitude.
\p
\v 31 For he shall stand at the right hand of the poor, to save \add him\add* from those that condemn his soul.\f + \fr 109:31 \fr*\fq those… \fq*\ft - Heb. the judges of\ft*\f*
\c 110
\d A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 The \nd LORD\nd* said unto my Lord, Sit thou at my right hand, until I make thine enemies thy footstool.
\p
\v 2 The \nd LORD\nd* shall send the rod of thy strength out of Zion: rule thou in the midst of thine enemies.
\p
\v 3 Thy people \add shall be\add* willing in the day of thy power, in the beauties of holiness from the womb of the morning: thou hast the dew of thy youth.\f + \fr 110:3 \fr*\fq from… \fq*\ft - or, more than the womb of the morning: thou shalt have, etc\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 The \nd LORD\nd* hath sworn, and will not repent, Thou \add art\add* a priest for ever after the order of Melchizedek.
\p
\v 5 The Lord at thy right hand shall strike through kings in the day of his wrath.
\p
\v 6 He shall judge among the heathen, he shall fill \add the places\add* with the dead bodies; he shall wound the heads over many countries.\f + \fr 110:6 \fr*\fq many \fq*\ft - or, great\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 He shall drink of the brook in the way: therefore shall he lift up the head.
\c 111
\p
\v 1 Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*. I will praise the \nd LORD\nd* with \add my\add* whole heart, in the assembly of the upright, and \add in\add* the congregation.\f + \fr 111:1 \fr*\fq Praise ye… \fq*\ft - Heb. Hallelujah\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 The works of the \nd LORD\nd* \add are\add* great, sought out of all them that have pleasure therein.
\p
\v 3 His work \add is\add* honourable and glorious: and his righteousness endureth for ever.
\p
\v 4 He hath made his wonderful works to be remembered: the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* gracious and full of compassion.
\p
\v 5 He hath given meat unto them that fear him: he will ever be mindful of his covenant.\f + \fr 111:5 \fr*\fq meat \fq*\ft - Heb. prey\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 He hath shewed his people the power of his works, that he may give them the heritage of the heathen.
\p
\v 7 The works of his hands \add are\add* verity and judgment; all his commandments \add are\add* sure.
\p
\v 8 They stand fast for ever and ever, \add and are\add* done in truth and uprightness.\f + \fr 111:8 \fr*\fq stand… \fq*\ft - Heb. are established\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 He sent redemption unto his people: he hath commanded his covenant for ever: holy and reverend \add is\add* his name.
\p
\v 10 The fear of the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* the beginning of wisdom: a good understanding have all they that do \add his commandments:\add* his praise endureth for ever.\f + \fr 111:10 \fr*\fq a good… \fq*\ft - or, good success\ft*\f*\f + \fr 111:10 \fr*\fq his commandments \fq*\ft - Heb. them\ft*\f*
\c 112
\p
\v 1 Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*. Blessed \add is\add* the man \add that\add* feareth the \nd LORD\nd*, \add that\add* delighteth greatly in his commandments.\f + \fr 112:1 \fr*\fq Praise… \fq*\ft - Heb. Hallelujah\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 His seed shall be mighty upon earth: the generation of the upright shall be blessed.
\p
\v 3 Wealth and riches \add shall be\add* in his house: and his righteousness endureth for ever.
\p
\v 4 Unto the upright there ariseth light in the darkness: \add he is\add* gracious, and full of compassion, and righteous.
\p
\v 5 A good man sheweth favour, and lendeth: he will guide his affairs with discretion.\f + \fr 112:5 \fr*\fq discretion \fq*\ft - Heb. judgment\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Surely he shall not be moved for ever: the righteous shall be in everlasting remembrance.
\p
\v 7 He shall not be afraid of evil tidings: his heart is fixed, trusting in the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 8 His heart \add is\add* established, he shall not be afraid, until he see \add his desire\add* upon his enemies.
\p
\v 9 He hath dispersed, he hath given to the poor; his righteousness endureth for ever; his horn shall be exalted with honour.
\p
\v 10 The wicked shall see \add it\add*, and be grieved; he shall gnash with his teeth, and melt away: the desire of the wicked shall perish.
\c 113
\p
\v 1 Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*. Praise, O ye servants of the \nd LORD\nd*, praise the name of the \nd LORD\nd*.\f + \fr 113:1 \fr*\fq Praise ye… \fq*\ft - Heb. Hallelujah\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Blessed be the name of the \nd LORD\nd* from this time forth and for evermore.
\p
\v 3 From the rising of the sun unto the going down of the same the \nd LORD’s\nd* name \add is\add* to be praised.
\p
\v 4 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* high above all nations, \add and\add* his glory above the heavens.
\p
\v 5 Who \add is\add* like unto the \nd LORD\nd* our God, who dwelleth on high,\f + \fr 113:5 \fr*\fq dwelleth… \fq*\ft - Heb. exalteth himself to dwell\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Who humbleth \add himself\add* to behold \add the things that are\add* in heaven, and in the earth!
\p
\v 7 He raiseth up the poor out of the dust, \add and\add* lifteth the needy out of the dunghill;
\p
\v 8 That he may set \add him\add* with princes, \add even\add* with the princes of his people.
\p
\v 9 He maketh the barren woman to keep house, \add and to be\add* a joyful mother of children. Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*.\f + \fr 113:9 \fr*\fq to keep… \fq*\ft - Heb. to dwell in an house\ft*\f*
\c 114
\p
\v 1 When Israel went out of Egypt, the house of Jacob from a people of strange language;
\p
\v 2 Judah was his sanctuary, \add and\add* Israel his dominion.
\p
\v 3 The sea saw \add it\add*, and fled: Jordan was driven back.
\p
\v 4 The mountains skipped like rams, \add and\add* the little hills like lambs.
\p
\v 5 What \add ailed\add* thee, O thou sea, that thou fleddest? thou Jordan, \add that\add* thou wast driven back?
\p
\v 6 Ye mountains, \add that\add* ye skipped like rams; \add and\add* ye little hills, like lambs?
\p
\v 7 Tremble, thou earth, at the presence of the Lord, at the presence of the God of Jacob;
\p
\v 8 Which turned the rock \add into\add* a standing water, the flint into a fountain of waters.
\c 115
\p
\v 1 Not unto us, O \nd LORD\nd*, not unto us, but unto thy name give glory, for thy mercy, \add and\add* for thy truth’s sake.
\p
\v 2 Wherefore should the heathen say, Where \add is\add* now their God?
\p
\v 3 But our God \add is\add* in the heavens: he hath done whatsoever he hath pleased.
\p
\v 4 Their idols \add are\add* silver and gold, the work of men’s hands.
\p
\v 5 They have mouths, but they speak not: eyes have they, but they see not:
\p
\v 6 They have ears, but they hear not: noses have they, but they smell not:
\p
\v 7 They have hands, but they handle not: feet have they, but they walk not: neither speak they through their throat.
\p
\v 8 They that make them are like unto them; \add so is\add* every one that trusteth in them.
\p
\v 9 O Israel, trust thou in the \nd LORD\nd*: he \add is\add* their help and their shield.
\p
\v 10 O house of Aaron, trust in the \nd LORD\nd*: he \add is\add* their help and their shield.
\p
\v 11 Ye that fear the \nd LORD\nd*, trust in the \nd LORD\nd*: he \add is\add* their help and their shield.
\p
\v 12 The \nd LORD\nd* hath been mindful of us: he will bless \add us;\add* he will bless the house of Israel; he will bless the house of Aaron.
\p
\v 13 He will bless them that fear the \nd LORD\nd*, \add both\add* small and great.\f + \fr 115:13 \fr*\fq and \fq*\ft - Heb. with\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 The \nd LORD\nd* shall increase you more and more, you and your children.
\p
\v 15 Ye \add are\add* blessed of the \nd LORD\nd* which made heaven and earth.
\p
\v 16 The heaven, \add even\add* the heavens, \add are\add* the \nd LORD’s\nd*: but the earth hath he given to the children of men.
\p
\v 17 The dead praise not the \nd LORD\nd*, neither any that go down into silence.
\p
\v 18 But we will bless the \nd LORD\nd* from this time forth and for evermore. Praise the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 116
\p
\v 1 I love the \nd LORD\nd*, because he hath heard my voice \add and\add* my supplications.
\p
\v 2 Because he hath inclined his ear unto me, therefore will I call upon \add him\add* as long as I live.\f + \fr 116:2 \fr*\fq as long… \fq*\ft - Heb. in my days\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 The sorrows of death compassed me, and the pains of hell gat hold upon me: I found trouble and sorrow.\f + \fr 116:3 \fr*\fq gat… \fq*\ft - Heb. found me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Then called I upon the name of the \nd LORD\nd*; O \nd LORD\nd*, I beseech thee, deliver my soul.
\p
\v 5 Gracious \add is\add* the \nd LORD\nd*, and righteous; yea, our God \add is\add* merciful.
\p
\v 6 The \nd LORD\nd* preserveth the simple: I was brought low, and he helped me.
\p
\v 7 Return unto thy rest, O my soul; for the \nd LORD\nd* hath dealt bountifully with thee.
\p
\v 8 For thou hast delivered my soul from death, mine eyes from tears, \add and\add* my feet from falling.
\p
\v 9 I will walk before the \nd LORD\nd* in the land of the living.
\p
\v 10 I believed, therefore have I spoken: I was greatly afflicted:
\p
\v 11 I said in my haste, All men \add are\add* liars.
\p
\v 12 What shall I render unto the \nd LORD\nd* \add for\add* all his benefits toward me?
\p
\v 13 I will take the cup of salvation, and call upon the name of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 14 I will pay my vows unto the \nd LORD\nd* now in the presence of all his people.
\p
\v 15 Precious in the sight of the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* the death of his saints.
\p
\v 16 O \nd LORD\nd*, truly I \add am\add* thy servant; I \add am\add* thy servant, \add and\add* the son of thine handmaid: thou hast loosed my bonds.
\p
\v 17 I will offer to thee the sacrifice of thanksgiving, and will call upon the name of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 18 I will pay my vows unto the \nd LORD\nd* now in the presence of all his people,
\p
\v 19 In the courts of the \nd LORD’s\nd* house, in the midst of thee, O Jerusalem. Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 117
\p
\v 1 O praise the \nd LORD\nd*, all ye nations: praise him, all ye people.
\p
\v 2 For his merciful kindness is great toward us: and the truth of the \nd LORD\nd* \add endureth\add* for ever. Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 118
\p
\v 1 O give thanks unto the \nd LORD\nd*; for \add he is\add* good: because his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 2 Let Israel now say, that his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 3 Let the house of Aaron now say, that his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 4 Let them now that fear the \nd LORD\nd* say, that his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 5 I called upon the \nd LORD\nd* in distress: the \nd LORD\nd* answered me, \add and set me\add* in a large place.\f + \fr 118:5 \fr*\fq in distress \fq*\ft - Heb. out of distress\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* on my side; I will not fear: what can man do unto me?\f + \fr 118:6 \fr*\fq on… \fq*\ft - Heb. for me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 The \nd LORD\nd* taketh my part with them that help me: therefore shall I see \add my desire\add* upon them that hate me.
\p
\v 8 \add It is\add* better to trust in the \nd LORD\nd* than to put confidence in man.
\p
\v 9 \add It is\add* better to trust in the \nd LORD\nd* than to put confidence in princes.
\p
\v 10 All nations compassed me about: but in the name of the \nd LORD\nd* will I destroy them.\f + \fr 118:10 \fr*\fq destroy… \fq*\ft - Heb. cut them off\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 They compassed me about; yea, they compassed me about: but in the name of the \nd LORD\nd* I will destroy them.
\p
\v 12 They compassed me about like bees; they are quenched as the fire of thorns: for in the name of the \nd LORD\nd* I will destroy them.\f + \fr 118:12 \fr*\fq destroy \fq*\ft - Heb. cut down\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 Thou hast thrust sore at me that I might fall: but the \nd LORD\nd* helped me.
\p
\v 14 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* my strength and song, and is become my salvation.
\p
\v 15 The voice of rejoicing and salvation \add is\add* in the tabernacles of the righteous: the right hand of the \nd LORD\nd* doeth valiantly.
\p
\v 16 The right hand of the \nd LORD\nd* is exalted: the right hand of the \nd LORD\nd* doeth valiantly.
\p
\v 17 I shall not die, but live, and declare the works of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 18 The \nd LORD\nd* hath chastened me sore: but he hath not given me over unto death.
\p
\v 19 Open to me the gates of righteousness: I will go into them, \add and\add* I will praise the \nd LORD\nd*:
\p
\v 20 This gate of the \nd LORD\nd*, into which the righteous shall enter.
\p
\v 21 I will praise thee: for thou hast heard me, and art become my salvation.
\p
\v 22 The stone \add which\add* the builders refused is become the head \add stone\add* of the corner.
\p
\v 23 This is the \nd LORD’s\nd* doing; it \add is\add* marvellous in our eyes.\f + \fr 118:23 \fr*\ft the\ft*\f*
\p
\v 24 This \add is\add* the day \add which\add* the \nd LORD\nd* hath made; we will rejoice and be glad in it.
\p
\v 25 Save now, I beseech thee, O \nd LORD\nd*: O \nd LORD\nd*, I beseech thee, send now prosperity.
\p
\v 26 Blessed \add be\add* he that cometh in the name of the \nd LORD\nd*: we have blessed you out of the house of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 27 God \add is\add* the \nd LORD\nd*, which hath shewed us light: bind the sacrifice with cords, \add even\add* unto the horns of the altar.
\p
\v 28 Thou \add art\add* my God, and I will praise thee: \add thou art\add* my God, I will exalt thee.
\p
\v 29 O give thanks unto the \nd LORD\nd*; for \add he is\add* good: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\c 119
\qa א ALEPH.
\p
\v 1 Blessed \add are\add* the undefiled in the way, who walk in the law of the \nd LORD\nd*.\f + \fr 119:1 \fr*\fq undefiled \fq*\ft - or, perfect, or, sincere\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Blessed \add are\add* they that keep his testimonies, \add and that\add* seek him with the whole heart.
\p
\v 3 They also do no iniquity: they walk in his ways.
\p
\v 4 Thou hast commanded \add us\add* to keep thy precepts diligently.
\p
\v 5 O that my ways were directed to keep thy statutes!
\p
\v 6 Then shall I not be ashamed, when I have respect unto all thy commandments.
\p
\v 7 I will praise thee with uprightness of heart, when I shall have learned thy righteous judgments.\f + \fr 119:7 \fr*\fq thy… \fq*\ft - Heb. judgments of thy righteousness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 I will keep thy statutes: O forsake me not utterly.
\qa ב BETH.
\p
\v 9 Wherewithal shall a young man cleanse his way? by taking heed \add thereto\add* according to thy word.
\p
\v 10 With my whole heart have I sought thee: O let me not wander from thy commandments.
\p
\v 11 Thy word have I hid in mine heart, that I might not sin against thee.
\p
\v 12 Blessed \add art\add* thou, O \nd LORD\nd*: teach me thy statutes.
\p
\v 13 With my lips have I declared all the judgments of thy mouth.
\p
\v 14 I have rejoiced in the way of thy testimonies, as \add much as\add* in all riches.
\p
\v 15 I will meditate in thy precepts, and have respect unto thy ways.
\p
\v 16 I will delight myself in thy statutes: I will not forget thy word.
\qa ג GIMEL.
\p
\v 17 Deal bountifully with thy servant, \add that\add* I may live, and keep thy word.
\p
\v 18 Open thou mine eyes, that I may behold wondrous things out of thy law.\f + \fr 119:18 \fr*\fq Open \fq*\ft - Heb. Reveal\ft*\f*
\p
\v 19 I \add am\add* a stranger in the earth: hide not thy commandments from me.
\p
\v 20 My soul breaketh for the longing \add that it hath\add* unto thy judgments at all times.
\p
\v 21 Thou hast rebuked the proud \add that are\add* cursed, which do err from thy commandments.
\p
\v 22 Remove from me reproach and contempt; for I have kept thy testimonies.
\p
\v 23 Princes also did sit \add and\add* speak against me: \add but\add* thy servant did meditate in thy statutes.
\p
\v 24 Thy testimonies also \add are\add* my delight \add and\add* my counsellors.\f + \fr 119:24 \fr*\fq my counsellors \fq*\ft - Heb. men of my counsel\ft*\f*
\qa ד DALETH.
\p
\v 25 My soul cleaveth unto the dust: quicken thou me according to thy word.
\p
\v 26 I have declared my ways, and thou heardest me: teach me thy statutes.
\p
\v 27 Make me to understand the way of thy precepts: so shall I talk of thy wondrous works.
\p
\v 28 My soul melteth for heaviness: strengthen thou me according unto thy word.\f + \fr 119:28 \fr*\fq melteth \fq*\ft - Heb. droppeth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 29 Remove from me the way of lying: and grant me thy law graciously.
\p
\v 30 I have chosen the way of truth: thy judgments have I laid \add before me\add*.
\p
\v 31 I have stuck unto thy testimonies: O \nd LORD\nd*, put me not to shame.
\p
\v 32 I will run the way of thy commandments, when thou shalt enlarge my heart.
\qa ה HE.
\p
\v 33 Teach me, O \nd LORD\nd*, the way of thy statutes; and I shall keep it \add unto\add* the end.
\p
\v 34 Give me understanding, and I shall keep thy law; yea, I shall observe it with \add my\add* whole heart.
\p
\v 35 Make me to go in the path of thy commandments; for therein do I delight.
\p
\v 36 Incline my heart unto thy testimonies, and not to covetousness.
\p
\v 37 Turn away mine eyes from beholding vanity; \add and\add* quicken thou me in thy way.\f + \fr 119:37 \fr*\fq Turn… \fq*\ft - Heb. Make to pass\ft*\f*
\p
\v 38 Stablish thy word unto thy servant, who \add is devoted\add* to thy fear.
\p
\v 39 Turn away my reproach which I fear: for thy judgments \add are\add* good.
\p
\v 40 Behold, I have longed after thy precepts: quicken me in thy righteousness.
\qa ו VAU.
\p
\v 41 Let thy mercies come also unto me, O \nd LORD\nd*, \add even\add* thy salvation, according to thy word.
\p
\v 42 So shall I have wherewith to answer him that reproacheth me: for I trust in thy word.\f + \fr 119:42 \fr*\fq So… \fq*\ft - or, So shall I answer him that reproveth me in a thing\ft*\f*
\p
\v 43 And take not the word of truth utterly out of my mouth; for I have hoped in thy judgments.
\p
\v 44 So shall I keep thy law continually for ever and ever.
\p
\v 45 And I will walk at liberty: for I seek thy precepts.\f + \fr 119:45 \fr*\fq at liberty \fq*\ft - Heb. at large\ft*\f*
\p
\v 46 I will speak of thy testimonies also before kings, and will not be ashamed.
\p
\v 47 And I will delight myself in thy commandments, which I have loved.
\p
\v 48 My hands also will I lift up unto thy commandments, which I have loved; and I will meditate in thy statutes.
\qa ז ZAIN.
\p
\v 49 Remember the word unto thy servant, upon which thou hast caused me to hope.
\p
\v 50 This \add is\add* my comfort in my affliction: for thy word hath quickened me.
\p
\v 51 The proud have had me greatly in derision: \add yet\add* have I not declined from thy law.
\p
\v 52 I remembered thy judgments of old, O \nd LORD\nd*; and have comforted myself.
\p
\v 53 Horror hath taken hold upon me because of the wicked that forsake thy law.
\p
\v 54 Thy statutes have been my songs in the house of my pilgrimage.
\p
\v 55 I have remembered thy name, O \nd LORD\nd*, in the night, and have kept thy law.
\p
\v 56 This I had, because I kept thy precepts.
\qa ח CHETH.
\p
\v 57 \add Thou art\add* my portion, O \nd LORD\nd*: I have said that I would keep thy words.
\p
\v 58 I intreated thy favour with \add my\add* whole heart: be merciful unto me according to thy word.\f + \fr 119:58 \fr*\fq favour \fq*\ft - Heb. face\ft*\f*
\p
\v 59 I thought on my ways, and turned my feet unto thy testimonies.
\p
\v 60 I made haste, and delayed not to keep thy commandments.
\p
\v 61 The bands of the wicked have robbed me: \add but\add* I have not forgotten thy law.\f + \fr 119:61 \fr*\fq bands \fq*\ft - or, companies\ft*\f*
\p
\v 62 At midnight I will rise to give thanks unto thee because of thy righteous judgments.
\p
\v 63 I \add am\add* a companion of all \add them\add* that fear thee, and of them that keep thy precepts.
\p
\v 64 The earth, O \nd LORD\nd*, is full of thy mercy: teach me thy statutes.
\qa ט TETH.
\p
\v 65 Thou hast dealt well with thy servant, O \nd LORD\nd*, according unto thy word.
\p
\v 66 Teach me good judgment and knowledge: for I have believed thy commandments.
\p
\v 67 Before I was afflicted I went astray: but now have I kept thy word.
\p
\v 68 Thou \add art\add* good, and doest good; teach me thy statutes.
\p
\v 69 The proud have forged a lie against me: \add but\add* I will keep thy precepts with \add my\add* whole heart.
\p
\v 70 Their heart is as fat as grease; \add but\add* I delight in thy law.
\p
\v 71 \add It is\add* good for me that I have been afflicted; that I might learn thy statutes.
\p
\v 72 The law of thy mouth \add is\add* better unto me than thousands of gold and silver.
\qa י JOD.
\p
\v 73 Thy hands have made me and fashioned me: give me understanding, that I may learn thy commandments.
\p
\v 74 They that fear thee will be glad when they see me; because I have hoped in thy word.
\p
\v 75 I know, O \nd LORD\nd*, that thy judgments \add are\add* right, and \add that\add* thou in faithfulness hast afflicted me.\f + \fr 119:75 \fr*\fq right \fq*\ft - Heb. righteousness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 76 Let, I pray thee, thy merciful kindness be for my comfort, according to thy word unto thy servant.\f + \fr 119:76 \fr*\fq for… \fq*\ft - Heb. to comfort me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 77 Let thy tender mercies come unto me, that I may live: for thy law \add is\add* my delight.
\p
\v 78 Let the proud be ashamed; for they dealt perversely with me without a cause: \add but\add* I will meditate in thy precepts.
\p
\v 79 Let those that fear thee turn unto me, and those that have known thy testimonies.
\p
\v 80 Let my heart be sound in thy statutes; that I be not ashamed.
\qa כ CAPH.
\p
\v 81 My soul fainteth for thy salvation: \add but\add* I hope in thy word.
\p
\v 82 Mine eyes fail for thy word, saying, When wilt thou comfort me?
\p
\v 83 For I am become like a bottle in the smoke; \add yet\add* do I not forget thy statutes.
\p
\v 84 How many \add are\add* the days of thy servant? when wilt thou execute judgment on them that persecute me?
\p
\v 85 The proud have digged pits for me, which \add are\add* not after thy law.
\p
\v 86 All thy commandments \add are\add* faithful: they persecute me wrongfully; help thou me.\f + \fr 119:86 \fr*\fq faithful \fq*\ft - Heb. faithfulness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 87 They had almost consumed me upon earth; but I forsook not thy precepts.
\p
\v 88 Quicken me after thy lovingkindness; so shall I keep the testimony of thy mouth.
\qa ל LAMED.
\p
\v 89 For ever, O \nd LORD\nd*, thy word is settled in heaven.
\p
\v 90 Thy faithfulness \add is\add* unto all generations: thou hast established the earth, and it abideth.\f + \fr 119:90 \fr*\fq unto… \fq*\ft - Heb. to generation and generation\ft*\f*\f + \fr 119:90 \fr*\fq abideth \fq*\ft - Heb. standeth\ft*\f*
\p
\v 91 They continue this day according to thine ordinances: for all \add are\add* thy servants.
\p
\v 92 Unless thy law \add had been\add* my delights, I should then have perished in mine affliction.
\p
\v 93 I will never forget thy precepts: for with them thou hast quickened me.
\p
\v 94 I \add am\add* thine, save me; for I have sought thy precepts.
\p
\v 95 The wicked have waited for me to destroy me: \add but\add* I will consider thy testimonies.
\p
\v 96 I have seen an end of all perfection: \add but\add* thy commandment \add is\add* exceeding broad.
\qa מ MEM.
\p
\v 97 O how love I thy law! it \add is\add* my meditation all the day.
\p
\v 98 Thou through thy commandments hast made me wiser than mine enemies: for they \add are\add* ever with me.\f + \fr 119:98 \fr*\fq they… \fq*\ft - Heb. it is ever with me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 99 I have more understanding than all my teachers: for thy testimonies \add are\add* my meditation.
\p
\v 100 I understand more than the ancients, because I keep thy precepts.
\p
\v 101 I have refrained my feet from every evil way, that I might keep thy word.
\p
\v 102 I have not departed from thy judgments: for thou hast taught me.
\p
\v 103 How sweet are thy words unto my taste! \add yea, sweeter\add* than honey to my mouth!\f + \fr 119:103 \fr*\fq taste \fq*\ft - Heb. palate\ft*\f*
\p
\v 104 Through thy precepts I get understanding: therefore I hate every false way.
\qa נ NUN.
\p
\v 105 Thy word \add is\add* a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path.\f + \fr 119:105 \fr*\fq lamp \fq*\ft - or, candle\ft*\f*
\p
\v 106 I have sworn, and I will perform \add it\add*, that I will keep thy righteous judgments.
\p
\v 107 I am afflicted very much: quicken me, O \nd LORD\nd*, according unto thy word.
\p
\v 108 Accept, I beseech thee, the freewill offerings of my mouth, O \nd LORD\nd*, and teach me thy judgments.
\p
\v 109 My soul \add is\add* continually in my hand: yet do I not forget thy law.
\p
\v 110 The wicked have laid a snare for me: yet I erred not from thy precepts.
\p
\v 111 Thy testimonies have I taken as an heritage for ever: for they \add are\add* the rejoicing of my heart.
\p
\v 112 I have inclined mine heart to perform thy statutes alway, \add even unto\add* the end.\f + \fr 119:112 \fr*\fq to perform \fq*\ft - Heb. to do\ft*\f*
\qa ס SAMECH.
\p
\v 113 I hate \add vain\add* thoughts: but thy law do I love.
\p
\v 114 Thou \add art\add* my hiding place and my shield: I hope in thy word.
\p
\v 115 Depart from me, ye evildoers: for I will keep the commandments of my God.
\p
\v 116 Uphold me according unto thy word, that I may live: and let me not be ashamed of my hope.
\p
\v 117 Hold thou me up, and I shall be safe: and I will have respect unto thy statutes continually.
\p
\v 118 Thou hast trodden down all them that err from thy statutes: for their deceit \add is\add* falsehood.
\p
\v 119 Thou puttest away all the wicked of the earth \add like\add* dross: therefore I love thy testimonies.\f + \fr 119:119 \fr*\fq puttest… \fq*\ft - Heb. causest to cease\ft*\f*
\p
\v 120 My flesh trembleth for fear of thee; and I am afraid of thy judgments.
\qa ע AIN.
\p
\v 121 I have done judgment and justice: leave me not to mine oppressors.
\p
\v 122 Be surety for thy servant for good: let not the proud oppress me.
\p
\v 123 Mine eyes fail for thy salvation, and for the word of thy righteousness.
\p
\v 124 Deal with thy servant according unto thy mercy, and teach me thy statutes.
\p
\v 125 I \add am\add* thy servant; give me understanding, that I may know thy testimonies.
\p
\v 126 \add It is\add* time for \add thee\add*, \nd LORD\nd*, to work: \add for\add* they have made void thy law.
\p
\v 127 Therefore I love thy commandments above gold; yea, above fine gold.
\p
\v 128 Therefore I esteem all \add thy\add* precepts \add concerning\add* all \add things to be\add* right; \add and\add* I hate every false way.
\qa פ PE.
\p
\v 129 Thy testimonies \add are\add* wonderful: therefore doth my soul keep them.
\p
\v 130 The entrance of thy words giveth light; it giveth understanding unto the simple.
\p
\v 131 I opened my mouth, and panted: for I longed for thy commandments.
\p
\v 132 Look thou upon me, and be merciful unto me, as thou usest to do unto those that love thy name.\f + \fr 119:132 \fr*\fq as thou… \fq*\ft - Heb. according to the custom toward those, etc\ft*\f*
\p
\v 133 Order my steps in thy word: and let not any iniquity have dominion over me.
\p
\v 134 Deliver me from the oppression of man: so will I keep thy precepts.
\p
\v 135 Make thy face to shine upon thy servant; and teach me thy statutes.
\p
\v 136 Rivers of waters run down mine eyes, because they keep not thy law.
\qa צ TZADDI.
\p
\v 137 Righteous \add art\add* thou, O \nd LORD\nd*, and upright \add are\add* thy judgments.
\p
\v 138 Thy testimonies \add that\add* thou hast commanded \add are\add* righteous and very faithful.\f + \fr 119:138 \fr*\fq righteous \fq*\ft - Heb. righteousness\ft*\f*\f + \fr 119:138 \fr*\fq faithful \fq*\ft - Heb. faithfulness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 139 My zeal hath consumed me, because mine enemies have forgotten thy words.\f + \fr 119:139 \fr*\fq consumed… \fq*\ft - Heb. cut me off\ft*\f*
\p
\v 140 Thy word \add is\add* very pure: therefore thy servant loveth it.\f + \fr 119:140 \fr*\fq pure \fq*\ft - Heb. tried, or, refined\ft*\f*
\p
\v 141 I \add am\add* small and despised: \add yet\add* do not I forget thy precepts.
\p
\v 142 Thy righteousness \add is\add* an everlasting righteousness, and thy law \add is\add* the truth.
\p
\v 143 Trouble and anguish have taken hold on me: \add yet\add* thy commandments \add are\add* my delights.\f + \fr 119:143 \fr*\fq taken… \fq*\ft - Heb. found me\ft*\f*
\p
\v 144 The righteousness of thy testimonies \add is\add* everlasting: give me understanding, and I shall live.
\qa ק KOPH.
\p
\v 145 I cried with \add my\add* whole heart; hear me, O \nd LORD\nd*: I will keep thy statutes.
\p
\v 146 I cried unto thee; save me, and I shall keep thy testimonies.\f + \fr 119:146 \fr*\fq and I… \fq*\ft - or, that I may keep\ft*\f*
\p
\v 147 I prevented the dawning of the morning, and cried: I hoped in thy word.
\p
\v 148 Mine eyes prevent the \add night\add* watches, that I might meditate in thy word.
\p
\v 149 Hear my voice according unto thy lovingkindness: O \nd LORD\nd*, quicken me according to thy judgment.
\p
\v 150 They draw nigh that follow after mischief: they are far from thy law.
\p
\v 151 Thou \add art\add* near, O \nd LORD\nd*; and all thy commandments \add are\add* truth.
\p
\v 152 Concerning thy testimonies, I have known of old that thou hast founded them for ever.
\qa ר RESH.
\p
\v 153 Consider mine affliction, and deliver me: for I do not forget thy law.
\p
\v 154 Plead my cause, and deliver me: quicken me according to thy word.
\p
\v 155 Salvation \add is\add* far from the wicked: for they seek not thy statutes.
\p
\v 156 Great \add are\add* thy tender mercies, O \nd LORD\nd*: quicken me according to thy judgments.\f + \fr 119:156 \fr*\fq Great \fq*\ft - or, Many\ft*\f*
\p
\v 157 Many \add are\add* my persecutors and mine enemies; \add yet\add* do I not decline from thy testimonies.
\p
\v 158 I beheld the transgressors, and was grieved; because they kept not thy word.
\p
\v 159 Consider how I love thy precepts: quicken me, O \nd LORD\nd*, according to thy lovingkindness.
\p
\v 160 Thy word \add is\add* true \add from\add* the beginning: and every one of thy righteous judgments \add endureth\add* for ever.\f + \fr 119:160 \fr*\fq Thy word… \fq*\ft - Heb. The beginning of thy word is true\ft*\f*
\qa ש SCHIN.
\p
\v 161 Princes have persecuted me without a cause: but my heart standeth in awe of thy word.
\p
\v 162 I rejoice at thy word, as one that findeth great spoil.
\p
\v 163 I hate and abhor lying: \add but\add* thy law do I love.
\p
\v 164 Seven times a day do I praise thee because of thy righteous judgments.
\p
\v 165 Great peace have they which love thy law: and nothing shall offend them.\f + \fr 119:165 \fr*\fq nothing… \fq*\ft - Heb. they shall have no stumblingblock\ft*\f*
\p
\v 166 \nd LORD\nd*, I have hoped for thy salvation, and done thy commandments.
\p
\v 167 My soul hath kept thy testimonies; and I love them exceedingly.
\p
\v 168 I have kept thy precepts and thy testimonies: for all my ways \add are\add* before thee.
\qa ת TAU.
\p
\v 169 Let my cry come near before thee, O \nd LORD\nd*: give me understanding according to thy word.
\p
\v 170 Let my supplication come before thee: deliver me according to thy word.
\p
\v 171 My lips shall utter praise, when thou hast taught me thy statutes.
\p
\v 172 My tongue shall speak of thy word: for all thy commandments \add are\add* righteousness.
\p
\v 173 Let thine hand help me; for I have chosen thy precepts.
\p
\v 174 I have longed for thy salvation, O \nd LORD\nd*; and thy law \add is\add* my delight.
\p
\v 175 Let my soul live, and it shall praise thee; and let thy judgments help me.
\p
\v 176 I have gone astray like a lost sheep; seek thy servant; for I do not forget thy commandments.
\c 120
\d A Song of degrees.
\p
\v 1 In my distress I cried unto the \nd LORD\nd*, and he heard me.
\p
\v 2 Deliver my soul, O \nd LORD\nd*, from lying lips, \add and\add* from a deceitful tongue.
\p
\v 3 What shall be given unto thee? or what shall be done unto thee, thou false tongue?\f + \fr 120:3 \fr*\fq What shall be given… \fq*\ft - or, What shall the deceitful tongue give unto thee? or, what shall is profit thee?\ft*\f*\f + \fr 120:3 \fr*\fq done \fq*\ft - Heb. added\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Sharp arrows of the mighty, with coals of juniper.\f + \fr 120:4 \fr*\fq Sharp… \fq*\ft - or, It is as the sharp arrows of the mighty man, with coals of juniper\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 Woe is me, that I sojourn in Mesech, \add that\add* I dwell in the tents of Kedar!
\p
\v 6 My soul hath long dwelt with him that hateth peace.
\p
\v 7 I \add am for\add* peace: but when I speak, they \add are\add* for war.\f + \fr 120:7 \fr*\fq for peace \fq*\ft - or, a man of peace\ft*\f*
\c 121
\d A Song of degrees.
\p
\v 1 I will lift up mine eyes unto the hills, from whence cometh my help.\f + \fr 121:1 \fr*\fq I will… \fq*\ft - or, Shall I lift up mine eyes to the hills? whence should my help come?\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 My help \add cometh\add* from the \nd LORD\nd*, which made heaven and earth.
\p
\v 3 He will not suffer thy foot to be moved: he that keepeth thee will not slumber.
\p
\v 4 Behold, he that keepeth Israel shall neither slumber nor sleep.
\p
\v 5 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* thy keeper: the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* thy shade upon thy right hand.
\p
\v 6 The sun shall not smite thee by day, nor the moon by night.
\p
\v 7 The \nd LORD\nd* shall preserve thee from all evil: he shall preserve thy soul.
\p
\v 8 The \nd LORD\nd* shall preserve thy going out and thy coming in from this time forth, and even for evermore.
\c 122
\d A Song of degrees of David.
\p
\v 1 I was glad when they said unto me, Let us go into the house of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 2 Our feet shall stand within thy gates, O Jerusalem.
\p
\v 3 Jerusalem is builded as a city that is compact together:
\p
\v 4 Whither the tribes go up, the tribes of the \nd LORD\nd*, unto the testimony of Israel, to give thanks unto the name of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 5 For there are set thrones of judgment, the thrones of the house of David.\f + \fr 122:5 \fr*\fq are… \fq*\ft - Heb. do sit\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Pray for the peace of Jerusalem: they shall prosper that love thee.
\p
\v 7 Peace be within thy walls, \add and\add* prosperity within thy palaces.
\p
\v 8 For my brethren and companions’ sakes, I will now say, Peace \add be\add* within thee.
\p
\v 9 Because of the house of the \nd LORD\nd* our God I will seek thy good.
\c 123
\d A Song of degrees.
\p
\v 1 Unto thee lift I up mine eyes, O thou that dwellest in the heavens.
\p
\v 2 Behold, as the eyes of servants \add look\add* unto the hand of their masters, \add and\add* as the eyes of a maiden unto the hand of her mistress; so our eyes \add wait\add* upon the \nd LORD\nd* our God, until that he have mercy upon us.
\p
\v 3 Have mercy upon us, O \nd LORD\nd*, have mercy upon us: for we are exceedingly filled with contempt.
\p
\v 4 Our soul is exceedingly filled with the scorning of those that are at ease, \add and\add* with the contempt of the proud.
\c 124
\d A Song of degrees of David.
\p
\v 1 If \add it had not been\add* the \nd LORD\nd* who was on our side, now may Israel say;
\p
\v 2 If \add it had not been\add* the \nd LORD\nd* who was on our side, when men rose up against us:
\p
\v 3 Then they had swallowed us up quick, when their wrath was kindled against us:
\p
\v 4 Then the waters had overwhelmed us, the stream had gone over our soul:
\p
\v 5 Then the proud waters had gone over our soul.
\p
\v 6 Blessed \add be\add* the \nd LORD\nd*, who hath not given us \add as\add* a prey to their teeth.
\p
\v 7 Our soul is escaped as a bird out of the snare of the fowlers: the snare is broken, and we are escaped.
\p
\v 8 Our help \add is\add* in the name of the \nd LORD\nd*, who made heaven and earth.
\c 125
\d A Song of degrees.
\p
\v 1 They that trust in the \nd LORD\nd* \add shall be\add* as mount Zion, \add which\add* cannot be removed, \add but\add* abideth for ever.
\p
\v 2 As the mountains \add are\add* round about Jerusalem, so the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* round about his people from henceforth even for ever.
\p
\v 3 For the rod of the wicked shall not rest upon the lot of the righteous; lest the righteous put forth their hands unto iniquity.\f + \fr 125:3 \fr*\fq the wicked \fq*\ft - Heb. wickedness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Do good, O \nd LORD\nd*, unto \add those that be\add* good, and \add to them that are\add* upright in their hearts.
\p
\v 5 As for such as turn aside unto their crooked ways, the \nd LORD\nd* shall lead them forth with the workers of iniquity: \add but\add* peace \add shall be\add* upon Israel.
\c 126
\d A Song of degrees.
\p
\v 1 When the \nd LORD\nd* turned again the captivity of Zion, we were like them that dream.\f + \fr 126:1 \fr*\fq turned… \fq*\ft - Heb. returned the returning\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Then was our mouth filled with laughter, and our tongue with singing: then said they among the heathen, The \nd LORD\nd* hath done great things for them.\f + \fr 126:2 \fr*\fq hath… \fq*\ft - Heb. hath magnified to do with them\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 The \nd LORD\nd* hath done great things for us; \add whereof\add* we are glad.
\p
\v 4 Turn again our captivity, O \nd LORD\nd*, as the streams in the south.
\p
\v 5 They that sow in tears shall reap in joy.\f + \fr 126:5 \fr*\fq joy \fq*\ft - or, singing\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 He that goeth forth and weepeth, bearing precious seed, shall doubtless come again with rejoicing, bringing his sheaves \add with him\add*.\f + \fr 126:6 \fr*\fq precious… \fq*\ft - or, seed basket\ft*\f*
\c 127
\d A Song of degrees for Solomon.
\p
\v 1 Except the \nd LORD\nd* build the house, they labour in vain that build it: except the \nd LORD\nd* keep the city, the watchman waketh \add but\add* in vain.\f + \fr 127:1 \fr*\fq for… \fq*\ft - or, of Solomon\ft*\f*\f + \fr 127:1 \fr*\fq that… \fq*\ft - Heb. that are builders of it in it\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 \add It is\add* vain for you to rise up early, to sit up late, to eat the bread of sorrows: \add for\add* so he giveth his beloved sleep.
\p
\v 3 Lo, children \add are\add* an heritage of the \nd LORD\nd*: \add and\add* the fruit of the womb \add is his\add* reward.
\p
\v 4 As arrows \add are\add* in the hand of a mighty man; so \add are\add* children of the youth.
\p
\v 5 Happy \add is\add* the man that hath his quiver full of them: they shall not be ashamed, but they shall speak with the enemies in the gate.\f + \fr 127:5 \fr*\fq his… \fq*\ft - Heb. filled his quiver with them\ft*\f*\f + \fr 127:5 \fr*\fq speak… \fq*\ft - or, subdue, or, destroy\ft*\f*
\c 128
\d A Song of degrees.
\p
\v 1 Blessed \add is\add* every one that feareth the \nd LORD\nd*; that walketh in his ways.
\p
\v 2 For thou shalt eat the labour of thine hands: happy \add shalt\add* thou \add be\add*, and \add it shall be\add* well with thee.
\p
\v 3 Thy wife \add shall be\add* as a fruitful vine by the sides of thine house: thy children like olive plants round about thy table.
\p
\v 4 Behold, that thus shall the man be blessed that feareth the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 5 The \nd LORD\nd* shall bless thee out of Zion: and thou shalt see the good of Jerusalem all the days of thy life.
\p
\v 6 Yea, thou shalt see thy children’s children, \add and\add* peace upon Israel.
\c 129
\d A Song of degrees.
\p
\v 1 Many a time have they afflicted me from my youth, may Israel now say:\f + \fr 129:1 \fr*\fq Many… \fq*\ft - or, Much\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Many a time have they afflicted me from my youth: yet they have not prevailed against me.\f + \fr 129:2 \fr*\fq Many… \fq*\ft - or, Much\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 The plowers plowed upon my back: they made long their furrows.
\p
\v 4 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* righteous: he hath cut asunder the cords of the wicked.
\p
\v 5 Let them all be confounded and turned back that hate Zion.
\p
\v 6 Let them be as the grass \add upon\add* the housetops, which withereth afore it groweth up:
\p
\v 7 Wherewith the mower filleth not his hand; nor he that bindeth sheaves his bosom.
\p
\v 8 Neither do they which go by say, The blessing of the \nd LORD\nd* \add be\add* upon you: we bless you in the name of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 130
\d A Song of degrees.
\p
\v 1 Out of the depths have I cried unto thee, O \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 2 Lord, hear my voice: let thine ears be attentive to the voice of my supplications.
\p
\v 3 If thou, \nd LORD\nd*, shouldest mark iniquities, O Lord, who shall stand?
\p
\v 4 But \add there is\add* forgiveness with thee, that thou mayest be feared.
\p
\v 5 I wait for the \nd LORD\nd*, my soul doth wait, and in his word do I hope.
\p
\v 6 My soul \add waiteth\add* for the Lord more than they that watch for the morning: \add I say, more than\add* they that watch for the morning.\f + \fr 130:6 \fr*\fq I say… \fq*\ft - or, which watch unto\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 Let Israel hope in the \nd LORD\nd*: for with the \nd LORD\nd* \add there is\add* mercy, and with him \add is\add* plenteous redemption.
\p
\v 8 And he shall redeem Israel from all his iniquities.
\c 131
\d A Song of degrees of David.
\p
\v 1 \nd LORD\nd*, my heart is not haughty, nor mine eyes lofty: neither do I exercise myself in great matters, or in things too high for me.\f + \fr 131:1 \fr*\fq exercise… \fq*\ft - Heb. walk\ft*\f*\f + \fr 131:1 \fr*\fq high \fq*\ft - Heb. wonderful\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Surely I have behaved and quieted myself, as a child that is weaned of his mother: my soul \add is\add* even as a weaned child.\f + \fr 131:2 \fr*\fq myself \fq*\ft - Heb. my soul\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 Let Israel hope in the \nd LORD\nd* from henceforth and for ever.\f + \fr 131:3 \fr*\fq henceforth \fq*\ft - Heb. now\ft*\f*
\c 132
\d A Song of degrees.
\p
\v 1 \nd LORD\nd*, remember David, \add and\add* all his afflictions:
\p
\v 2 How he sware unto the \nd LORD\nd*, \add and\add* vowed unto the mighty \add God\add* of Jacob;
\p
\v 3 Surely I will not come into the tabernacle of my house, nor go up into my bed;
\p
\v 4 I will not give sleep to mine eyes, \add or\add* slumber to mine eyelids,
\p
\v 5 Until I find out a place for the \nd LORD\nd*, an habitation for the mighty \add God\add* of Jacob.\f + \fr 132:5 \fr*\fq an habitation \fq*\ft - Heb. habitations\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 Lo, we heard of it at Ephratah: we found it in the fields of the wood.
\p
\v 7 We will go into his tabernacles: we will worship at his footstool.
\p
\v 8 Arise, O \nd LORD\nd*, into thy rest; thou, and the ark of thy strength.
\p
\v 9 Let thy priests be clothed with righteousness; and let thy saints shout for joy.
\p
\v 10 For thy servant David’s sake turn not away the face of thine anointed.
\p
\v 11 The \nd LORD\nd* hath sworn \add in\add* truth unto David; he will not turn from it; Of the fruit of thy body will I set upon thy throne.\f + \fr 132:11 \fr*\fq body \fq*\ft - Heb. belly\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 If thy children will keep my covenant and my testimony that I shall teach them, their children shall also sit upon thy throne for evermore.
\p
\v 13 For the \nd LORD\nd* hath chosen Zion; he hath desired \add it\add* for his habitation.
\p
\v 14 This \add is\add* my rest for ever: here will I dwell; for I have desired it.
\p
\v 15 I will abundantly bless her provision: I will satisfy her poor with bread.\f + \fr 132:15 \fr*\fq abundantly \fq*\ft - or, surely\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 I will also clothe her priests with salvation: and her saints shall shout aloud for joy.
\p
\v 17 There will I make the horn of David to bud: I have ordained a lamp for mine anointed.\f + \fr 132:17 \fr*\fq lamp \fq*\ft - or, candle\ft*\f*
\p
\v 18 His enemies will I clothe with shame: but upon himself shall his crown flourish.
\c 133
\d A Song of degrees of David.
\p
\v 1 Behold, how good and how pleasant \add it is\add* for brethren to dwell together in unity!\f + \fr 133:1 \fr*\fq together… \fq*\ft - Heb. even together\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 \add It is\add* like the precious ointment upon the head, that ran down upon the beard, \add even\add* Aaron’s beard: that went down to the skirts of his garments;
\p
\v 3 As the dew of Hermon, \add and as the dew\add* that descended upon the mountains of Zion: for there the \nd LORD\nd* commanded the blessing, \add even\add* life for evermore.
\c 134
\d A Song of degrees.
\p
\v 1 Behold, bless ye the \nd LORD\nd*, all \add ye\add* servants of the \nd LORD\nd*, which by night stand in the house of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 2 Lift up your hands \add in\add* the sanctuary, and bless the \nd LORD\nd*.\f + \fr 134:2 \fr*\fq the sanctuary \fq*\ft - or, holiness\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 The \nd LORD\nd* that made heaven and earth bless thee out of Zion.
\c 135
\p
\v 1 Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*. Praise ye the name of the \nd LORD\nd*; praise \add him\add*, O ye servants of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 2 Ye that stand in the house of the \nd LORD\nd*, in the courts of the house of our God,
\p
\v 3 Praise the \nd LORD\nd*; for the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* good: sing praises unto his name; for \add it is\add* pleasant.
\p
\v 4 For the \nd LORD\nd* hath chosen Jacob unto himself, \add and\add* Israel for his peculiar treasure.
\p
\v 5 For I know that the \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* great, and \add that\add* our Lord \add is\add* above all gods.
\p
\v 6 Whatsoever the \nd LORD\nd* pleased, \add that\add* did he in heaven, and in earth, in the seas, and all deep places.
\p
\v 7 He causeth the vapours to ascend from the ends of the earth; he maketh lightnings for the rain; he bringeth the wind out of his treasuries.
\p
\v 8 Who smote the firstborn of Egypt, both of man and beast.\f + \fr 135:8 \fr*\fq both… \fq*\ft - Heb. from man unto beast\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 \add Who\add* sent tokens and wonders into the midst of thee, O Egypt, upon Pharaoh, and upon all his servants.
\p
\v 10 Who smote great nations, and slew mighty kings;
\p
\v 11 Sihon king of the Amorites, and Og king of Bashan, and all the kingdoms of Canaan:
\p
\v 12 And gave their land \add for\add* an heritage, an heritage unto Israel his people.
\p
\v 13 Thy name, O \nd LORD\nd*, \add endureth\add* for ever; \add and\add* thy memorial, O \nd LORD\nd*, throughout all generations.\f + \fr 135:13 \fr*\fq throughout… \fq*\ft - Heb. to generation and generation\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 For the \nd LORD\nd* will judge his people, and he will repent himself concerning his servants.
\p
\v 15 The idols of the heathen \add are\add* silver and gold, the work of men’s hands.
\p
\v 16 They have mouths, but they speak not; eyes have they, but they see not;
\p
\v 17 They have ears, but they hear not; neither is there \add any\add* breath in their mouths.
\p
\v 18 They that make them are like unto them: \add so is\add* every one that trusteth in them.
\p
\v 19 Bless the \nd LORD\nd*, O house of Israel: bless the \nd LORD\nd*, O house of Aaron:
\p
\v 20 Bless the \nd LORD\nd*, O house of Levi: ye that fear the \nd LORD\nd*, bless the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 21 Blessed be the \nd LORD\nd* out of Zion, which dwelleth at Jerusalem. Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 136
\p
\v 1 O give thanks unto the \nd LORD\nd*; for \add he is\add* good: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 2 O give thanks unto the God of gods: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 3 O give thanks to the Lord of lords: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 4 To him who alone doeth great wonders: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 5 To him that by wisdom made the heavens: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 6 To him that stretched out the earth above the waters: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 7 To him that made great lights: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever:
\p
\v 8 The sun to rule by day: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever:\f + \fr 136:8 \fr*\fq to rule… \fq*\ft - Heb. for the rulings by day\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 The moon and stars to rule by night: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 10 To him that smote Egypt in their firstborn: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever:
\p
\v 11 And brought out Israel from among them: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever:
\p
\v 12 With a strong hand, and with a stretched out arm: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 13 To him which divided the Red sea into parts: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever:
\p
\v 14 And made Israel to pass through the midst of it: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever:
\p
\v 15 But overthrew Pharaoh and his host in the Red sea: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.\f + \fr 136:15 \fr*\fq overthrew \fq*\ft - Heb. shaked off\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 To him which led his people through the wilderness: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 17 To him which smote great kings: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever:
\p
\v 18 And slew famous kings: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever:
\p
\v 19 Sihon king of the Amorites: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever:
\p
\v 20 And Og the king of Bashan: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever:
\p
\v 21 And gave their land for an heritage: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever:
\p
\v 22 \add Even\add* an heritage unto Israel his servant: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 23 Who remembered us in our low estate: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever:
\p
\v 24 And hath redeemed us from our enemies: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 25 Who giveth food to all flesh: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\p
\v 26 O give thanks unto the God of heaven: for his mercy \add endureth\add* for ever.
\c 137
\p
\v 1 By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down, yea, we wept, when we remembered Zion.
\p
\v 2 We hanged our harps upon the willows in the midst thereof.
\p
\v 3 For there they that carried us away captive required of us a song; and they that wasted us \add required of us\add* mirth, \add saying\add*, Sing us \add one\add* of the songs of Zion.\f + \fr 137:3 \fr*\fq a song \fq*\ft - Heb. the words of a song\ft*\f*\f + \fr 137:3 \fr*\fq wasted… \fq*\ft - Heb. laid us on heaps\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 How shall we sing the \nd LORD’s\nd* song in a strange land?\f + \fr 137:4 \fr*\fq strange… \fq*\ft - Heb. land of a stranger?\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 If I forget thee, O Jerusalem, let my right hand forget \add her cunning\add*.
\p
\v 6 If I do not remember thee, let my tongue cleave to the roof of my mouth; if I prefer not Jerusalem above my chief joy.\f + \fr 137:6 \fr*\fq my chief… \fq*\ft - Heb. the head of my joy\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 Remember, O \nd LORD\nd*, the children of Edom in the day of Jerusalem; who said, Rase \add it\add*, rase \add it, even\add* to the foundation thereof.\f + \fr 137:7 \fr*\fq Rase it \fq*\ft - Heb. Make bare\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 O daughter of Babylon, who art to be destroyed; happy \add shall he be\add*, that rewardeth thee as thou hast served us.\f + \fr 137:8 \fr*\fq destroyed \fq*\ft - Heb. wasted\ft*\f*\f + \fr 137:8 \fr*\fq rewardeth… \fq*\ft - Heb. recompenseth unto thee thy deed which thou didst to us\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 Happy \add shall he be\add*, that taketh and dasheth thy little ones against the stones.\f + \fr 137:9 \fr*\fq the stones \fq*\ft - Heb. the rock\ft*\f*
\c 138
\d \add A Psalm\add* of David.
\p
\v 1 I will praise thee with my whole heart: before the gods will I sing praise unto thee.
\p
\v 2 I will worship toward thy holy temple, and praise thy name for thy lovingkindness and for thy truth: for thou hast magnified thy word above all thy name.
\p
\v 3 In the day when I cried thou answeredst me, \add and\add* strengthenedst me \add with\add* strength in my soul.
\p
\v 4 All the kings of the earth shall praise thee, O \nd LORD\nd*, when they hear the words of thy mouth.
\p
\v 5 Yea, they shall sing in the ways of the \nd LORD\nd*: for great \add is\add* the glory of the \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 6 Though the \nd LORD\nd* \add be\add* high, yet hath he respect unto the lowly: but the proud he knoweth afar off.
\p
\v 7 Though I walk in the midst of trouble, thou wilt revive me: thou shalt stretch forth thine hand against the wrath of mine enemies, and thy right hand shall save me.
\p
\v 8 The \nd LORD\nd* will perfect \add that which\add* concerneth me: thy mercy, O \nd LORD\nd*, \add endureth\add* for ever: forsake not the works of thine own hands.
\c 139
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 O \nd LORD\nd*, thou hast searched me, and known \add me\add*.
\p
\v 2 Thou knowest my downsitting and mine uprising, thou understandest my thought afar off.
\p
\v 3 Thou compassest my path and my lying down, and art acquainted \add with\add* all my ways.\f + \fr 139:3 \fr*\fq compassest \fq*\ft - or, winnowest\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 For \add there is\add* not a word in my tongue, \add but\add*, lo, O \nd LORD\nd*, thou knowest it altogether.
\p
\v 5 Thou hast beset me behind and before, and laid thine hand upon me.
\p
\v 6 \add Such\add* knowledge \add is\add* too wonderful for me; it is high, I cannot \add attain\add* unto it.
\p
\v 7 Whither shall I go from thy spirit? or whither shall I flee from thy presence?
\p
\v 8 If I ascend up into heaven, thou \add art\add* there: if I make my bed in hell, behold, thou \add art there\add*.
\p
\v 9 \add If\add* I take the wings of the morning, \add and\add* dwell in the uttermost parts of the sea;
\p
\v 10 Even there shall thy hand lead me, and thy right hand shall hold me.
\p
\v 11 If I say, Surely the darkness shall cover me; even the night shall be light about me.
\p
\v 12 Yea, the darkness hideth not from thee; but the night shineth as the day: the darkness and the light \add are\add* both alike \add to thee\add*.\f + \fr 139:12 \fr*\fq hideth… \fq*\ft - Heb. darkeneth not\ft*\f*\f + \fr 139:12 \fr*\fq the darkness and… \fq*\ft - Heb. as is the darkness, so is the light\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 For thou hast possessed my reins: thou hast covered me in my mother’s womb.
\p
\v 14 I will praise thee; for I am fearfully \add and\add* wonderfully made: marvellous \add are\add* thy works; and \add that\add* my soul knoweth right well.\f + \fr 139:14 \fr*\fq right… \fq*\ft - Heb. greatly\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 My substance was not hid from thee, when I was made in secret, \add and\add* curiously wrought in the lowest parts of the earth.\f + \fr 139:15 \fr*\fq substance \fq*\ft - or, strength, or, body\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 Thine eyes did see my substance, yet being unperfect; and in thy book all \add my members\add* were written, \add which\add* in continuance were fashioned, when \add as yet there was\add* none of them.\f + \fr 139:16 \fr*\fq all… \fq*\ft - Heb. all of them\ft*\f*\f + \fr 139:16 \fr*\fq which… \fq*\ft - or, what days they should be fashioned\ft*\f*
\p
\v 17 How precious also are thy thoughts unto me, O God! how great is the sum of them!
\p
\v 18 \add If\add* I should count them, they are more in number than the sand: when I awake, I am still with thee.
\p
\v 19 Surely thou wilt slay the wicked, O God: depart from me therefore, ye bloody men.
\p
\v 20 For they speak against thee wickedly, \add and\add* thine enemies take \add thy name\add* in vain.
\p
\v 21 Do not I hate them, O \nd LORD\nd*, that hate thee? and am not I grieved with those that rise up against thee?
\p
\v 22 I hate them with perfect hatred: I count them mine enemies.
\p
\v 23 Search me, O God, and know my heart: try me, and know my thoughts:
\p
\v 24 And see if \add there be any\add* wicked way in me, and lead me in the way everlasting.\f + \fr 139:24 \fr*\fq wicked… \fq*\ft - Heb. way of pain, or, grief\ft*\f*
\c 140
\d To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 Deliver me, O \nd LORD\nd*, from the evil man: preserve me from the violent man;\f + \fr 140:1 \fr*\fq violent… \fq*\ft - Heb. man of violences\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Which imagine mischiefs in \add their\add* heart; continually are they gathered together \add for\add* war.
\p
\v 3 They have sharpened their tongues like a serpent; adders’ poison \add is\add* under their lips. Selah.
\p
\v 4 Keep me, O \nd LORD\nd*, from the hands of the wicked; preserve me from the violent man; who have purposed to overthrow my goings.
\p
\v 5 The proud have hid a snare for me, and cords; they have spread a net by the wayside; they have set gins for me. Selah.
\p
\v 6 I said unto the \nd LORD\nd*, Thou \add art\add* my God: hear the voice of my supplications, O \nd LORD\nd*.
\p
\v 7 O \nd GOD\nd* the Lord, the strength of my salvation, thou hast covered my head in the day of battle.
\p
\v 8 Grant not, O \nd LORD\nd*, the desires of the wicked: further not his wicked device; \add lest\add* they exalt themselves. Selah.\f + \fr 140:8 \fr*\fq lest… \fq*\ft - or, let them not be exalted\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 \add As for\add* the head of those that compass me about, let the mischief of their own lips cover them.
\p
\v 10 Let burning coals fall upon them: let them be cast into the fire; into deep pits, that they rise not up again.
\p
\v 11 Let not an evil speaker be established in the earth: evil shall hunt the violent man to overthrow \add him\add*.\f + \fr 140:11 \fr*\fq an… \fq*\ft - or, an evil speaker (Heb. a man of tongue), a wicked man of violence, be established in the earth: let him be hunted to his overthrow\ft*\f*
\p
\v 12 I know that the \nd LORD\nd* will maintain the cause of the afflicted, \add and\add* the right of the poor.
\p
\v 13 Surely the righteous shall give thanks unto thy name: the upright shall dwell in thy presence.
\c 141
\d A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 \nd LORD\nd*, I cry unto thee: make haste unto me; give ear unto my voice, when I cry unto thee.
\p
\v 2 Let my prayer be set forth before thee \add as\add* incense; \add and\add* the lifting up of my hands \add as\add* the evening sacrifice.\f + \fr 141:2 \fr*\fq set… \fq*\ft - Heb. directed\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 Set a watch, O \nd LORD\nd*, before my mouth; keep the door of my lips.
\p
\v 4 Incline not my heart to \add any\add* evil thing, to practise wicked works with men that work iniquity: and let me not eat of their dainties.
\p
\v 5 Let the righteous smite me; \add it shall be\add* a kindness: and let him reprove me; \add it shall be\add* an excellent oil, \add which\add* shall not break my head: for yet my prayer also \add shall be\add* in their calamities.\f + \fr 141:5 \fr*\fq me; it shall be a… \fq*\ft - or, me kindly, and reprove me; let not their precious oil break, etc\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 When their judges are overthrown in stony places, they shall hear my words; for they are sweet.
\p
\v 7 Our bones are scattered at the grave’s mouth, as when one cutteth and cleaveth \add wood\add* upon the earth.
\p
\v 8 But mine eyes \add are\add* unto thee, O \nd GOD\nd* the Lord: in thee is my trust; leave not my soul destitute.\f + \fr 141:8 \fr*\fq leave… \fq*\ft - Heb. make not my soul bare\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 Keep me from the snares \add which\add* they have laid for me, and the gins of the workers of iniquity.
\p
\v 10 Let the wicked fall into their own nets, whilst that I withal escape.\f + \fr 141:10 \fr*\fq escape \fq*\ft - Heb. pass over\ft*\f*
\c 142
\d Maschil of David; A Prayer when he was in the cave.
\p
\v 1 I cried unto the \nd LORD\nd* with my voice; with my voice unto the \nd LORD\nd* did I make my supplication.\f + \fr 142:1 \fr*\fq Maschil… \fq*\ft - or, A Psalm of David, giving instruction\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 I poured out my complaint before him; I shewed before him my trouble.
\p
\v 3 When my spirit was overwhelmed within me, then thou knewest my path. In the way wherein I walked have they privily laid a snare for me.
\p
\v 4 I looked on \add my\add* right hand, and beheld, but \add there was\add* no man that would know me: refuge failed me; no man cared for my soul.\f + \fr 142:4 \fr*\fq I looked… \fq*\ft - or, Look on the right hand, and see\ft*\f*\f + \fr 142:4 \fr*\fq failed… \fq*\ft - Heb. perished from me\ft*\f*\f + \fr 142:4 \fr*\fq cared… \fq*\ft - Heb. sought after\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 I cried unto thee, O \nd LORD\nd*: I said, Thou \add art\add* my refuge \add and\add* my portion in the land of the living.
\p
\v 6 Attend unto my cry; for I am brought very low: deliver me from my persecutors; for they are stronger than I.
\p
\v 7 Bring my soul out of prison, that I may praise thy name: the righteous shall compass me about; for thou shalt deal bountifully with me.
\c 143
\d A Psalm of David.
\p
\v 1 Hear my prayer, O \nd LORD\nd*, give ear to my supplications: in thy faithfulness answer me, \add and\add* in thy righteousness.
\p
\v 2 And enter not into judgment with thy servant: for in thy sight shall no man living be justified.
\p
\v 3 For the enemy hath persecuted my soul; he hath smitten my life down to the ground; he hath made me to dwell in darkness, as those that have been long dead.
\p
\v 4 Therefore is my spirit overwhelmed within me; my heart within me is desolate.
\p
\v 5 I remember the days of old; I meditate on all thy works; I muse on the work of thy hands.
\p
\v 6 I stretch forth my hands unto thee: my soul \add thirsteth\add* after thee, as a thirsty land. Selah.
\p
\v 7 Hear me speedily, O \nd LORD\nd*: my spirit faileth: hide not thy face from me, lest I be like unto them that go down into the pit.\f + \fr 143:7 \fr*\fq lest… \fq*\ft - or, for I am become like, etc\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 Cause me to hear thy lovingkindness in the morning; for in thee do I trust: cause me to know the way wherein I should walk; for I lift up my soul unto thee.
\p
\v 9 Deliver me, O \nd LORD\nd*, from mine enemies: I flee unto thee to hide me.\f + \fr 143:9 \fr*\fq flee… \fq*\ft - Heb. hide me with thee\ft*\f*
\p
\v 10 Teach me to do thy will; for thou \add art\add* my God: thy spirit \add is\add* good; lead me into the land of uprightness.
\p
\v 11 Quicken me, O \nd LORD\nd*, for thy name’s sake: for thy righteousness’ sake bring my soul out of trouble.
\p
\v 12 And of thy mercy cut off mine enemies, and destroy all them that afflict my soul: for I \add am\add* thy servant.
\c 144
\d \add A Psalm\add* of David.
\p
\v 1 Blessed \add be\add* the \nd LORD\nd* my strength, which teacheth my hands to war, \add and\add* my fingers to fight:\f + \fr 144:1 \fr*\fq strength \fq*\ft - Heb. rock\ft*\f*\f + \fr 144:1 \fr*\fq to war… \fq*\ft - Heb. to the war, etc\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 My goodness, and my fortress; my high tower, and my deliverer; my shield, and \add he\add* in whom I trust; who subdueth my people under me.\f + \fr 144:2 \fr*\fq My goodness \fq*\ft - or, My mercy\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 \nd LORD\nd*, what \add is\add* man, that thou takest knowledge of him! \add or\add* the son of man, that thou makest account of him!
\p
\v 4 Man is like to vanity: his days \add are\add* as a shadow that passeth away.
\p
\v 5 Bow thy heavens, O \nd LORD\nd*, and come down: touch the mountains, and they shall smoke.
\p
\v 6 Cast forth lightning, and scatter them: shoot out thine arrows, and destroy them.
\p
\v 7 Send thine hand from above; rid me, and deliver me out of great waters, from the hand of strange children;\f + \fr 144:7 \fr*\fq hand from \fq*\ft - Heb. hands from\ft*\f*
\p
\v 8 Whose mouth speaketh vanity, and their right hand \add is\add* a right hand of falsehood.
\p
\v 9 I will sing a new song unto thee, O God: upon a psaltery \add and\add* an instrument of ten strings will I sing praises unto thee.
\p
\v 10 \add It is he\add* that giveth salvation unto kings: who delivereth David his servant from the hurtful sword.\f + \fr 144:10 \fr*\fq salvation \fq*\ft - or, victory\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 Rid me, and deliver me from the hand of strange children, whose mouth speaketh vanity, and their right hand \add is\add* a right hand of falsehood:
\p
\v 12 That our sons \add may be\add* as plants grown up in their youth; \add that\add* our daughters \add may be\add* as corner stones, polished \add after\add* the similitude of a palace:\f + \fr 144:12 \fr*\fq polished \fq*\ft - Heb. cut\ft*\f*
\p
\v 13 \add That\add* our garners \add may be\add* full, affording all manner of store: \add that\add* our sheep may bring forth thousands and ten thousands in our streets:\f + \fr 144:13 \fr*\fq all… \fq*\ft - Heb. from kind to kind\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 \add That\add* our oxen \add may be\add* strong to labour; \add that there be\add* no breaking in, nor going out; that \add there be\add* no complaining in our streets.\f + \fr 144:14 \fr*\fq strong… \fq*\ft - Heb. able to bear burdens, or, loaden with flesh\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 Happy \add is that\add* people, that is in such a case: \add yea\add*, happy \add is that\add* people, whose God \add is\add* the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 145
\d David’s \add Psalm\add* of praise.
\p
\v 1 I will extol thee, my God, O king; and I will bless thy name for ever and ever.
\p
\v 2 Every day will I bless thee; and I will praise thy name for ever and ever.
\p
\v 3 Great \add is\add* the \nd LORD\nd*, and greatly to be praised; and his greatness \add is\add* unsearchable.\f + \fr 145:3 \fr*\fq and his… \fq*\ft - Heb. and of his greatness there is no search\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 One generation shall praise thy works to another, and shall declare thy mighty acts.
\p
\v 5 I will speak of the glorious honour of thy majesty, and of thy wondrous works.\f + \fr 145:5 \fr*\fq works \fq*\ft - Heb. things, or, words\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 And \add men\add* shall speak of the might of thy terrible acts: and I will declare thy greatness.\f + \fr 145:6 \fr*\fq declare \fq*\ft - Heb. declare it\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 They shall abundantly utter the memory of thy great goodness, and shall sing of thy righteousness.
\p
\v 8 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* gracious, and full of compassion; slow to anger, and of great mercy.\f + \fr 145:8 \fr*\fq of great… \fq*\ft - Heb. great in mercy\ft*\f*
\p
\v 9 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* good to all: and his tender mercies \add are\add* over all his works.
\p
\v 10 All thy works shall praise thee, O \nd LORD\nd*; and thy saints shall bless thee.
\p
\v 11 They shall speak of the glory of thy kingdom, and talk of thy power;
\p
\v 12 To make known to the sons of men his mighty acts, and the glorious majesty of his kingdom.
\p
\v 13 Thy kingdom \add is\add* an everlasting kingdom, and thy dominion \add endureth\add* throughout all generations.\f + \fr 145:13 \fr*\fq an… \fq*\ft - Heb. a kingdom of all ages\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 The \nd LORD\nd* upholdeth all that fall, and raiseth up all \add those that be\add* bowed down.
\p
\v 15 The eyes of all wait upon thee; and thou givest them their meat in due season.\f + \fr 145:15 \fr*\fq wait… \fq*\ft - or, look unto\ft*\f*
\p
\v 16 Thou openest thine hand, and satisfiest the desire of every living thing.
\p
\v 17 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* righteous in all his ways, and holy in all his works.\f + \fr 145:17 \fr*\fq holy \fq*\ft - or, merciful, or, bountiful\ft*\f*
\p
\v 18 The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* nigh unto all them that call upon him, to all that call upon him in truth.
\p
\v 19 He will fulfil the desire of them that fear him: he also will hear their cry, and will save them.
\p
\v 20 The \nd LORD\nd* preserveth all them that love him: but all the wicked will he destroy.
\p
\v 21 My mouth shall speak the praise of the \nd LORD\nd*: and let all flesh bless his holy name for ever and ever.
\c 146
\p
\v 1 Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*. Praise the \nd LORD\nd*, O my soul.\f + \fr 146:1 \fr*\fq Praise ye… \fq*\ft - Heb. Hallelujah\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 While I live will I praise the \nd LORD\nd*: I will sing praises unto my God while I have any being.
\p
\v 3 Put not your trust in princes, \add nor\add* in the son of man, in whom \add there is\add* no help.\f + \fr 146:3 \fr*\fq help \fq*\ft - or, salvation\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 His breath goeth forth, he returneth to his earth; in that very day his thoughts perish.
\p
\v 5 Happy \add is he\add* that \add hath\add* the God of Jacob for his help, whose hope \add is\add* in the \nd LORD\nd* his God:
\p
\v 6 Which made heaven, and earth, the sea, and all that therein \add is:\add* which keepeth truth for ever:
\p
\v 7 Which executeth judgment for the oppressed: which giveth food to the hungry. The \nd LORD\nd* looseth the prisoners:
\p
\v 8 The \nd LORD\nd* openeth \add the eyes of\add* the blind: the \nd LORD\nd* raiseth them that are bowed down: the \nd LORD\nd* loveth the righteous:
\p
\v 9 The \nd LORD\nd* preserveth the strangers; he relieveth the fatherless and widow: but the way of the wicked he turneth upside down.
\p
\v 10 The \nd LORD\nd* shall reign for ever, \add even\add* thy God, O Zion, unto all generations. Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 147
\p
\v 1 Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*: for \add it is\add* good to sing praises unto our God; for \add it is\add* pleasant; \add and\add* praise is comely.
\p
\v 2 The \nd LORD\nd* doth build up Jerusalem: he gathereth together the outcasts of Israel.
\p
\v 3 He healeth the broken in heart, and bindeth up their wounds.\f + \fr 147:3 \fr*\fq wounds \fq*\ft - Heb. griefs\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 He telleth the number of the stars; he calleth them all by \add their\add* names.
\p
\v 5 Great \add is\add* our Lord, and of great power: his understanding \add is\add* infinite.\f + \fr 147:5 \fr*\fq his… \fq*\ft - Heb. of his understanding there is no number\ft*\f*
\p
\v 6 The \nd LORD\nd* lifteth up the meek: he casteth the wicked down to the ground.
\p
\v 7 Sing unto the \nd LORD\nd* with thanksgiving; sing praise upon the harp unto our God:
\p
\v 8 Who covereth the heaven with clouds, who prepareth rain for the earth, who maketh grass to grow upon the mountains.
\p
\v 9 He giveth to the beast his food, \add and\add* to the young ravens which cry.
\p
\v 10 He delighteth not in the strength of the horse: he taketh not pleasure in the legs of a man.
\p
\v 11 The \nd LORD\nd* taketh pleasure in them that fear him, in those that hope in his mercy.
\p
\v 12 Praise the \nd LORD\nd*, O Jerusalem; praise thy God, O Zion.
\p
\v 13 For he hath strengthened the bars of thy gates; he hath blessed thy children within thee.
\p
\v 14 He maketh peace \add in\add* thy borders, \add and\add* filleth thee with the finest of the wheat.\f + \fr 147:14 \fr*\fq He… \fq*\ft - Heb. Who maketh thy border peace\ft*\f*\f + \fr 147:14 \fr*\fq finest… \fq*\ft - Heb. fat of wheat\ft*\f*
\p
\v 15 He sendeth forth his commandment \add upon\add* earth: his word runneth very swiftly.
\p
\v 16 He giveth snow like wool: he scattereth the hoarfrost like ashes.
\p
\v 17 He casteth forth his ice like morsels: who can stand before his cold?
\p
\v 18 He sendeth out his word, and melteth them: he causeth his wind to blow, \add and\add* the waters flow.
\p
\v 19 He sheweth his word unto Jacob, his statutes and his judgments unto Israel.\f + \fr 147:19 \fr*\fq his word \fq*\ft - Heb. his words\ft*\f*
\p
\v 20 He hath not dealt so with any nation: and \add as for his\add* judgments, they have not known them. Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 148
\p
\v 1 Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*. Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd* from the heavens: praise him in the heights.\f + \fr 148:1 \fr*\ft Praise ye the\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Praise ye him, all his angels: praise ye him, all his hosts.
\p
\v 3 Praise ye him, sun and moon: praise him, all ye stars of light.
\p
\v 4 Praise him, ye heavens of heavens, and ye waters that \add be\add* above the heavens.
\p
\v 5 Let them praise the name of the \nd LORD\nd*: for he commanded, and they were created.
\p
\v 6 He hath also stablished them for ever and ever: he hath made a decree which shall not pass.
\p
\v 7 Praise the \nd LORD\nd* from the earth, ye dragons, and all deeps:
\p
\v 8 Fire, and hail; snow, and vapour; stormy wind fulfilling his word:
\p
\v 9 Mountains, and all hills; fruitful trees, and all cedars:
\p
\v 10 Beasts, and all cattle; creeping things, and flying fowl:\f + \fr 148:10 \fr*\fq flying… \fq*\ft - Heb. birds of wing\ft*\f*
\p
\v 11 Kings of the earth, and all people; princes, and all judges of the earth:
\p
\v 12 Both young men, and maidens; old men, and children:
\p
\v 13 Let them praise the name of the \nd LORD\nd*: for his name alone is excellent; his glory \add is\add* above the earth and heaven.\f + \fr 148:13 \fr*\fq excellent \fq*\ft - Heb. exalted\ft*\f*
\p
\v 14 He also exalteth the horn of his people, the praise of all his saints; \add even\add* of the children of Israel, a people near unto him. Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 149
\p
\v 1 Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*. Sing unto the \nd LORD\nd* a new song, \add and\add* his praise in the congregation of saints.\f + \fr 149:1 \fr*\fq Praise… \fq*\ft - Heb. Hallelujah\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Let Israel rejoice in him that made him: let the children of Zion be joyful in their King.\f + \fr 149:2 \fr*\fq in him… \fq*\ft - Heb. in his Makers\ft*\f*
\p
\v 3 Let them praise his name in the dance: let them sing praises unto him with the timbrel and harp.\f + \fr 149:3 \fr*\fq in… \fq*\ft - or, with the pipe\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 For the \nd LORD\nd* taketh pleasure in his people: he will beautify the meek with salvation.
\p
\v 5 Let the saints be joyful in glory: let them sing aloud upon their beds.
\p
\v 6 \add Let\add* the high \add praises\add* of God \add be\add* in their mouth, and a twoedged sword in their hand;\f + \fr 149:6 \fr*\fq mouth \fq*\ft - Heb. throat\ft*\f*
\p
\v 7 To execute vengeance upon the heathen, \add and\add* punishments upon the people;
\p
\v 8 To bind their kings with chains, and their nobles with fetters of iron;
\p
\v 9 To execute upon them the judgment written: this honour have all his saints. Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*.
\c 150
\p
\v 1 Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*. Praise God in his sanctuary: praise him in the firmament of his power.\f + \fr 150:1 \fr*\fq Praise ye… \fq*\ft - Heb. Hallelujah\ft*\f*
\p
\v 2 Praise him for his mighty acts: praise him according to his excellent greatness.
\p
\v 3 Praise him with the sound of the trumpet: praise him with the psaltery and harp.\f + \fr 150:3 \fr*\fq trumpet \fq*\ft - or, cornet\ft*\f*
\p
\v 4 Praise him with the timbrel and dance: praise him with stringed instruments and organs.\f + \fr 150:4 \fr*\fq dance \fq*\ft - or, pipe\ft*\f*
\p
\v 5 Praise him upon the loud cymbals: praise him upon the high sounding cymbals.
\p
\v 6 Let every thing that hath breath praise the \nd LORD\nd*. Praise ye the \nd LORD\nd*.
